"longname":"CsvController#metadata","name":"metadata","kind":"function","scope":"instance","description":"Structural CSV metadata: rows, columns, delimiter, per-column type census.","memberof":"CsvController","params":[{"description":"Flat csv-parse options plus `maxRows` for the type census.","name":"query","type":{"names":["{ [x: string]: any; maxRows: number; trim?: boolean; bom?: boolean; escape?: string; quote?: string | false; cast_date?: boolean; comment?: string; comment_no_infix?: boolean; delimiter_auto?: boolean; encoding?: \"ascii\" | \"utf8\" | \"utf16le\" | \"ucs2\" | \"base64\" | \"latin1\" | \"binary\" | \"hex\"; max_record_size?: number; relax_column_count?: boolean; relax_column_count_less?: boolean; relax_column_count_more?: boolean; relax_quotes?: boolean; skip_empty_lines?: boolean; }"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The metadata document (201).","type":{"names":["Promise<{ bom: boolean; columns: number; delimiter: string | string[] | Buffer<ArrayBufferLike> | Buffer<ArrayBufferLike>[]; maxRows: number; perColumn: { index: number; types: Record<\"string\" | \"number\" | \"boolean\" | \"date\" | \"empty\", number>; }[]; recordDelimiter: string | string[] | Buffer<ArrayBufferLike> | Buffer<ArrayBufferLike>[]; rows: number; truncatedTypes: boolean; }>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":100},"order":3,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/csv/csv.controller.js:35","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/csv/csv.controller.ts:77"},"level":0}],"fp":"91064d8daa446f37650e0292f904c5425b52faeecd5e9c959d477ed808ce9f4f","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730449094,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/resources/csv/csv.controller.ts":{"fp":"a248a8203ccae3e5b88d331a1fe89090981974918af18b8055ca25e98ed69556","issues":[],"kind":"md","markdown":"<a name=\"CsvController\"></a>\n\n## CsvController\nCSV routes. Unlike the media modules this controller binds interceptors\nper route: `/csv/build` consumes a JSON body (the media parser never sees it),\nwhile `/csv/extract` and `/csv/metadata` take the binary upload and are\nClamAV-scanned like any other binary payload.\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/csv/csv.controller.ts:35  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/csv/csv.controller.js:20\n\n* [CsvController](#CsvController)\n    * [.build(response, body)](#CsvController+build) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code>\n    * [.extract(query)](#CsvController+extract) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;{ records: unknown[]; }&gt;</code>\n    * [.metadata(query)](#CsvController+metadata) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;{ bom: boolean; columns: number; delimiter: string \\| string[] \\| Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt; \\| Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;[]; maxRows: number; perColumn: { index: number; types: Record&lt;&quot;string&quot; \\| &quot;number&quot; \\| &quot;boolean&quot; \\| &quot;date&quot; \\| &quot;empty&quot;, number&gt;; }[]; recordDelimiter: string \\| string[] \\| Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt; \\| Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;[]; rows: number; truncatedTypes: boolean; }&gt;</code>\n\n<a name=\"CsvController+build\"></a>\n\n### csvController.build(response, body) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code>\nSerializes JSON rows to CSV. POST-only: there is no meaningful GET shape.\n\n**Kind**: instance method of [<code>CsvController</code>](#CsvController)  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code> - CSV bytes.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| response | <code>FastifyReply&lt;import(&quot;fastify&quot;).RouteGenericInterface, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).RawServerDefault, import(&quot;http&quot;).IncomingMessage, import(&quot;http&quot;).ServerResponse&lt;import(&quot;http&quot;).IncomingMessage&gt;, unknown, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).FastifySchema, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).FastifyTypeProviderDefault, unknown&gt;</code> | Raw reply, streamed with `text/csv`. |\n| body | <code>{ records: (Record&lt;string, unknown&gt; \\| unknown[])[]; options?: { [x: string]: any; bom?: boolean; columns?: (string \\| { key: string; header?: string; })[]; eof?: boolean; escape?: string; escape\\_formulas?: boolean; header?: boolean; header\\_as\\_comment?: boolean; quote?: string \\| false; quote\\_record\\_delimiter?: boolean; quoted?: boolean; quoted\\_empty?: boolean; quoted\\_string?: boolean; }; }</code> | Rows and csv-stringify options. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/csv/csv.controller.ts:48  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/csv/csv.controller.js:27\n<a name=\"CsvController+extract\"></a>\n\n### csvController.extract(query) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;{ records: unknown[]; }&gt;</code>\nParses an uploaded CSV into typed JSON records.\n\n**Kind**: instance method of [<code>CsvController</code>](#CsvController)  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;{ records: unknown[]; }&gt;</code> - The parsed records (201).  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| query | <code>{ [x: string]: any; bom?: boolean; cast?: boolean; cast\\_date?: boolean; columns?: boolean \\| string[] \\| any[]; comment?: string; comment\\_no\\_infix?: boolean; delimiter\\_auto?: boolean; encoding?: &quot;ascii&quot; \\| &quot;utf8&quot; \\| &quot;utf16le&quot; \\| &quot;ucs2&quot; \\| &quot;base64&quot; \\| &quot;latin1&quot; \\| &quot;binary&quot; \\| &quot;hex&quot;; escape?: string; from?: number; from\\_line?: number; group\\_columns\\_by\\_name?: boolean; ignore\\_last\\_delimiters?: boolean; ltrim?: boolean; max\\_record\\_size?: number; quote?: string \\| false; relax\\_column\\_count?: boolean; relax\\_column\\_count\\_less?: boolean; relax\\_column\\_count\\_more?: boolean; relax\\_quotes?: boolean; rtrim?: boolean; skip\\_empty\\_lines?: boolean; skip\\_records\\_with\\_empty\\_values?: boolean; skip\\_records\\_with\\_error?: boolean; to?: number; to\\_line?: number; trim?: boolean; }</code> | Flat csv-parse options. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/csv/csv.controller.ts:64  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/csv/csv.controller.js:32\n<a name=\"CsvController+metadata\"></a>\n\n### csvController.metadata(query) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;{ bom: boolean; columns: number; delimiter: string \\| string[] \\| Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt; \\| Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;[]; maxRows: number; perColumn: { index: number; types: Record&lt;&quot;string&quot; \\| &quot;number&quot; \\| &quot;boolean&quot; \\| &quot;date&quot; \\| &quot;empty&quot;, number&gt;; }[]; recordDelimiter: string \\| string[] \\| Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt; \\| Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;[]; rows: number; truncatedTypes: boolean; }&gt;</code>\nStructural CSV metadata: rows, columns, delimiter, per-column type census.\n\n**Kind**: instance method of [<code>CsvController</code>](#CsvController)  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;{ bom: boolean; columns: number; delimiter: string \\| string[] \\| Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt; \\| Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;[]; maxRows: number; perColumn: { index: number; types: Record&lt;&quot;string&quot; \\| &quot;number&quot; \\| &quot;boolean&quot; \\| &quot;date&quot; \\| &quot;empty&quot;, number&gt;; }[]; recordDelimiter: string \\| string[] \\| Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt; \\| Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;[]; rows: number; truncatedTypes: boolean; }&gt;</code> - The metadata document (201).  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| query | <code>{ [x: string]: any; maxRows: number; trim?: boolean; bom?: boolean; escape?: string; quote?: string \\| false; cast\\_date?: boolean; comment?: string; comment\\_no\\_infix?: boolean; delimiter\\_auto?: boolean; encoding?: &quot;ascii&quot; \\| &quot;utf8&quot; \\| &quot;utf16le&quot; \\| &quot;ucs2&quot; \\| &quot;base64&quot; \\| &quot;latin1&quot; \\| &quot;binary&quot; \\| &quot;hex&quot;; max\\_record\\_size?: number; relax\\_column\\_count?: boolean; relax\\_column\\_count\\_less?: boolean; relax\\_column\\_count\\_more?: boolean; relax\\_quotes?: boolean; skip\\_empty\\_lines?: boolean; }</code> | Flat csv-parse options plus `maxRows` for the type census. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/csv/csv.controller.ts:77  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/csv/csv.controller.js:35\n","symbols":4,"lastUsed":1795730449160},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/csv/csv.module.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"CsvModule","longname":"CsvModule","name":"CsvModule","kind":"member","scope":"global","description":"CSV feature module: build, extract and metadata routes.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":41},"order":0,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/csv/csv.module.js:10","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/csv/csv.module.ts:13"},"level":0}],"fp":"16f94002ae71211536fff58ba8d970c0623115408e093dd3f123cdec5cb21199","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730449094,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/resources/csv/csv.module.ts":{"fp":"16164dd2193aaa8a5a0b7efa752ded95cd24f92e0955aef82864701d014c01ca","issues":[],"kind":"md","markdown":"<a name=\"CsvModule\"></a>\n\n## CsvModule\nCSV feature module: build, extract and metadata routes.\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/csv/csv.module.ts:13  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/csv/csv.module.js:10\n","symbols":1,"lastUsed":1795730449189},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/csv/csv.service.spec.ts":{"doclets":[],"fp":"a773142d0398236c0a717c222a2af79f630785721674b4f3682cc0f49732aa2d","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730449115,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/resources/csv/csv.service.spec.ts":{"fp":"d0d45bc41fe93fb7daa0dd41e588e5d69eef281763ddf21aef950db47dfabf86","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","skipped":"no-jsdoc","symbols":0,"lastUsed":1795730449115},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/csv/csv.service.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"RecordCapError","longname":"RecordCapError","name":"RecordCapError","kind":"class","scope":"global","description":"Error thrown when a record cap is exceeded; maps to 413 at the boundary.","meta":{"lineno":50},"order":1,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/csv/csv.service.js:20","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/csv/csv.service.ts:29"},"level":0},{"id":"CsvService","longname":"CsvService","name":"CsvService","kind":"member","scope":"global","description":"CSV feature service: builds CSV from rows and parses/metadata-inspects uploads.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":91},"order":4,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/csv/csv.service.js:44","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/csv/csv.service.ts:74"},"level":0},{"id":"MAX_RECORDS","longname":"MAX_RECORDS","name":"MAX_RECORDS","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Hard cap on parsed records; beyond it the response would exhaust memory.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":46},"order":0,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/csv/csv.service.js:19","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/csv/csv.service.ts:24"},"level":0},{"id":"toBadRequest","longname":"toBadRequest","name":"toBadRequest","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Maps a csv-parse/csv-stringify failure to a 400 with the library's error code.","params":[{"description":"The library error (carries `code` and `message`).","name":"error","type":{"names":["unknown"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"A 400 exception carrying the library's code and message.","type":{"names":["BadRequestException"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":57},"order":2,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/csv/csv.service.js:22","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/csv/csv.service.ts:36"},"level":0},{"id":"readBody","longname":"readBody","name":"readBody","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Opens (idempotently) and reads the uploaded CSV body, bounded by the scanner cap.\nThe scanner opens the source only when ClamAV is enabled, so the service must too.\nOnly `text/csv` and `application/octet-stream` bodies are accepted.","params":[{"description":"The normalized request context (source stream accessors).","name":"cls","type":{"names":["NormalizedClsService"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The body bytes, capped.","type":{"names":["Promise<Buffer<ArrayBufferLike>>"]}}],"exceptions":[{"type":{"names":["UnsupportedMediaTypeException"]},"description":"For any other content type."}],"meta":{"lineno":75},"async":true,"order":3,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/csv/csv.service.js:32","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/csv/csv.service.ts:56"},"level":0},{"id":"kindOf","longname":"kindOf","name":"kindOf","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Classifies a cast csv-parse value. `empty` covers null/undefined and empty strings;\nexact `true`/`false` strings count as boolean (csv-parse does not cast them).","params":[{"description":"One cast field value.","name":"value","type":{"names":["unknown"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The census key for the value.","type":{"names":["\"string\" | \"number\" | \"boolean\" | \"date\" | \"empty\""]}}],"meta":{"lineno":211},"order":8,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/csv/csv.service.js:122","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/csv/csv.service.ts:180"},"level":0},{"id":"CsvService#buildCsv","longname":"CsvService#buildCsv","name":"buildCsv","kind":"function","scope":"instance","description":"Builds the CSV response stream for `POST /csv/build`.\n`escape_formulas` defaults to true: cells starting with `= + - @ TAB CR` are prefixed with `'`.","memberof":"CsvService","params":[{"description":"Validated build payload (rows plus csv-stringify options).","name":"body","type":{"names":["{ records: (Record<string, unknown> | unknown[])[]; options?: { [x: string]: any; bom?: boolean; columns?: (string | { key: string; header?: string; })[]; eof?: boolean; escape?: string; escape_formulas?: boolean; header?: boolean; header_as_comment?: boolean; quote?: string | false; quote_record_delimiter?: boolean; quoted?: boolean; quoted_empty?: boolean; quoted_string?: boolean; }; }"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The readable CSV byte stream (201 by POST convention).","type":{"names":["Readable"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":115},"order":5,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/csv/csv.service.js:49","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/csv/csv.service.ts:83"},"level":0},{"id":"CsvService#extract","longname":"CsvService#extract","name":"extract","kind":"function","scope":"instance","description":"Parses the uploaded CSV into typed JSON records.\nFunction-valued csv-parse options are not exposed over HTTP. At most\n{@link MAX_RECORDS} records are materialized; larger files answer 413.\nThe first record is treated as data (no header semantics here).","memberof":"CsvService","params":[{"description":"Validated, flat csv-parse options (file travels in the body).","name":"query","type":{"names":["{ [x: string]: any; bom?: boolean; cast?: boolean; cast_date?: boolean; columns?: boolean | string[] | any[]; comment?: string; comment_no_infix?: boolean; delimiter_auto?: boolean; encoding?: \"ascii\" | \"utf8\" | \"utf16le\" | \"ucs2\" | \"base64\" | \"latin1\" | \"binary\" | \"hex\"; escape?: string; from?: number; from_line?: number; group_columns_by_name?: boolean; ignore_last_delimiters?: boolean; ltrim?: boolean; max_record_size?: number; quote?: string | false; relax_column_count?: boolean; relax_column_count_less?: boolean; relax_column_count_more?: boolean; relax_quotes?: boolean; rtrim?: boolean; skip_empty_lines?: boolean; skip_records_with_empty_values?: boolean; skip_records_with_error?: boolean; to?: number; to_line?: number; trim?: boolean; }"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The parsed records.","type":{"names":["Promise<{ records: unknown[]; }>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":127},"async":true,"order":6,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/csv/csv.service.js:52","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/csv/csv.service.ts:96"},"level":0},{"id":"CsvService#metadata","longname":"CsvService#metadata","name":"metadata","kind":"function","scope":"instance","description":"Computes structural metadata for an uploaded CSV. One streaming pass.\n`maxRows` limits the per-column type census; row/column counting always scans everything.\nThe first record counts as a data row (header or not). `delimiter_auto`\ndefaults on unless `delimiter` is given; the reported delimiter is the\nsupplied value, or `auto` when none was (csv-parse does not hand the\nwinning value back).","memberof":"CsvService","params":[{"description":"Validated, flat csv-parse options plus `maxRows`.","name":"query","type":{"names":["{ [x: string]: any; maxRows: number; trim?: boolean; bom?: boolean; escape?: string; quote?: string | false; cast_date?: boolean; comment?: string; comment_no_infix?: boolean; delimiter_auto?: boolean; encoding?: \"ascii\" | \"utf8\" | \"utf16le\" | \"ucs2\" | \"base64\" | \"latin1\" | \"binary\" | \"hex\"; max_record_size?: number; relax_column_count?: boolean; relax_column_count_less?: boolean; relax_column_count_more?: boolean; relax_quotes?: boolean; skip_empty_lines?: boolean; }"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"Rows, columns, delimiter handed over (`auto` unless given), and per-column type counts.","type":{"names":["Promise<{ bom: boolean; columns: number; delimiter: string | string[] | Buffer<ArrayBufferLike> | Buffer<ArrayBufferLike>[]; maxRows: number; perColumn: { index: number; types: Record<\"string\" | \"number\" | \"boolean\" | \"date\" | \"empty\", number>; }[]; recordDelimiter: string | string[] | Buffer<ArrayBufferLike> | Buffer<ArrayBufferLike>[]; rows: number; truncatedTypes: boolean; }>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":155},"async":true,"order":7,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/csv/csv.service.js:70","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/csv/csv.service.ts:124"},"level":0}],"fp":"7e3fb8a353c5f7f7045763e7bcbb1024fde2bc34c5ed5e2a8be9e1d9126543c4","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730449132,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/resources/csv/csv.service.ts":{"fp":"c3d42d79d84d87eed56f02542c573b1a0ff968847c56bd63b5bc1b52bcefb0ba","issues":[],"kind":"md","markdown":"## Classes\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#RecordCapError\">RecordCapError</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Error thrown when a record cap is exceeded; maps to 413 at the boundary.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n## Members\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#CsvService\">CsvService</a></dt>\n<dd><p>CSV feature service: builds CSV from rows and parses/metadata-inspects uploads.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n## Constants\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#MAX_RECORDS\">MAX_RECORDS</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Hard cap on parsed records; beyond it the response would exhaust memory.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#toBadRequest\">toBadRequest</a> ⇒ <code>BadRequestException</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Maps a csv-parse/csv-stringify failure to a 400 with the library&#39;s error code.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n## Functions\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#readBody\">readBody(cls)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Opens (idempotently) and reads the uploaded CSV body, bounded by the scanner cap.\nThe scanner opens the source only when ClamAV is enabled, so the service must too.\nOnly <code>text/csv</code> and <code>application/octet-stream</code> bodies are accepted.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#kindOf\">kindOf(value)</a> ⇒ <code>&quot;string&quot; | &quot;number&quot; | &quot;boolean&quot; | &quot;date&quot; | &quot;empty&quot;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Classifies a cast csv-parse value. <code>empty</code> covers null/undefined and empty strings;\nexact <code>true</code>/<code>false</code> strings count as boolean (csv-parse does not cast them).</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"RecordCapError\"></a>\n\n## RecordCapError\nError thrown when a record cap is exceeded; maps to 413 at the boundary.\n\n**Kind**: global class  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/csv/csv.service.ts:29  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/csv/csv.service.js:20\n<a name=\"CsvService\"></a>\n\n## CsvService\nCSV feature service: builds CSV from rows and parses/metadata-inspects uploads.\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/csv/csv.service.ts:74  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/csv/csv.service.js:44\n\n* [CsvService](#CsvService)\n    * [.buildCsv(body)](#CsvService+buildCsv) ⇒ <code>Readable</code>\n    * [.extract(query)](#CsvService+extract) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;{ records: unknown[]; }&gt;</code>\n    * [.metadata(query)](#CsvService+metadata) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;{ bom: boolean; columns: number; delimiter: string \\| string[] \\| Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt; \\| Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;[]; maxRows: number; perColumn: { index: number; types: Record&lt;&quot;string&quot; \\| &quot;number&quot; \\| &quot;boolean&quot; \\| &quot;date&quot; \\| &quot;empty&quot;, number&gt;; }[]; recordDelimiter: string \\| string[] \\| Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt; \\| Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;[]; rows: number; truncatedTypes: boolean; }&gt;</code>\n\n<a name=\"CsvService+buildCsv\"></a>\n\n### csvService.buildCsv(body) ⇒ <code>Readable</code>\nBuilds the CSV response stream for `POST /csv/build`.\n`escape_formulas` defaults to true: cells starting with `= + - @ TAB CR` are prefixed with `'`.\n\n**Kind**: instance method of [<code>CsvService</code>](#CsvService)  \n**Returns**: <code>Readable</code> - The readable CSV byte stream (201 by POST convention).  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| body | <code>{ records: (Record&lt;string, unknown&gt; \\| unknown[])[]; options?: { [x: string]: any; bom?: boolean; columns?: (string \\| { key: string; header?: string; })[]; eof?: boolean; escape?: string; escape\\_formulas?: boolean; header?: boolean; header\\_as\\_comment?: boolean; quote?: string \\| false; quote\\_record\\_delimiter?: boolean; quoted?: boolean; quoted\\_empty?: boolean; quoted\\_string?: boolean; }; }</code> | Validated build payload (rows plus csv-stringify options). |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/csv/csv.service.ts:83  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/csv/csv.service.js:49\n<a name=\"CsvService+extract\"></a>\n\n### csvService.extract(query) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;{ records: unknown[]; }&gt;</code>\nParses the uploaded CSV into typed JSON records.\nFunction-valued csv-parse options are not exposed over HTTP. At most\n[MAX_RECORDS](#MAX_RECORDS) records are materialized; larger files answer 413.\nThe first record is treated as data (no header semantics here).\n\n**Kind**: instance method of [<code>CsvService</code>](#CsvService)  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;{ records: unknown[]; }&gt;</code> - The parsed records.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| query | <code>{ [x: string]: any; bom?: boolean; cast?: boolean; cast\\_date?: boolean; columns?: boolean \\| string[] \\| any[]; comment?: string; comment\\_no\\_infix?: boolean; delimiter\\_auto?: boolean; encoding?: &quot;ascii&quot; \\| &quot;utf8&quot; \\| &quot;utf16le&quot; \\| &quot;ucs2&quot; \\| &quot;base64&quot; \\| &quot;latin1&quot; \\| &quot;binary&quot; \\| &quot;hex&quot;; escape?: string; from?: number; from\\_line?: number; group\\_columns\\_by\\_name?: boolean; ignore\\_last\\_delimiters?: boolean; ltrim?: boolean; max\\_record\\_size?: number; quote?: string \\| false; relax\\_column\\_count?: boolean; relax\\_column\\_count\\_less?: boolean; relax\\_column\\_count\\_more?: boolean; relax\\_quotes?: boolean; rtrim?: boolean; skip\\_empty\\_lines?: boolean; skip\\_records\\_with\\_empty\\_values?: boolean; skip\\_records\\_with\\_error?: boolean; to?: number; to\\_line?: number; trim?: boolean; }</code> | Validated, flat csv-parse options (file travels in the body). |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/csv/csv.service.ts:96  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/csv/csv.service.js:52\n<a name=\"CsvService+metadata\"></a>\n\n### csvService.metadata(query) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;{ bom: boolean; columns: number; delimiter: string \\| string[] \\| Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt; \\| Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;[]; maxRows: number; perColumn: { index: number; types: Record&lt;&quot;string&quot; \\| &quot;number&quot; \\| &quot;boolean&quot; \\| &quot;date&quot; \\| &quot;empty&quot;, number&gt;; }[]; recordDelimiter: string \\| string[] \\| Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt; \\| Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;[]; rows: number; truncatedTypes: boolean; }&gt;</code>\nComputes structural metadata for an uploaded CSV. One streaming pass.\n`maxRows` limits the per-column type census; row/column counting always scans everything.\nThe first record counts as a data row (header or not). `delimiter_auto`\ndefaults on unless `delimiter` is given; the reported delimiter is the\nsupplied value, or `auto` when none was (csv-parse does not hand the\nwinning value back).\n\n**Kind**: instance method of [<code>CsvService</code>](#CsvService)  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;{ bom: boolean; columns: number; delimiter: string \\| string[] \\| Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt; \\| Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;[]; maxRows: number; perColumn: { index: number; types: Record&lt;&quot;string&quot; \\| &quot;number&quot; \\| &quot;boolean&quot; \\| &quot;date&quot; \\| &quot;empty&quot;, number&gt;; }[]; recordDelimiter: string \\| string[] \\| Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt; \\| Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;[]; rows: number; truncatedTypes: boolean; }&gt;</code> - Rows, columns, delimiter handed over (`auto` unless given), and per-column type counts.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| query | <code>{ [x: string]: any; maxRows: number; trim?: boolean; bom?: boolean; escape?: string; quote?: string \\| false; cast\\_date?: boolean; comment?: string; comment\\_no\\_infix?: boolean; delimiter\\_auto?: boolean; encoding?: &quot;ascii&quot; \\| &quot;utf8&quot; \\| &quot;utf16le&quot; \\| &quot;ucs2&quot; \\| &quot;base64&quot; \\| &quot;latin1&quot; \\| &quot;binary&quot; \\| &quot;hex&quot;; max\\_record\\_size?: number; relax\\_column\\_count?: boolean; relax\\_column\\_count\\_less?: boolean; relax\\_column\\_count\\_more?: boolean; relax\\_quotes?: boolean; skip\\_empty\\_lines?: boolean; }</code> | Validated, flat csv-parse options plus `maxRows`. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/csv/csv.service.ts:124  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/csv/csv.service.js:70\n<a name=\"MAX_RECORDS\"></a>\n\n## MAX\\_RECORDS\nHard cap on parsed records; beyond it the response would exhaust memory.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/csv/csv.service.ts:24  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/csv/csv.service.js:19\n<a name=\"toBadRequest\"></a>\n\n## toBadRequest ⇒ <code>BadRequestException</code>\nMaps a csv-parse/csv-stringify failure to a 400 with the library's error code.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \n**Returns**: <code>BadRequestException</code> - A 400 exception carrying the library's code and message.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| error | <code>unknown</code> | The library error (carries `code` and `message`). |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/csv/csv.service.ts:36  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/csv/csv.service.js:22\n<a name=\"readBody\"></a>\n\n## readBody(cls) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;&gt;</code>\nOpens (idempotently) and reads the uploaded CSV body, bounded by the scanner cap.\nThe scanner opens the source only when ClamAV is enabled, so the service must too.\nOnly `text/csv` and `application/octet-stream` bodies are accepted.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;&gt;</code> - The body bytes, capped.  \n**Throws**:\n\n- <code>UnsupportedMediaTypeException</code> For any other content type.\n\n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| cls | <code>NormalizedClsService</code> | The normalized request context (source stream accessors). |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/csv/csv.service.ts:56  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/csv/csv.service.js:32\n<a name=\"kindOf\"></a>\n\n## kindOf(value) ⇒ <code>&quot;string&quot; \\| &quot;number&quot; \\| &quot;boolean&quot; \\| &quot;date&quot; \\| &quot;empty&quot;</code>\nClassifies a cast csv-parse value. `empty` covers null/undefined and empty strings;\nexact `true`/`false` strings count as boolean (csv-parse does not cast them).\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>&quot;string&quot; \\| &quot;number&quot; \\| &quot;boolean&quot; \\| &quot;date&quot; \\| &quot;empty&quot;</code> - The census key for the value.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| value | <code>unknown</code> | One cast field value. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/csv/csv.service.ts:180  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/csv/csv.service.js:122\n","symbols":9,"lastUsed":1795730449230},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/csv/schema.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"options","longname":"options","name":"options","kind":"member","scope":"global","description":"csv-stringify options (names kept as in the library). `escape_formulas` defaults to true.","meta":{"lineno":21},"order":1,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/csv/schema.js:14","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/csv/schema.ts:24"},"level":0},{"id":"records","longname":"records","name":"records","kind":"member","scope":"global","description":"Rows to serialize; objects map keys to cells, arrays emit positional cells.","meta":{"lineno":43},"order":2,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/csv/schema.js:33","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/csv/schema.ts:46"},"level":0},{"id":"CsvBuildSchema","longname":"CsvBuildSchema","name":"CsvBuildSchema","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"JSON body for `POST /csv/build`: rows in, CSV bytes out.\nElements may be row objects or arrays of cell values.","meta":{"lineno":16},"order":0,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/csv/schema.js:12","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/csv/schema.ts:19"},"level":0},{"id":"csvParseOptions","longname":"csvParseOptions","name":"csvParseOptions","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"csv-parse options shared by `/csv/extract` and `/csv/metadata` (function-valued options excluded).","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":49},"order":3,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/csv/schema.js:36","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/csv/schema.ts:57"},"level":0},{"id":"CsvExtractSchema","longname":"CsvExtractSchema","name":"CsvExtractSchema","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Flat query parameters for `POST /csv/extract`.\nThe raw CSV travels in the request body; everything here is csv-parse options.","meta":{"lineno":93},"order":4,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/csv/schema.js:76","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/csv/schema.ts:102"},"level":0},{"id":"CsvMetadataSchema","longname":"CsvMetadataSchema","name":"CsvMetadataSchema","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Flat query parameters for `POST /csv/metadata`.\n`maxRows` caps the per-cell type census; row and column counting always scans the whole file.","meta":{"lineno":117},"order":5,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/csv/schema.js:96","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/csv/schema.ts:132"},"level":0}],"fp":"6552450c482f61f0943b506aab1779c1422c5ea4cd149646a3e41f7110b79224","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730449192,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/resources/csv/schema.ts":{"fp":"a7fc9fb56a57a699eced2449a1507bea1031534aa913299ee545a27b745cc4da","issues":[],"kind":"md","markdown":"## Members\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#options\">options</a></dt>\n<dd><p>csv-stringify options (names kept as in the library). <code>escape_formulas</code> defaults to true.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#records\">records</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Rows to serialize; objects map keys to cells, arrays emit positional cells.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n## Constants\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#CsvBuildSchema\">CsvBuildSchema</a></dt>\n<dd><p>JSON body for <code>POST /csv/build</code>: rows in, CSV bytes out.\nElements may be row objects or arrays of cell values.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#csvParseOptions\">csvParseOptions</a></dt>\n<dd><p>csv-parse options shared by <code>/csv/extract</code> and <code>/csv/metadata</code> (function-valued options excluded).</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#CsvExtractSchema\">CsvExtractSchema</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Flat query parameters for <code>POST /csv/extract</code>.\nThe raw CSV travels in the request body; everything here is csv-parse options.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#CsvMetadataSchema\">CsvMetadataSchema</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Flat query parameters for <code>POST /csv/metadata</code>.\n<code>maxRows</code> caps the per-cell type census; row and column counting always scans the whole file.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"options\"></a>\n\n## options\ncsv-stringify options (names kept as in the library). `escape_formulas` defaults to true.\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/csv/schema.ts:24  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/csv/schema.js:14\n<a name=\"records\"></a>\n\n## records\nRows to serialize; objects map keys to cells, arrays emit positional cells.\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/csv/schema.ts:46  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/csv/schema.js:33\n<a name=\"CsvBuildSchema\"></a>\n\n## CsvBuildSchema\nJSON body for `POST /csv/build`: rows in, CSV bytes out.\nElements may be row objects or arrays of cell values.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/csv/schema.ts:19  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/csv/schema.js:12\n<a name=\"csvParseOptions\"></a>\n\n## csvParseOptions\ncsv-parse options shared by `/csv/extract` and `/csv/metadata` (function-valued options excluded).\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/csv/schema.ts:57  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/csv/schema.js:36\n<a name=\"CsvExtractSchema\"></a>\n\n## CsvExtractSchema\nFlat query parameters for `POST /csv/extract`.\nThe raw CSV travels in the request body; everything here is csv-parse options.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/csv/schema.ts:102  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/csv/schema.js:76\n<a name=\"CsvMetadataSchema\"></a>\n\n## CsvMetadataSchema\nFlat query parameters for `POST /csv/metadata`.\n`maxRows` caps the per-cell type census; row and column counting always scans the whole file.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/csv/schema.ts:132  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/csv/schema.js:96\n","symbols":6,"lastUsed":1795730449272},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/docx/docx.controller.spec.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"rawSink","longname":"rawSink","name":"rawSink","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Creates a Writable raw sink with `setHeader` mocks for assertions.","params":[],"returns":[{"description":"A writable with a mocked `setHeader`.","type":{"names":["Writable & { setHeader: ReturnType<typeof vi.fn>; }"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":8},"order":0,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/backend/src/resources/docx/docx.controller.spec.ts:10"},"level":0}],"fp":"ebbbd07ce92f1a157354f2053e89fb4810b0f5ef48db86e5d5d5ee97a6ded138","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730449245,"symbols":0},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/docx/docx.controller.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"DocxController","longname":"DocxController","name":"DocxController","kind":"member","scope":"global","description":"DOCX routes. `/docx/build` consumes JSON and bypasses the media\ninterceptors by design (JSON bodies are never virus-scanned or signature-probed);\n`/docx/extract` and `/docx/metadata` take the binary upload and are ClamAV-scanned.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":46},"order":0,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/docx/docx.controller.js:21","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/docx/docx.controller.ts:28"},"level":0},{"id":"DocxController#build","longname":"DocxController#build","name":"build","kind":"function","scope":"instance","description":"Builds a .docx from the JSON payload (201).","memberof":"DocxC