:["{ promise: Promise<T>; resolve: (value: PromiseLike<T> | T) => void; }"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":21},"order":0,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/backend/src/resources/docx/worker/worker.spec.ts:23"},"level":0},{"id":"captureStdout","longname":"captureStdout","name":"captureStdout","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Captures the worker's stdout byte channel and resolves as soon as the first\nwrite lands, so tests never depend on wall-clock timing.","params":[],"returns":[{"description":"The captured writes and a promise resolving on the first write.","type":{"names":["{ writes: Buffer<ArrayBufferLike>[]; written: Promise<void>; }"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":35},"order":1,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/backend/src/resources/docx/worker/worker.spec.ts:38"},"level":0}],"fp":"944b6bf1d6d28791b8dbdae4a2580403ec8b00290ecbbdb2b63d7b7e79ed5a9e","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730467063,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/resources/docx/worker/worker.spec.ts":{"fp":"896d462ceedb0096a9f004145568fe4ac461324c13a780236d1415fd12322a6e","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","markdown":"## Functions\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#deferred\">deferred()</a> ⇒ <code>{ promise: Promise&lt;T&gt;; resolve: (value: PromiseLike&lt;T&gt; | T) &#x3D;&gt; void; }</code></dt>\n<dd><p>A promise with an externally callable resolver. The resolver stays on an\nobject property instead of being extracted into a bare local: this package\ntargets ES2023, whose lib has no Promise.withResolvers.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#captureStdout\">captureStdout()</a> ⇒ <code>{ writes: Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;[]; written: Promise&lt;void&gt;; }</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Captures the worker&#39;s stdout byte channel and resolves as soon as the first\nwrite lands, so tests never depend on wall-clock timing.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"deferred\"></a>\n\n## deferred() ⇒ <code>{ promise: Promise&lt;T&gt;; resolve: (value: PromiseLike&lt;T&gt; \\| T) &#x3D;&gt; void; }</code>\nA promise with an externally callable resolver. The resolver stays on an\nobject property instead of being extracted into a bare local: this package\ntargets ES2023, whose lib has no Promise.withResolvers.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>{ promise: Promise&lt;T&gt;; resolve: (value: PromiseLike&lt;T&gt; \\| T) &#x3D;&gt; void; }</code> - The promise and its resolver.  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/docx/worker/worker.spec.ts:23  \n<a name=\"captureStdout\"></a>\n\n## captureStdout() ⇒ <code>{ writes: Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;[]; written: Promise&lt;void&gt;; }</code>\nCaptures the worker's stdout byte channel and resolves as soon as the first\nwrite lands, so tests never depend on wall-clock timing.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>{ writes: Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;[]; written: Promise&lt;void&gt;; }</code> - The captured writes and a promise resolving on the first write.  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/docx/worker/worker.spec.ts:38  \n","symbols":2,"lastUsed":1795730467191},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/font/font.controller.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"FontController","longname":"FontController","name":"FontController","kind":"member","scope":"global","description":"Font routes. All routes take the binary upload and bypass the JSON parser by\ndesign; they are ClamAV-scanned and font-signature gated (TTF/OTF/WOFF/WOFF2/TTC).","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":46},"order":0,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/font/font.controller.js:22","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/font/font.controller.ts:36"},"level":0},{"id":"FontController#extract","longname":"FontController#extract","name":"extract","kind":"function","scope":"instance","description":"Extracts the font's coverage and glyph inventory (201).","memberof":"FontController","params":[{"description":"Optional collection member.","name":"query","type":{"names":["{ [x: string]: any; limit?: number; }"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The extraction document.","type":{"names":["Promise<{ availableFeatures: string[]; collection: string[]; familyName: string; format: string; glyphs: Record<string, unknown>[]; numGlyphs: number; postscriptName: string; returnedGlyphs: number; }>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":84},"order":1,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/font/font.controller.js:29","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/font/font.controller.ts:49"},"level":0},{"id":"FontController#metadata","longname":"FontController#metadata","name":"metadata","kind":"function","scope":"instance","description":"Normalized font metadata (201).","memberof":"FontController","params":[{"description":"Optional collection member.","name":"query","type":{"names":["{ [x: string]: any; }"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The metadata document.","type":{"names":["Promise<{ ascent: number; availableFeatures: string[]; bbox: import(\"fontkit\").BBOX; capHeight: number; characterSetSize: number; collection: string[]; copyright: string; descent: number; embedding: { bitmapOnly: boolean; editable: boolean; noEmbedding: boolean; noSubsetting: boolean; viewOnly: boolean; }; familyName: string; format: string; fullName: string; italicAngle: number; license: string; licenseURL: string; lineGap: number; namedVariations: Record<string, unknown>; numGlyphs: number; postscriptName: string; subfamilyName: string; underlinePosition: number; underlineThickness: number; unitsPerEm: number; variationAxes: Partial<Record<string, { name: string; min: number; default: number; max: number; }>>; version: number; weightClass: number; xHeight: number; }>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":92},"order":2,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/font/font.controller.js:32","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/font/font.controller.ts:62"},"level":0},{"id":"FontController#shape","longname":"FontController#shape","name":"shape","kind":"function","scope":"instance","description":"Shapes text with the font's OpenType engine (201).","memberof":"FontController","para