issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730467192,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/resources/font/font.controller.ts":{"fp":"e8575fe929bd77b862f26e1405fe3578255d61b8a7e8adff92de7fcdc57efeb8","issues":[],"kind":"md","markdown":"<a name=\"FontController\"></a>\n\n## FontController\nFont routes. All routes take the binary upload and bypass the JSON parser by\ndesign; they are ClamAV-scanned and font-signature gated (TTF/OTF/WOFF/WOFF2/TTC).\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/font/font.controller.ts:36  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/font/font.controller.js:22\n\n* [FontController](#FontController)\n    * [.extract(query)](#FontController+extract) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;{ availableFeatures: string[]; collection: string[]; familyName: string; format: string; glyphs: Record&lt;string, unknown&gt;[]; numGlyphs: number; postscriptName: string; returnedGlyphs: number; }&gt;</code>\n    * [.metadata(query)](#FontController+metadata) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;{ ascent: number; availableFeatures: string[]; bbox: import(&quot;fontkit&quot;).BBOX; capHeight: number; characterSetSize: number; collection: string[]; copyright: string; descent: number; embedding: { bitmapOnly: boolean; editable: boolean; noEmbedding: boolean; noSubsetting: boolean; viewOnly: boolean; }; familyName: string; format: string; fullName: string; italicAngle: number; license: string; licenseURL: string; lineGap: number; namedVariations: Record&lt;string, unknown&gt;; numGlyphs: number; postscriptName: string; subfamilyName: string; underlinePosition: number; underlineThickness: number; unitsPerEm: number; variationAxes: Partial&lt;Record&lt;string, { name: string; min: number; default: number; max: number; }&gt;&gt;; version: number; weightClass: number; xHeight: number; }&gt;</code>\n    * [.shape(query)](#FontController+shape) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;{ advanceHeight: number; advanceWidth: number; bbox: import(&quot;fontkit&quot;).BBOX; direction: string; features: Record&lt;string, boolean&gt;; format: string; glyphs: { xAdvance: number; yAdvance: number; xOffset: number; yOffset: number; advanceWidth: number; codePoints: number[]; id: number; isLigature: boolean; isMark: boolean; name: string; }[]; language: string; script: string; }&gt;</code>\n    * [.subset(response, query)](#FontController+subset) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code>\n\n<a name=\"FontController+extract\"></a>\n\n### fontController.extract(query) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;{ availableFeatures: string[]; collection: string[]; familyName: string; format: string; glyphs: Record&lt;string, unknown&gt;[]; numGlyphs: number; postscriptName: string; returnedGlyphs: number; }&gt;</code>\nExtracts the font's coverage and glyph inventory (201).\n\n**Kind**: instance method of [<code>FontController</code>](#FontController)  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;{ availableFeatures: string[]; collection: string[]; familyName: string; format: string; glyphs: Record&lt;string, unknown&gt;[]; numGlyphs: number; postscriptName: string; returnedGlyphs: number; }&gt;</code> - The extraction document.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| query | <code>{ [x: string]: any; limit?: number; }</code> | Optional collection member. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/font/font.controller.ts:49  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/font/font.controller.js:29\n<a name=\"FontController+metadata\"></a>\n\n### fontController.metadata(query) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;{ ascent: number; availableFeatures: string[]; bbox: import(&quot;fontkit&quot;).BBOX; capHeight: number; characterSetSize: number; collection: string[]; copyright: string; descent: number; embedding: { bitmapOnly: boolean; editable: boolean; noEmbedding: boolean; noSubsetting: boolean; viewOnly: boolean; }; familyName: string; format: string; fullName: string; italicAngle: number; license: string; licenseURL: string; lineGap: number; namedVariations: Record&lt;string, unknown&gt;; numGlyphs: number; postscriptName: string; subfamilyName: string; underlinePosition: number; underlineThickness: number; unitsPerEm: number; variationAxes: Partial&lt;Record&lt;string, { name: string; min: number; default: number; max: number; }&gt;&gt;; version: number; weightClass: number; xHeight: number; }&gt;</code>\nNormalized font metadata (201).\n\n**Kind**: instance method of [<code>FontController</code>](#FontController)  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;{ ascent: number; availableFeatures: string[]; bbox: import(&quot;fontkit&quot;).BBOX; capHeight: number; characterSetSize: number; collection: string[]; copyright: string; descent: number; embedding: { bitmapOnly: boolean; editable: boolean; noEmbedding: boolean; noSubsetting: boolean; viewOnly: boolean; }; familyName: string; format: string; fullName: string; italicAngle: number; license: string; licenseURL: string; lineGap: number; namedVariations: Record&lt;string, unknown&gt;; numGlyphs: number; postscriptName: string; subfamilyName: string; underlinePosition: number; underlineThickness: number; unitsPerEm: number; variationAxes: Partial&lt;Record&lt;string, { name: string; min: number; default: number; max: number; }&gt;&gt;; version: number; weightClass: number; xHeight: number; }&gt;</code> - The metadata document.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| query | <code>{ [x: string]: any; }</code> | Optional collection member. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/font/font.controller.ts:62  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/font/font.controller.js:32\n<a name=\"FontController+shape\"></a>\n\n### fontController.shape(query) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;{ advanceHeight: number; advanceWidth: number; bbox: import(&quot;fontkit&quot;).BBOX; direction: string; features: Record&lt;string, boolean&gt;; format: string; glyphs: { xAdvance: number; yAdvance: number; xOffset: number; yOffset: number; advanceWidth: number; codePoints: number[]; id: number; isLigature: boolean; isMark: boolean; name: string; }[]; language: string; script: string; }&gt;</code>\nShapes text with the font's OpenType engine (201).\n\n**Kind**: instance method of [<code>FontController</code>](#FontController)  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;{ advanceHeight: number; advanceWidth: number; bbox: import(&quot;fontkit&quot;).BBOX; direction: string; features: Record&lt;string, boolean&gt;; format: string; glyphs: { xAdvance: number; yAdvance: number; xOffset: number; yOffset: number; advanceWidth: number; codePoints: number[]; id: number; isLigature: boolean; isMark: boolean; name: string; }[]; language: string; script: string; }&gt;</code> - The shaped glyph run.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| query | <code>{ [x: string]: any; direction?: &quot;auto&quot; \\| &quot;ltr&quot; \\| &quot;rtl&quot;; }</code> | Text plus optional script/language/direction/features. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/font/font.controller.ts:75  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/font/font.controller.js:35\n<a name=\"FontController+subset\"></a>\n\n### fontController.subset(response, query) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code>\nSubsets the font to the glyphs needed for the given text (201).\nThe output is a minimal sfnt for PDF embedding (no cmap); it is not a web font.\n\n**Kind**: instance method of [<code>FontController</code>](#FontController)  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code> - The subsetted font bytes (201).  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| response | <code>FastifyReply&lt;import(&quot;fastify&quot;).RouteGenericInterface, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).RawServerDefault, import(&quot;http&quot;).IncomingMessage, import(&quot;http&quot;).ServerResponse&lt;import(&quot;http&quot;).IncomingMessage&gt;, unknown, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).FastifySchema, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).FastifyTypeProviderDefault, unknown&gt;</code> | Raw reply, streamed as font/ttf. |\n| query | <code>{ [x: string]: any; }</code> | The text to include. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/reso