><p>Comma-separated feature tags to enable or disable with a leading &#39;-&#39; (e.g. &#39;liga,-dlig,kern&#39;).</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#font\">font</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Collection member to select by PostScript name; defaults to the first.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#language\">language</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Language override (e.g. en); defaults to the script default.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#script\">script</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Script override (e.g. Latn); defaults to the shaper&#39;s detection.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#text\">text</a></dt>\n<dd><p>The text to shape (max 500 chars).</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#font\">font</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Collection member to select by PostScript name; defaults to the first.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#text\">text</a></dt>\n<dd><p>The text to include in the subset (max 10 000 chars).</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n## Constants\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#FONT_MIMES\">FONT_MIMES</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Plain mimes (no macro/executable fonts); file-type detects all of these.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#isFontMime\">isFontMime</a> ⇒ <code>boolean</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Whether the mime is a supported font container.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#FontMetaSchema\">FontMetaSchema</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Flat query parameters for <code>POST /font/metadata</code>.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#FontExtractSchema\">FontExtractSchema</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Flat query parameters for <code>POST /font/extract</code>.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#FontShapeSchema\">FontShapeSchema</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Flat query parameters for <code>POST /font/shape</code>.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#FontSubsetSchema\">FontSubsetSchema</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Flat query parameters for <code>POST /font/subset</code>.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"font\"></a>\n\n## font\nCollection member to select by PostScript name; defaults to the first.\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/font/schema.ts:33  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/font/schema.js:14\n<a name=\"font\"></a>\n\n## font\nCollection member to select by PostScript name; defaults to the first.\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/font/schema.ts:49  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/font/schema.js:19\n<a name=\"limit\"></a>\n\n## limit\nMaximum glyph records to return (default: 10 000, capped at the `limit` max).\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/font/schema.ts:53  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/font/schema.js:20\n<a name=\"direction\"></a>\n\n## direction\nDirection override; defaults to the script default.\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/font/schema.ts:68  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/font/schema.js:24\n<a name=\"features\"></a>\n\n## features\nComma-separated feature tags to enable or disable with a leading '-' (e.g. 'liga,-dlig,kern').\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/font/schema.ts:72  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/font/schema.js:25\n<a name=\"font\"></a>\n\n## font\nCollection member to select by PostScript name; defaults to the first.\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/font/schema.ts:76  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/font/schema.js:26\n<a name=\"language\"></a>\n\n## language\nLanguage override (e.g. en); defaults to the script default.\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/font/schema.ts:80  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/font/schema.js:27\n<a name=\"script\"></a>\n\n## script\nScript override (e.g. Latn); defaults to the shaper's detection.\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/font/schema.ts:84  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/font/schema.js:28\n<a name=\"text\"></a>\n\n## text\nThe text to shape (max 500 chars).\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/font/schema.ts:88  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/font/schema.js:29\n<a name=\"font\"></a>\n\n## font\nCollection member to select by PostScript name; defaults to the first.\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/font/schema.ts:102  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/font/schema.js:32\n<a name=\"text\"></a>\n\n## text\nThe text to include in the subset (max 10 000 chars).\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/font/schema.ts:106  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/font/schema.js:33\n<a name=\"FONT_MIMES\"></a>\n\n## FONT\\_MIMES\nPlain mimes (no macro/executable fonts); file-type detects all of these.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/font/schema.ts:8  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/font/schema.js:3\n<a name=\"isFontMime\"></a>\n\n## isFontMime ⇒ <code>boolean</code>\nWhether the mime is a supported font container.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \n**Returns**: <code>boolean</code> - True for the five supported container mimes.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| mime | <code>string</code> | The lowercased content-type mime. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/font/schema.ts:23  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/font/schema.js:11\n<a name=\"FontMetaSchema\"></a>\n\n## FontMetaSchema\nFlat query parameters for `POST /font/metadata`.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/font/schema.ts:28  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/font/schema.js:12\n<a name=\"FontExtractSchema\"></a>\n\n## FontExtractSchema\nFlat query parameters for `POST /font/extract`.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/font/schema.ts:44  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/font/schema.js:17\n<a name=\"FontShapeSchema\"></a>\n\n## FontShapeSchema\nFlat query parameters for `POST /font/shape`.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/font/schema.ts:64  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/font/schema.js:23\n<a name=\"FontSubsetSchema\"></a>\n\n## FontSubsetSchema\nFlat query parameters for `POST /font/subset`.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/font/schema.ts:98  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/font/schema.js:31\n","symbols":17,"lastUsed":1795730467462},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/font/font.service.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"FontService","longname":"FontService","name":"FontService","kind":"member","scope":"global","description":"Font feature service: parses sfnt containers (metadata, extraction, shaping, subsetting).","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":184},"order":3,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/font/font.service.js:131","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/font/font.service.ts:167"},"level":0},{"id":"signatureFormat","longname":"signatureFormat","name":"signatureFormat","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Maps the file's magic bytes to a short format tag.","params":[{"description":"The buffered upload.","name":"buffer","type":{"names":["Buffer<ArrayBufferLike>"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The format tag (ttf, otf, woff, woff2).","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":124},"order":2,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/font/font.service.js:79","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/font/font.service.ts:106"},"level":0},{"id":"readBody","longname":"readBody","name":"readBody","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Only font container mimes; macro/executable payloads are rejected at the boundary.","params":[{"description":"Normalized request context.","name":"cls","type":{"names":["NormalizedClsService"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The body bytes, capped.","type":{"names":["Promise<Buffer<ArrayBufferLike>>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":48},"async":true,"order":0,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/font/font.service.js:19","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/font/font.service.ts:22"},"level":0},{"id":"assertFontSignature","longname":"assertFontSignature","name":"assertFontSignature","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Signature must be a font container; closes the renamed-image and non-font holes.","params":[{"description":"The buffered upload.","name":"buffer","type":{"names":["Buffer<ArrayBufferLike>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":64},"async":true,"order":1,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/font/font.service.js:31","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/font/font.service.ts:39"},"returns":[{"type":{"names":["Promise<void>"]}}],"level":0},{"id":"parseFeatures","longname":"parseFeatures","name":"parseFeatures","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Parses 'liga,kern,-dlig' into a fontkit features record (enabled default, '-' disables).\nUnknown 4-character tags pass through to the shaper (it ignores them); malformed tags are a client error.","params":[{"description":"The raw feature string from the query.","name":"raw","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The features record, or undefined when no features were given.","type":{"names":["Record<string, boolean>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":370},"order":8,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/font/font.service.js:261","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/font/font.service.ts:346"},"level":0},{"id":"FontService#extract","longname":"FontService#extract","name":"extract","kind":"function","scope":"instance","description":"Extracts every glyph's coverage and identity plus the supported OpenType features.","memberof":"FontService","params":[{"description":"The validated query object.","name":"query","type":{"names":["{ font?: string; limit?: number; }"]}},{"description":"Optional collection member to select by PostScript name.","name":"query.font"},{"description":"Optional cap on the number of returned glyph records.","name":"query.limit"}],"returns":[{"description":"The extraction document (could be large for CJK fonts).","type":{"names":["Promise<{ availableFeatures: string[]; collection: string[]; familyName: string; format: string; glyphs: Record<string, unknown>[]; numGlyphs: number; postscriptName: string; returnedGlyphs: number; }>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":209},"async":true,"order":4,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/font/font.service.js:136","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/font/font.service.ts:177"},"level":0},{"id":"FontService#metadata","longname":"FontService#metadata","name":"metadata","kind":"function","scope":"instance","description":"Reads the uploaded font (ClamAV-scanned, signature-gated) and normalizes its metadata.","memberof":"FontService","params":[{"description":"The validated query object.","name":"query","type":{"names":["{ font?: string; }"]}},{"description":"Optional collection member to select by PostScript name.","name":"query.font"}],"returns":[{"description":"The font metadata document.","type":{"names":["Promise<{ ascent: number; availableFeatures: string[]; bbox: fontkit.BBOX; capHeight: number; characterSetSize: number; collection: string[]; copyright: string; descent: number; embedding: { bitmapOnly: boolean; editable: boolean; noEmbedding: boolean; noSubsetting: boolean; viewOnly: boolean; }; familyName: string; format: string; fullName: string; italicAngle: number; license: string; licenseURL: string; lineGap: number; namedVariations: Record<string, unknown>; numGlyphs: number; postscriptName: string; subfamilyName: string; underlinePosition: number; underlineThickness: number; unitsPerEm: number; variationAxes: Partial<Record<string, { name: string; min: number; default: number; max: number; }>>; version: number; weightClass: number; xHeight: number; }>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":261},"async":true,"order":5,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/font/font.service.js:180","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/font/font.service.ts:227"},"level":0},{"id":"FontService#shape","longname":"FontService#shape","name":"shape","kind":"function","scope":"instance","description":"Shapes text with the font's OpenType engine.","memberof":"FontService","params":[{"description":"The validated query object.","name":"query","type":{"names":["{ direction?: \"auto\" | \"ltr\" | \"rtl\"; features?: string; font?: string; language?: string; script?: string; text: string; }"]}},{"description":"Optional direction override; defaults to the script default.","name":"query.direction"},{"description":"Optional `+tag`/`-tag`/`tag` comma-separated feature overrides.","name":"query.features"},{"description":"Optional collection member to select by PostScript name.","name":"query.font"},{"description":"Optional language override; defaults to the script default.","name":"query.language"},{"description":"Optional script override; defaults to detection.","name":"query.script"},{"description":"The text to shape.","name":"query.text"}],"returns":[{"description":"The glyph run with positions and aggregate metrics.","type":{"names":["Promise<{ advanceHeight: number; advanceWidth: number; bbox: fontkit.BBOX; direction: string; features: Record<string, boolean>; format: string; glyphs: { xAdvance: number; yAdvance: number; xOffset: number; yOffset: number; advanceWidth: number; codePoints: number[]; id: number; isLigature: boolean; isMark: boolean; name: string; }[]; language: string; script: string; }>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":283},"async":true,"order":6,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/font/font.service.js:191","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/font/font.service.ts:249"},"level":0},{"id":"FontService#subset","longname":"FontService#subset","name":"subset","kind":"function","scope":"instance","description":"Subsets the font to the glyphs needed for the given text.\nThe output is a minimal sfnt intended for PDF embedding (no cmap); it is not\na standalone web font.","memberof":"FontService","params":[{"description":"The validated query object.","name":"query","type":{"names":["{ font?: string; text: string; }"]}},{"description":"Optional collection member to select by PostScript name.","name":"query.font"},{"description":"The text whose glyphs are kept.","name":"query.text"}],"returns":[{"description":"The subsetted sfnt bytes.","type":{"names":["Promise<Buffer<ArrayBuffer>>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":328},"async":true,"order":7,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/font/font.service.js:225","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/font/font.service.ts:307"},"level":0}],"fp":"e79cdf565087bbe9070bed09665acf81c5fc949a21ef9619a1e23216114c1499","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730467333,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/resources/font/font.service.ts":{"fp":"97da4549d6cff6a26fcb1a16fe4bb5dc4711cc6384e239c5a60e7f7aec5b5f0f","issues":[],"kind":"md","markdown":"## Members\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#FontService\">FontService</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Font feature service: parses sfnt containers (metadata, extraction, shaping, subsetting).</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n## Constants\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#signatureFormat\">signatureFormat</a> ⇒ <code>string</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Maps the file&#39;s magic bytes to a short format tag.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n## Functions\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#readBody\">readBody(cls)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Only font container mimes; macro/executable payloads are rejected at the boundary.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#assertFontSignature\">assertFontSignature(buffer)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Signature must be a font container; closes the renamed-image and non-font holes.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#parseFeatures\">parseFeatures(raw)</a> ⇒ <code>Record&lt;string, boolean&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Parses &#39;liga,kern,-dlig&#39; into a fontkit features record (enabled default, &#39;-&#39; disables).\nUnknown 4-character tags pass through to the shaper (it ignores them); malformed tags are a client error.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"FontService\"></a>\n\n## FontService\nFont feature service: parses sfnt containers (metadata, extraction, shaping, subsetting).\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/font/font.service.ts:167  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/font/font.service.js:131\n\n* [FontService](#FontService)\n    * [.extract(query)](#FontService+extract) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;{ availableFeatures: string[]; collection: string[]; familyName: string; format: string; glyphs: Record&lt;string, unknown&gt;[]; numGlyphs: number; postscriptName: string; returnedGlyphs: number; }&gt;</code>\n    * [.metadata(query)](#FontService+metadata) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;{ ascent: number; availableFeatures: string[]; bbox: fontkit.BBOX; capHeight: number; characterSetSize: number; collection: string[]; copyright: string; descent: number; embedding: { bitmapOnly: boolean; editable: boolean; noEmbedding: boolean; noSubsetting: boolean; viewOnly: boolean; }; familyName: string; format: string; fullName: string; italicAngle: number; license: string; licenseURL: string; lineGap: number; namedVariations: Record&lt;string, unknown&gt;; numGlyphs: number; postscriptName: string; subfamilyName: string; underlinePosition: number; underlineThickness: number; unitsPerEm: number; variationAxes: Partial&lt;Record&lt;string, { name: string; min: number; default: number; max: number; }&gt;&gt;; version: number; weightClass: number; xHeight: number; }&gt;</code>\n    * [.shape(query)](#FontService+shape) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;{ advanceHeight: number; advanceWidth: number; bbox: fontkit.BBOX; direction: string; features: Record&lt;string, boolean&gt;; format: string; glyphs: { xAdvance: number; yAdvance: number; xOffset: number; yOffset: number; advanceWidth: number; codePoints: number[]; id: number; isLigature: boolean; isMark: boolean; name: string; }[]; language: string; script: string; }&gt;</code>\n    * [.subset(query)](#FontService+subset) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;Buffer&lt;ArrayBuffer&gt;&gt;</code>\n\n<a name=\"FontService+extract\"></a>\n\n### fontService.extract(query) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;{ availableFeatures: string[]; collection: string[]; familyName: string; format: string; glyphs: Record&lt;string, unknown&gt;[]; numGlyphs: number; postscriptName: string; returnedGlyphs: number; }&gt;</code>\nExtracts every glyph's coverage and identity plus the supported OpenType features.\n\n**Kind**: instance method of [<code>FontService</code>](#FontService)  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;{ availableFeatures: string[]; collection: string[]; familyName: string; format: string; glyphs: Record&lt;string, unknown&gt;[]; numGlyphs: number; postscriptName: string; returnedGlyphs: number; }&gt;</code> - The extraction document (could be large for CJK fonts).  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| query | <code>{ font?: string; limit?: number; }</code> | The validated query object. |\n| query.font |  | Optional collection member to select by PostScript name. |\n| query.limit |  | Optional cap on the number of returned glyph records. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/font/font.service.ts:177  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/font/font.service.js:136\n<a name=\"FontService+metadata\"></a>\n\n### fontService.metadata(query) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;{ ascent: number; availableFeatures: string[]; bbox: fontkit.BBOX; capHeight: number; characterSetSize: number; collection: string[]; copyright: string; descent: number; embedding: { bitmapOnly: boolean; editable: boolean; noEmbedding: boolean; noSubsetting: boolean; viewOnly: boolean; }; familyName: string; format: string; fullName: string; italicAngle: number; license: string; licenseURL: string; lineGap: number; namedVariations: Record&lt;string, unknown&gt;; numGlyphs: number; postscriptName: string; subfamilyName: string; underlinePosition: number; underlineThickness: number; unitsPerEm: number; variationAxes: Partial&lt;Record&lt;string, { name: string; min: number; default: number; max: number; }&gt;&gt;; version: number; weightClass: number; xHeight: number; }&gt;</code>\nReads the uploaded font (ClamAV-scanned, signature-gated) and normalizes its metadata.\n\n**Kind**: instance method of [<code>FontService</code>](#FontService)  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;{ ascent: number; availableFeatures: string[]; bbox: fontkit.BBOX; capHeight: number; characterSetSize: number; collection: string[]; copyright: string; descent: number; embedding: { bitmapOnly: boolean; editable: boolean; noEmbedding: boolean; noSubsetting: boolean; viewOnly: boolean; }; familyName: string; format: string; fullName: string; italicAngle: number; license: string; licenseURL: string; lineGap: number; namedVariations: Record&lt;string, unknown&gt;; numGlyphs: number; postscriptName: string; subfamilyName: string; underlinePosition: number; underlineThickness: number; unitsPerEm: number; variationAxes: Partial&lt;Record&lt;string, { name: string; min: number; default: number; max: number; }&gt;&gt;; version: number; weightClass: number; xHeight: number; }&gt;</code> - The font metadata document.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| query | <code>{ font?: string; }</code> | The validated query object. |\n| query.font |  | Optional collection member to select by PostScript name. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/font/font.service.ts:227  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/font/font.service.js:180\n<a name=\"FontService+shape\"></a>\n\n### fontService.shape(query) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;{ advanceHeight: number; advanceWidth: number; bbox: fontkit.BBOX; direction: string; features: Record&lt;string, boolean&gt;; format: string; glyphs: { xAdvance: number; yAdvance: number; xOffset: number; yOffset: number; advanceWidth: number; codePoints: number[]; id: number; isLigature: boolean; isMark: boolean; name: string; }[]; language: string; script: string; }&gt;</code>\nShapes text with the font's OpenType engine.\n\n**Kind**: instance method of [<code>FontService</code>](#FontService)  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;{ advanceHeight: number; advanceWidth: number; bbox: fontkit.BBOX; direction: string; features: Record&lt;string, boolean&gt;; format: string; glyphs: { xAdvance: number; yAdvance: number; xOffset: number; yOffset: number; advanceWidth: number; codePoints: number[]; id: number; isLigature: boolean; isMark: boolean; name: string; }[]; language: string; script: string; }&gt;</code> - The glyph run with positions and aggregate metrics.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| query | <code>{ direction?: &quot;auto&quot; \\| &quot;ltr&quot; \\| &quot;rtl&quot;; features?: string; font?: string; language?: string; script?: string; text: string; }</code> | The validated query object. |\n| query.direction |  | Optional direction override; defaults to the script default. |\n| query.features |  | Optional `+tag`/`-tag`/`tag` comma-separated feature overrides. |\n| query.font |  | Optional collection member to select by PostScript name. |\n| query.language |  | Optional language override; defaults to the script default. |\n| query.script |  | Optional script override; defaults to detection. |\n| query.text |  | The text to shape. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/font/font.service.ts:249  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/font/font.service.js:191\n<a name=\"FontService+subset\"></a>\n\n### fontService.subset(query) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;Buffer&lt;ArrayBuffer&gt;&gt;</code>\nSubsets the font to the glyphs needed for the given text.\nThe output is a minimal sfnt intended for PDF embedding (no cmap); it is not\na standalone web font.\n\n**Kind**: instance method of [<code>FontService</code>](#FontService)  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;Buffer&lt;ArrayBuffer&gt;&gt;</code> - The subsetted sfnt bytes.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| query | <code>{ font?: string; text: string; }</code> | The validated query object. |\n| query.font |  | Optional collection member to select by PostScript name. |\n| query.text |  | The text whose glyphs are kept. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/font/font.service.ts:307  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/font/font.service.js:225\n<a name=\"signatureFormat\"></a>\n\n## signatureFormat ⇒ <code>string</code>\nMaps the file's magic bytes to a short format tag.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \n**Returns**: <code>string</code> - The format tag (ttf, otf, woff, woff2).  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| buffer | <code>Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;</code> | The buffered upload. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/font/font.service.ts:106  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/font/font.service.js:79\n<a name=\"readBody\"></a>\n\n## readBody(cls) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;&gt;</code>\nOnly font container mimes; macro/executable payloads are rejected at the boundary.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;&gt;</code> - The body bytes, capped.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| cls | <code>NormalizedClsService</code> | Normalized request context. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/font/font.service.ts:22  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/font/font.service.js:19\n<a name=\"assertFontSignature\"></a>\n\n## assertFontSignature(buffer) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code>\nSignature must be a font container; closes the renamed-image and non-font holes.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| buffer | <code>Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;</code> | The buffered upload. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/font/font.service.ts:39  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/font/font.service.js:31\n<a name=\"parseFeatures\"></a>\n\n## parseFeatures(raw) ⇒ <code>Record&lt;string, boolean&gt;</code>\nParses 'liga,kern,-dlig' into a fontkit features record (enabled default, '-' disables).\nUnknown 4-character tags pass through to the shaper (it ignores them); malformed tags are a client error.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Record&lt;string, boolean&gt;</code> - The features record, or undefined when no features were given.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| raw | <code>string</code> | The raw feature string from the query. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/font/font.service.ts:346  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/font/font.service.js:261\n","symbols":9,"lastUsed":1795730467423},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/image/image-signature.interceptor.spec.ts":{"doclets":[],"fp":"955ade092a1162e023100989dca2d424550a052bb39b9b8cde156c8c5102e8a3","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730467462,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/resources/image/image-signature.interceptor.spec.ts":{"fp":"2c85800b87bfe9f13f4c78c5870f6a47947454a09e5413098185edd6f671d7c9","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","skipped":"no-jsdoc","symbols":0,"lastUsed":1795730467463},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/image/dna.spec.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"chunks","longname":"chunks","name":"chunks","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Yields 21 one-MiB chunks to exceed the 20 MiB cap.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":14},"yields":[{"description":"A 1 MiB zero-filled chunk."}],"generator":true,"order":0,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/backend/src/resources/image/dna.spec.ts:18"},"returns":[{"type":{"names":["Generator<Buffer<ArrayBufferLike>, any, any>"]}}],"level":0},{"id":"jpegStream","longname":"jpegStream","name":"jpegStream","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Opens a fresh readable stream over the JPEG fixture.","params":[],"returns":[{"description":"A readable stream of the fixture bytes.","type":{"names":["Readable"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":23},"order":1,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/backend/src/resources/image/dna.spec.ts:28"},"level":0},{"id":"makeService","longname":"makeService","name":"makeService","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Builds an ImageService with stubbed dependencies for DNA tests.","params":[{"description":"The file signature returned by the stubbed CLS store.","name":"s