","description":"Points stdin/stdout at the tiny fixture and a capturing sink, then runs the worker with explicit data.","params":[{"description":"Worker-thread data (`operation` and optional payload) passed to the worker.","name":"data","type":{"names":["Record<string, unknown>"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The captured stdout chunks.","type":{"names":["Promise<Buffer<ArrayBufferLike>[]>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":49},"async":true,"order":2,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/backend/src/resources/image/image.worker.spec.ts:54"},"level":0}],"fp":"e2f3981011358a9c7f7a78b1625cead7930156e5c5d33f0d4123d5845c888819","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730467702,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/resources/image/image.worker.spec.ts":{"fp":"7ee71eafe6b5ad361bc57f16001e0d02f1b8b9effdf59a01e5de9fa6a956f44d","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","markdown":"## Functions\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#createTinyJpeg\">createTinyJpeg()</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Creates a tiny synthetic JPEG (64x48, blue with a white 16x16 square): large\nenough for every sharp operation in the worker, small enough to keep the\nsuite fast and deterministic.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#capturingStdout\">capturingStdout()</a> ⇒ <code>{ finished: Promise&lt;void&gt;; stdout: Writable; writes: Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;[]; }</code></dt>\n<dd><p>A capturing stdout Writable: <code>writes</code> accumulates chunks, <code>finished</code> resolves on <code>end</code>.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#run\">run(data)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;[]&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Points stdin/stdout at the tiny fixture and a capturing sink, then runs the worker with explicit data.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"createTinyJpeg\"></a>\n\n## createTinyJpeg() ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;&gt;</code>\nCreates a tiny synthetic JPEG (64x48, blue with a white 16x16 square): large\nenough for every sharp operation in the worker, small enough to keep the\nsuite fast and deterministic.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;&gt;</code> - The encoded JPEG bytes.  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/image/image.worker.spec.ts:18  \n<a name=\"capturingStdout\"></a>\n\n## capturingStdout() ⇒ <code>{ finished: Promise&lt;void&gt;; stdout: Writable; writes: Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;[]; }</code>\nA capturing stdout Writable: `writes` accumulates chunks, `finished` resolves on `end`.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>{ finished: Promise&lt;void&gt;; stdout: Writable; writes: Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;[]; }</code> - The writes, the sink and the completion promise.  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/image/image.worker.spec.ts:34  \n<a name=\"run\"></a>\n\n## run(data) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;[]&gt;</code>\nPoints stdin/stdout at the tiny fixture and a capturing sink, then runs the worker with explicit data.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;[]&gt;</code> - The captured stdout chunks.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| data | <code>Record&lt;string, unknown&gt;</code> | Worker-thread data (`operation` and optional payload) passed to the worker. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/image/image.worker.spec.ts:54  \n","symbols":3,"lastUsed":1795730467738},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/image/schema.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"positionKeys","longname":"positionKeys","name":"positionKeys","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"resize position accepts sharp's corner/edge names plus everything in sharp.gravity.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":12},"order":0,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/image/schema.js:8","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/image/schema.ts:16"},"level":0},{"id":"ImageProcessorSchema","longname":"ImageProcessorSchema","name":"ImageProcessorSchema","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Query parameters for `/image/processor`, `/image/metadata`, `/image/dna` and `/image/stats` uploads.","meta":{"lineno":27},"order":1,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/image/schema.js:20","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/image/schema.ts:33"},"level":0},{"id":"LANG_REGEX","longname":"LANG_REGEX","name":"LANG_REGEX","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Case-insensitive language code pattern: a three-letter ISO 639-2 code\noptionally followed by a script suffix (`_latn`, `_cyrl`, ...). Codes are\ncombined with `+` or `,` (up to four). `+` only reaches this endpoint\nURL-encoded (`%2B`), because query-string decoders treat a raw `+` as a space.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":58},"order":2,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/image/schema.js:44","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/image/schema.ts:70"},"level":0},{"id":"OcrSchema","longname":"OcrSchema","name":"OcrSchema","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Query schema for the `/image/ocr` endpoint.","meta":{"lineno":62},"order":3,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/image/schema.js:45","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/image/schema.ts:75"},"level":0}],"fp":"665d8fd1ab45ddd206b58e61d139e15e86318e3b32793903e52921e7e4dbd0db","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730467709,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/resources/image/schema.ts":{"fp":"d8a3b096a1e8522e57d3c5947093dcf3175291fd357adb27a50f16ea8180952c","issues":[],"kind":"md","markdown":"## Constants\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#positionKeys\">positionKeys</a></dt>\n<dd><p>resize position accepts sharp&#39;s corner/edge names plus everything in sharp.gravity.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#ImageProcessorSchema\">ImageProcessorSchema</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Query parameters for <code>/image/processor</code>, <code>/image/metadata</code>, <code>/image/dna</code> and <code>/image/stats</code> uploads.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#LANG_REGEX\">LANG_REGEX</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Case-insensitive language code pattern: a three-letter ISO 639-2 code\noptionally followed by a script suffix (<code>_latn</code>, <code>_cyrl</code>, ...). Codes are\ncombined with <code>+</code> or <code>,</code> (up to four). <code>+</code> only reaches this endpoint\nURL-encoded (<code>%2B</code>), because query-string decoders treat a raw <code>+</code> as a space.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#OcrSchema\">OcrSchema</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Query schema for the <code>/image/ocr</code> endpoint.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"positionKeys\"></a>\n\n## positionKeys\nresize position accepts sharp's corner/edge names plus everything in sharp.gravity.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/image/schema.ts:16  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/image/schema.js:8\n<a name=\"ImageProcessorSchema\"></a>\n\n## ImageProcessorSchema\nQuery parameters for `/image/processor`, `/image/metadata`, `/image/dna` and `/image/stats` uploads.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/image/schema.ts:33  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/image/schema.js:20\n<a name=\"LANG_REGEX\"></a>\n\n## LANG\\_REGEX\nCase-insensitive language code pattern: a three-letter ISO 639-2 code\noptionally followed by a script suffix (`_latn`, `_cyrl`, ...). Codes are\ncombined with `+` or `,` (up to four). `+` only reaches this endpoint\nURL-encoded (`%2B`), because query-string decoders treat a raw `+` as a space.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/image/schema.ts:70  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/image/schema.js:44\n<a name=\"OcrSchema\"></a>\n\n## OcrSchema\nQuery schema for the `/image/ocr` endpoint.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/image/schema.ts:75  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/image/schema.js:45\n","symbols":4,"lastUsed":1795730467789},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/image/tesseract.service.edge.spec.ts":{"doclets":[],"fp":"afb95c858988