din.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;&gt;</code> - The encoded JPEG bytes.  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/image/worker/worker.spec.ts:12  \n<a name=\"importWorker\"></a>\n\n## importWorker(workerData) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code>\nImports the image worker fresh with the given workerData.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| workerData | <code>Record&lt;string, unknown&gt;</code> | the worker payload (operation). |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/image/worker/worker.spec.ts:43  \n","symbols":2,"lastUsed":1795730467954},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/model/gltf.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"ioCache","longname":"ioCache","name":"ioCache","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Lazily-built NodeIO with meshopt and draco registered; wasm modules are created once per process.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":11},"order":0,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/model/gltf.js:7","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/model/gltf.ts:22"},"level":0},{"id":"readModel","longname":"readModel","name":"readModel","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Opens a GLB work package; a single corrupt byte answers 400.","params":[{"description":"The uploaded GLB bytes.","name":"buffer","type":{"names":["Buffer<ArrayBufferLike>"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The parsed gltf-transform document.","type":{"names":["Promise<Document>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":40},"order":1,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/model/gltf.js:29","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/model/gltf.ts:52"},"level":0},{"id":"writeGlb","longname":"writeGlb","name":"writeGlb","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Serializes a document to GLB bytes.","params":[{"description":"The document to serialize.","name":"document","type":{"names":["Document"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The GLB bytes.","type":{"names":["Promise<Uint8Array<ArrayBufferLike>>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":55},"order":2,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/model/gltf.js:38","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/model/gltf.ts:67"},"level":0},{"id":"writeGltfJson","longname":"writeGltfJson","name":"writeGltfJson","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Converts a document to the glTF JSON document plus its resources.","params":[{"description":"The document to convert.","name":"document","type":{"names":["Document"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The JSON document and the resource map.","type":{"names":["Promise<GltfJsonOutput>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":64},"order":3,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/model/gltf.js:42","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/model/gltf.ts:77"},"level":0},{"id":"optimizeDocument","longname":"optimizeDocument","name":"optimizeDocument","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Runs the optimize pipeline in the caller (used by the worker, where transforms are safe).","params":[{"description":"The document to optimize (already opened via {@link readModel}).","name":"document","type":{"names":["Document"]}},{"description":"Compression codec, simplification ratio and weld.","name":"options","type":{"names":["{ compress: \"draco\" | \"meshopt\" | \"none\"; simplify: number; weld: boolean; }"]}},{"description":"The compression codec ('meshopt', 'draco' or 'none').","name":"options.compress"},{"description":"The simplification ratio in [0, 1]; 1 disables it.","name":"options.simplify"},{"description":"Whether to weld bitwise-identical vertices.","name":"options.weld"}],"meta":{"lineno":77},"order":4,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/model/gltf.js:47","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/model/gltf.ts:91"},"returns":[{"type":{"names":["Promise<void>"]}}],"level":0}],"fp":"d4c4131570f47e96786b3dcc821feedfb3b5895fc82b9ce6897fb995a27fe258","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730467962,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/resources/model/gltf.ts":{"fp":"bcc813f593f58acc9ffb7b8599770ead06b2bd9843a0ee83a0801ee6d17daea5","issues":[],"kind":"md","markdown":"## Constants\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#ioCache\">ioCache</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Lazily-built NodeIO with meshopt and draco registered; wasm modules are created once per process.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#readModel\">readModel</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;Document&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Opens a GLB work package; a single corrupt byte answers 400.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#writeGlb\">writeGlb</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;Uint8Array&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Serializes a document to GLB bytes.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#writeGltfJson\">writeGltfJson</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;GltfJsonOutput&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Converts a document to the glTF JSON document plus its resources.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#optimizeDocument\">optimizeDocument</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Runs the optimize pipeline in the caller (used by the worker, where transforms are safe).</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"ioCache\"></a>\n\n## ioCache\nLazily-built NodeIO with meshopt and draco registered; wasm modules are created once per process.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/model/gltf.ts:22  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/model/gltf.js:7\n<a name=\"readModel\"></a>\n\n## readModel ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;Document&gt;</code>\nOpens a GLB work package; a single corrupt byte answers 400.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;Document&gt;</code> - The parsed gltf-transform document.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| buffer | <code>Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;</code> | The uploaded GLB bytes. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/model/gltf.ts:52  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/model/gltf.js:29\n<a name=\"writeGlb\"></a>\n\n## writeGlb ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;Uint8Array&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;&gt;</code>\nSerializes a document to GLB bytes.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;Uint8Array&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;&gt;</code> - The GLB bytes.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| document | <code>Document</code> | The document to serialize. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/model/gltf.ts:67  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/model/gltf.js:38\n<a name=\"writeGltfJson\"></a>\n\n## writeGltfJson ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;GltfJsonOutput&gt;</code>\nConverts a document to the glTF JSON document plus its resources.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;GltfJsonOutput&gt;</code> - The JSON document and the resource map.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| document | <code>Document</code> | The document to convert. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/model/gltf.ts:77  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/model/gltf.js:42\n<a name=\"optimizeDocument\"></a>\n\n## optimizeDocument ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code>\nRuns the optimize pipeline in the caller (used by the worker, where transforms are safe).\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| document | <code>Document</code> | The document to optimize (already opened via [readModel](#readModel)). |\n| options | <code>{ compress: &quot;draco&quot; \\| &quot;meshopt&quot; \\| &quot;none&quot;; simplify: number; weld: boolean; }</code> | Compression codec, simplification ratio and weld. |\n| options.compress |  | The compression codec ('meshopt', 'draco' or 'none'). |\n| options.simplify |  | The simplification ratio in [0, 1]; 1 disables it. |\n| options.weld |  | Whether to weld bitwise-identical vertices. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/model/gltf.ts:91  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/model/gltf.js:47\n","symbols":5,"lastUsed":1795730468027},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/model/model.controller.spec.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"rawSink","longname":"rawSink","name":"rawSink","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Creates a Writable raw sink with `setHeader` mocks for assertions.","params":[],"returns":[{"description":"A writable with a mocked `setHeader`.","type":{"names":["Writable & { setHeader: ReturnType<typeof vi.fn>; }"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":8},"order":0,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/backend/src/resources/model/model.controller.spec.ts:10"},"level":0}],"fp":"e35af53dfeacb16e6634aaae594e93dc839e1fa4e366db94af23a59926fa3187","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730467969,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/resources/model/model.controller.spec.ts":{"fp":"f03cbc0f80d3535d62723adf8499d8b86d8a48c694c8b9680a9b5e77dc2dbc4e","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","markdown":"<a name=\"rawSink\"></a>\n\n## rawSink() ⇒ <code>Writable &amp; { setHeader: ReturnType&lt;typeof vi.fn&gt;; }</code>\nCreates a Writable raw sink with `setHeader` mocks for assertions.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Writable &amp; { setHeader: ReturnType&lt;typeof vi.fn&gt;; }</code> - A writable with a mocked `setHeader`.  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/model/model.controller.spec.ts:10  \n","symbols":1,"lastUsed":1795730467996},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/model/model.controller.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"ModelController","longname":"ModelController","name":"ModelController","kind":"member","scope":"global","description":"GLB routes. All routes take the binary upload and bypass the JSON parser by\ndesign; they are ClamAV-scanned and GLB-signature gated (`glTF` magic).","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":45},"order":0,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/model/model.controller.js:21","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/model/model.controller.ts:34"},"level":0},{"id":"ModelController#convert","longname":"ModelController#convert","name":"convert","kind":"function","scope":"instance","description":"Converts the uploaded GLB between container formats (201).","memberof":"ModelController","params":[{"description":"Raw reply, streamed as model/gltf-b