}; bounds: { max: [number, number, number]; min: [number, number, number]; }; counts: { accessors: number; animations: number; cameras: number; materials: number; meshes: number; nodes: number; primitives: number; scenes: number; skins: number; textures: number; triangles: number; vertices: number; }; extensionsRequired: string[]; extensionsUsed: string[]; format: string; }</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Normalized metadata payload (used by the metadata route).</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#extractOf\">extractOf(document)</a> ⇒ <code>{ animations: { channels: number; name: string; samplers: number; }[]; format: string; materials: { alphaMode: GLTF.MaterialAlphaMode; baseColorFactor: import(&quot;@gltf-transform/core&quot;).vec4; doubleSided: boolean; emissiveFactor: import(&quot;@gltf-transform/core&quot;).vec3; metallicFactor: number; name: string; roughnessFactor: number; }[]; meshes: { name: string; primitives: { triangles: number; vertices: number; attributes: string[]; material: string; mode: GLTF.MeshPrimitiveMode; targets: number; }[]; }[]; scenes: { name: string; nodes: Record&lt;string, unknown&gt;[]; }[]; skins: { joints: number; name: string; }[]; textures: { bytes: number; mimeType: string; name: string; }[]; }</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Structural extraction payload (used by the extract route).</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#mimeFor\">mimeFor(uri)</a> ⇒ <code>string</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Rewrites resource URIs to data URIs so the .gltf is a single self-contained file.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#inlineResources\">inlineResources(json, resources)</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Rewrites resource URIs to data URIs so the .gltf is a single self-contained file.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"ModelService\"></a>\n\n## ModelService\nModel feature service: glTF/GLB inspection, extraction, optimization (DRACO/Meshopt) and conversion.\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/model/model.service.ts:247  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/model/model.service.js:193\n\n* [ModelService](#ModelService)\n    * [.convert(query)](#ModelService+convert) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;&gt;</code>\n    * [.extract()](#ModelService+extract) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;{ animations: { channels: number; name: string; samplers: number; }[]; format: string; materials: { alphaMode: GLTF.MaterialAlphaMode; baseColorFactor: import(&quot;@gltf-transform/core&quot;).vec4; doubleSided: boolean; emissiveFactor: import(&quot;@gltf-transform/core&quot;).vec3; metallicFactor: number; name: string; roughnessFactor: number; }[]; meshes: { name: string; primitives: { triangles: number; vertices: number; attributes: string[]; material: string; mode: GLTF.MeshPrimitiveMode; targets: number; }[]; }[]; scenes: { name: string; nodes: Record&lt;string, unknown&gt;[]; }[]; skins: { joints: number; name: string; }[]; textures: { bytes: number; mimeType: string; name: string; }[]; }&gt;</code>\n    * [.metadata()](#ModelService+metadata) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;{ asset: { generator: string; version: string; }; bounds: { max: [number, number, number]; min: [number, number, number]; }; counts: { accessors: number; animations: number; cameras: number; materials: number; meshes: number; nodes: number; primitives: number; scenes: number; skins: number; textures: number; triangles: number; vertices: number; }; extensionsRequired: string[]; extensionsUsed: string[]; format: string; }&gt;</code>\n    * [.optimize(query)](#ModelService+optimize) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;&gt;</code>\n\n<a name=\"ModelService+convert\"></a>\n\n### modelService.convert(query) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;&gt;</code>\nConverts the uploaded GLB between container formats.\n`glb`: binary container (lossless round-trip). `gltf`: self-contained JSON with data URIs.\n\n**Kind**: instance method of [<code>ModelService</code>](#ModelService)  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;&gt;</code> - The converted bytes.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| query | <code>{ to: &quot;glb&quot; \\| &quot;gltf&quot;; }</code> | Target container. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/model/model.service.ts:259  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/model/model.service.js:200\n<a name=\"ModelService+extract\"></a>\n\n### modelService.extract() ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;{ animations: { channels: number; name: string; samplers: number; }[]; format: string; materials: { alphaMode: GLTF.MaterialAlphaMode; baseColorFactor: import(&quot;@gltf-transform/core&quot;).vec4; doubleSided: boolean; emissiveFactor: import(&quot;@gltf-transform/core&quot;).vec3; metallicFactor: number; name: string; roughnessFactor: number; }[]; meshes: { name: string; primitives: { triangles: number; vertices: number; attributes: string[]; material: string; mode: GLTF.MeshPrimitiveMode; targets: number; }[]; }[]; scenes: { name: string; nodes: Record&lt;string, unknown&gt;[]; }[]; skins: { joints: number; name: string; }[]; textures: { bytes: number; mimeType: string; name: string; }[]; }&gt;</code>\nExtracts the scene graph, meshes, materials, textures, animations and skins.\n\n**Kind**: instance method of [<code>ModelService</code>](#ModelService)  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;{ animations: { channels: number; name: string; samplers: number; }[]; format: string; materials: { alphaMode: GLTF.MaterialAlphaMode; baseColorFactor: import(&quot;@gltf-transform/core&quot;).vec4; doubleSided: boolean; emissiveFactor: import(&quot;@gltf-transform/core&quot;).vec3; metallicFactor: number; name: string; roughnessFactor: number; }[]; meshes: { name: string; primitives: { triangles: number; vertices: number; attributes: string[]; material: string; mode: GLTF.MeshPrimitiveMode; targets: number; }[]; }[]; scenes: { name: string; nodes: Record&lt;string, unknown&gt;[]; }[]; skins: { joints: number; name: string; }[]; textures: { bytes: number; mimeType: string; name: string; }[]; }&gt;</code> - The structural extraction of the model.  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/model/model.service.ts:275  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/model/model.service.js:211\n<a name=\"ModelService+metadata\"></a>\n\n### modelService.metadata() ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;{ asset: { generator: string; version: string; }; bounds: { max: [number, number, number]; min: [number, number, number]; }; counts: { accessors: number; animations: number; cameras: number; materials: number; meshes: number; nodes: number; primitives: number; scenes: number; skins: number; textures: number; triangles: number; vertices: number; }; extensionsRequired: string[]; extensionsUsed: string[]; format: string; }&gt;</code>\nNormalized GLB metadata for an uploaded model.\n\n**Kind**: instance method of [<code>ModelService</code>](#ModelService)  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;{ asset: { generator: string; version: string; }; bounds: { max: [number, number, number]; min: [number, number, number]; }; counts: { accessors: number; animations: number; cameras: number; materials: number; meshes: number; nodes: number; primitives: number; scenes: number; skins: number; textures: number; triangles: number; vertices: number; }; extensionsRequired: string[]; extensionsUsed: string[]; format: string; }&gt;</code> - Format, asset descriptor, counts, extensions and bounds.  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/model/model.service.ts:286  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/model/model.service.js:217\n<a name=\"ModelService+optimize\"></a>\n\n### modelService.optimize(query) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;&gt;</code>\nOptimizes the uploaded model in a worker thread and returns GLB bytes.\n\n**Kind**: instance method of [<code>ModelService</code>](#ModelService)  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;&gt;</code> - The optimized GLB bytes.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| query | <code>{ compress: &quot;none&quot; \\| &quot;draco&quot; \\| &quot;meshopt&quot;; weld: boolean; simplify?: number; }</code> | Compression codec, simplification ratio and weld. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/model/model.service.ts:298  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/model/model.service.js:223\n<a name=\"MODE_TRIANGLES\"></a>\n\n## MODE\\_TRIANGLES\nglTF primitive mode constants.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/model/model.service.ts:64  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/model/model.service.js:40\n<a name=\"readBody\"></a>\n\n## readBody(cls) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;&gt;</code>\nOnly the GLB container; .gltf JSON with external resources is out of scope.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;&gt;</code> - The body bytes, capped.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| cls | <code>NormalizedClsService</code> | Normalized request context. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/model/model.service.ts:27  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/model/model.service.js:22\n<a name=\"assertModelSignature\"></a>\n\n## assertModelSignature(buffer) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code>\nSignature must be the GLB magic; closes the renamed-image and JSON-mislabeled holes.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| buffer | <code>Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;</code> | The buffered upload. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/model/model.service.ts:44  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/model/model.service.js:34\n<a name=\"boundsOf\"></a>\n\n## boundsOf(document) ⇒ <code>{ max: [number, number, number]; min: [number, number, number]; }</code>\nAxis-aligned bounding box over every POSITION accessor, or undefined when nothing carries positions.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>{ max: [number, number, number]; min: [number, number, number]; }</code> - The axis-aligned bounds, or undefined when no primitive carries positions.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| document | <code>Document</code> | The parsed GLB document. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/model/model.service.ts:90  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/model/model.service.js:57\n<a name=\"metadataOf\"></a>\n\n## metadataOf(document) ⇒ <code>{ asset: { generator: string; version: string; }; bounds: { max: [number, number, number]; min: [number, number, number]; }; counts: { accessors: number; animations: number; cameras: number; materials: number; meshes: number; nodes: number; primitives: number; scenes: number; skins: number; textures: number; triangles: number; vertices: number; }; extensionsRequired: string[]; extensionsUsed: string[]; format: string; }</code>\nNormalized metadata payload (used by the metadata route).\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>{ asset: { generator: string; version: string; }; bounds: { max: [number, number, number]; min: [number, number, number]; }; counts: { accessors: number; animations: number; cameras: number; materials: number; meshes: number; nodes: number; primitives: number; scenes: number; skins: number; textures: number; triangles: number; vertices: number; }; extensionsRequired: string[]; extensionsUsed: string[]; format: string; }</code> - The normalized metadata payload.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| document | <code>Document</code> | The parsed GLB document. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/model/model.service.ts:123  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/model/model.service.js:83\n<a name=\"extractOf\"></a>\n\n## extractOf(document) ⇒ <code>{ animations: { channels: number; name: string; samplers: number; }[]; format: string; materials: { alphaMode: GLTF.MaterialAlphaMode; baseColorFactor: import(&quot;@gltf-transform/core&quot;).vec4; doubleSided: boolean; emissiveFactor: import(&quot;@gltf-transform/core&quot;).vec3; metallicFactor: number; name: string; roughnessFactor: number; }[]; meshes: { name: string; primitives: { triangles: number; vertices: number; attributes: string[]; material: string; mode: GLTF.MeshPrimitiveMode; targets: number; }[]; }[]; scenes: { name: string; nodes: Record&lt;string, unknown&gt;[]; }[]; skins: { joints: number; name: string; }[]; textures: { bytes: number; mimeType: string; name: string; }[]; }</code>\nStructural extraction payload (used by the extract route).\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>{ animations: { channels: number; name: string; samplers: number; }[]; format: string; materials: { alphaMode: GLTF.MaterialAlphaMode; baseColorFactor: import(&quot;@gltf-transform/core&quot;).vec4; doubleSided: boolean; emissiveFactor: import(&quot;@gltf-transform/core&quot;).vec3; metallicFactor: number; name: string; roughnessFactor: number; }[]; meshes: { name: string; primitives: { triangles: number; vertices: number; attributes: string[]; material: string; mode: GLTF.MeshPrimitiveMode; targets: number; }[]; }[]; scenes: { name: string; nodes: Record&lt;string, unknown&gt;[]; }[]; skins: { joints: number; name: string; }[]; textures: { bytes: number; mimeType: string; name: string; }[]; }</code> - The structural extraction payload.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| document | <code>Document</code> | The parsed GLB document. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/model/model.service.ts:159  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/model/model.service.js:113\n<a name=\"mimeFor\"></a>\n\n## mimeFor(uri) ⇒ <code>string</code>\nRewrites resource URIs to data URIs so the .gltf is a single self-contained file.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>string</code> - The best-known MIME type for the resource.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| uri | <code>string</code> | The resource URI. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/model/model.service.ts:334  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/model/model.service.js:250\n<a name=\"inlineResources\"></a>\n\n## inlineResources(json, resources)\nRewrites resource URIs to data URIs so the .gltf is a single self-contained file.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| json | <code>GLTF.IGLTF</code> | The glTF JSON document to rewrite in place. |\n| resources | <code>{ [s: string]: Uint8Array&lt;ArrayBuffer&gt;; }</code> | The resource map from writeJSON. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/model/model.service.ts:350  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/model/model.service.js:267\n","symbols":13,"lastUsed":1795730468310},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/model/schema.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"compress","longname":"compress","name":"compress","kind":"member","scope":"global","description":"Compression codec for mesh data; `none` keeps uncompressed accessors.","meta":{"lineno":19},"order":3,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/model/schema.js:7","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/model/schema.ts:23"},"level":0},{"id":"simplify","longname":"simplify","name":"simplify","kind":"member","scope":"global","description":"Lossy simplification ratio in [0, 1]; 1 (default) disables it. Values < 1 force weld on.","meta":{"lineno":23},"order":4,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/model/schema.js:8","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/model/schema.ts:27"},"level":0},{"id":"weld","longname":"weld","name":"weld","kind":"member","scope":"global","description":"Weld bitwise-identical vertices (forced on when simplify < 1); default on.","meta":{"lineno":31},"order":5,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/model/schema.js:13","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/model/schema.ts:35"},"level":0},{"id":"to","longname":"to","name":"to","kind":"member","scope":"global","description":"`glb`: binary container. `gltf`: self-contained JSON container with data URIs.","meta":{"lineno":42},"order":7,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/model/schema.js:18","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/model/schema.ts:51"},"level":0},