utes. `/pdf/build` consumes JSON and bypasses the media\ninterceptors by design (JSON bodies are never virus-scanned or signature-probed);\n`/pdf/extract` and `/pdf/metadata` take the binary upload and are ClamAV-scanned.\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/pdf/pdf.controller.ts:28  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/pdf/pdf.controller.js:21\n\n* [PdfController](#PdfController)\n    * [.build(response, body)](#PdfController+build) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code>\n    * [.extract(_query)](#PdfController+extract) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;{ format: string; metadata: { author: string; creationDate: string; creator: string; keywords: string; modificationDate: string; producer: string; subject: string; title: string; }; pageCount: number; structure: { pages: { page: number; text: string; }[]; }; text: string; }&gt;</code>\n    * [.metadata(_query)](#PdfController+metadata) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;{ author: string; creationDate: string; creator: string; encrypted: boolean; keywords: string; modificationDate: string; orientation: &quot;portrait&quot; \\| &quot;landscape&quot;; pageCount: number; pageSize: { height: number; width: number; }; producer: string; subject: string; title: string; format: string; }&gt;</code>\n\n<a name=\"PdfController+build\"></a>\n\n### pdfController.build(response, body) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code>\nBuilds a PDF from the JSON payload (201).\n\n**Kind**: instance method of [<code>PdfController</code>](#PdfController)  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code> - The document bytes (201).  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| response | <code>FastifyReply&lt;import(&quot;fastify&quot;).RouteGenericInterface, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).RawServerDefault, import(&quot;http&quot;).IncomingMessage, import(&quot;http&quot;).ServerResponse&lt;import(&quot;http&quot;).IncomingMessage&gt;, unknown, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).FastifySchema, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).FastifyTypeProviderDefault, unknown&gt;</code> | Raw reply, streamed as application/pdf. |\n| body | <code>{ pages: { elements: ({ [x: string]: any; text: string; type: &quot;text&quot;; x: number; y: number; align?: &quot;left&quot; \\| &quot;center&quot; \\| &quot;right&quot;; font?: string; size?: number; w?: number; } \\| { [x: string]: any; h: number; type: &quot;rect&quot;; w: number; x: number; y: number; dash?: boolean; strokeWidth?: number; } \\| { [x: string]: any; h: number; type: &quot;ellipse&quot;; w: number; x: number; y: number; strokeWidth?: number; } \\| { [x: string]: any; type: &quot;line&quot;; x1: number; x2: number; y1: number; y2: number; dash?: boolean; thickness?: number; } \\| { data: string; h: number; imageType: &quot;png&quot; \\| &quot;jpg&quot;; type: &quot;image&quot;; w: number; x: number; y: number; opacity?: number; } \\| { rows: (string \\| { [x: string]: any; text: string; align?: &quot;left&quot; \\| &quot;center&quot; \\| &quot;right&quot;; colSpan?: number; size?: number; })[][]; type: &quot;table&quot;; w: number; x: number; y: number; colWidths?: number[]; header?: boolean; } \\| { [x: string]: any; fieldType: &quot;text&quot; \\| &quot;checkbox&quot;; type: &quot;field&quot;; x: number; y: number; h?: number; value?: string; w?: number; } \\| { [x: string]: any; format: string; type: &quot;pageNumber&quot;; x: number; y: number; font?: string; size?: number; } \\| { type: &quot;pageBreak&quot;; })[]; margin: { bottom: number; left: number; right: number; top: number; }; orientation: &quot;portrait&quot; \\| &quot;landscape&quot;; size: &quot;a4&quot; \\| &quot;a3&quot; \\| &quot;a5&quot; \\| &quot;letter&quot; \\| &quot;legal&quot; \\| &quot;tabloid&quot;; }[]; embeddedFonts?: { [x: string]: any; data: string; }[]; metadata?: { author?: string; creationDate?: string; creator?: string; keywords?: string \\| string[]; language?: string; subject?: string; title?: string; }; }</code> | Pages, elements, embedded fonts and metadata. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/pdf/pdf.controller.ts:41  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/pdf/pdf.controller.js:28\n<a name=\"PdfController+extract\"></a>\n\n### pdfController.extract(_query) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;{ format: string; metadata: { author: string; creationDate: string; creator: string; keywords: string; modificationDate: string; producer: string; subject: string; title: string; }; pageCount: number; structure: { pages: { page: number; text: string; }[]; }; text: string; }&gt;</code>\nExtracts text page by page (201).\n\n**Kind**: instance method of [<code>PdfController</code>](#PdfController)  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;{ format: string; metadata: { author: string; creationDate: string; creator: string; keywords: string; modificationDate: string; producer: string; subject: string; title: string; }; pageCount: number; structure: { pages: { page: number; text: string; }[]; }; text: string; }&gt;</code> - The extracted metadata, page count and per-page text.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| _query | <code>unknown</code> | Empty query object; junk parameters are rejected with 400. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/pdf/pdf.controller.ts:60  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/pdf/pdf.controller.js:34\n<a name=\"PdfController+metadata\"></a>\n\n### pdfController.metadata(_query) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;{ author: string; creationDate: string; creator: string; encrypted: boolean; keywords: string; modificationDate: string; orientation: &quot;portrait&quot; \\| &quot;landscape&quot;; pageCount: number; pageSize: { height: number; width: number; }; producer: string; subject: string; title: string; format: string; }&gt;</code>\nNormalized PDF metadata (201).\n\n**Kind**: instance method of [<code>PdfController</code>](#PdfController)  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;{ author: string; creationDate: string; creator: string; encrypted: boolean; keywords: string; modificationDate: string; orientation: &quot;portrait&quot; \\| &quot;landscape&quot;; pageCount: number; pageSize: { height: number; width: number; }; producer: string; subject: string; title: string; format: string; }&gt;</code> - The metadata document.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| _query | <code>unknown</code> | Empty query object; junk parameters are rejected with 400. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/pdf/pdf.controller.ts:73  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/pdf/pdf.controller.js:37\n","symbols":4,"lastUsed":1795730468562},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/pdf/pdf.module.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"PdfModule","longname":"PdfModule","name":"PdfModule","kind":"member","scope":"global","description":"PDF feature module: build, extract and metadata routes.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":41},"order":0,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/pdf/pdf.module.js:10","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/pdf/pdf.module.ts:13"},"level":0}],"fp":"9cd4a3a191c36bf13b4516367703e083db4986199c843240294b5e05b6b9a384","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730468593,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/resources/pdf/pdf.module.ts":{"fp":"6c1730e4f2f3e7b68ed500c6b1edcfdd7c4155596ff1d6efa9e6577fe767e1c9","issues":[],"kind":"md","markdown":"<a name=\"PdfModule\"></a>\n\n## PdfModule\nPDF feature module: build, extract and metadata routes.\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/pdf/pdf.module.ts:13  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/pdf/pdf.module.js:10\n","symbols":1,"lastUsed":1795730468662},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/pdf/pdf.service.spec.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"unparseablePdf","longname":"unparseablePdf","name":"unparseablePdf","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Passes the signature gate (%PDF magic) but pdf-lib cannot parse it at all.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":249},"order":1,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/backend/src/resources/pdf/pdf.service.spec.ts:293"},"level":0},{"id":"handCraftedPdf","longname":"handCraftedPdf","name":"handCraftedPdf","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Hand-crafts a minimal PDF with an optional /Info dict; usable where pdf-lib cannot (or chooses not to) emit one.","params":[{"description":"The raw object body for the /Info dict (e.g. an empty-string CreationDate), or undefined for no /Info at all.","name":"infoObject","type":{"names":["string"]}},{"description":"The raw contents of the /Kids array of the pages object (e.g. `'3 0 R'`, or `''` for zero pages).","name":"kids","type":{"names":["string"]}},{"description":"The /Count value written into the pages object.","name":"pageCount","type":{"names":["number"]}},{"description":"The raw MediaBox array for the single page object.","name":"mediaBox","defaultvalue":"[0 0 200 200]","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The raw bytes of the hand-crafted PDF.","type":{"names":["Buffer<ArrayBufferLike>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":223},"order":0,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/backend/src/resources/pdf/pdf.service.spec.ts:262"},"level":0}],"fp":"087034a8f5ac65e1aae8609bd1285c3f98dc9a4475781137137f15189a81634a","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730468593,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/resources/pdf/pdf.service.spec.ts":{"fp":"bd823af73ee96f1f622606acac552c0e6f3ed5ad02b9586f15931325cd110324","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","markdown":"## Constants\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#unparseablePdf\">unparseablePdf</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Passes the signature gate (%PDF magic) but pdf-lib cannot parse it at all.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n## Functions\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#handCraftedPdf\">handCraftedPdf(infoObject, kids, pageCount, mediaBox)</a> ⇒ <code>Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Hand-crafts a minimal PDF with an optional /Info dict; usable where pdf-lib cannot (or chooses not to) emit one.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"unparseablePdf\"></a>\n\n## unparseablePdf\nPasses the signature gate (%PDF magic) but pdf-lib cannot parse it at all.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/pdf/pdf.service.spec.ts:293  \n<a name=\"handCraftedPdf\"></a>\n\n## handCraftedPdf(infoObject, kids, pageCount, mediaBox) ⇒ <code>Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;</code>\nHand-crafts a minimal PDF with an optional /Info dict; usable where pdf-lib cannot (or chooses not to) emit one.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;</code> - The raw bytes of the hand-crafted PDF.  \n\n| Param | Type | Default | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| infoObject | <code>string</code> |  | The raw object body for the /Info dict (e.g. an empty-string CreationDate), or undefined for no /Info at all. |\n| kids | <code>string</code> |  | The raw contents of the /Kids array of the pages object (e.g. `'3 0 R'`, or `''` for zero pages). |\n| pageCount | <code>number</code> |  | The /Count value written into the pages object. |\n| mediaBox | <code>string</code> | <code>&quot;[0 0 200 200]&quot;</code> | The raw MediaBox array for the single page object. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/pdf/pdf.service.spec.ts:262  \n","symbols":2,"lastUsed":1795730468636},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/pdf/pdf.service.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"PdfService","longname":"PdfService","name":"PdfService","kind":"member","scope":"global","description":"PDF feature service: builds documents, extracts text and reads metadata.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":128},"order":4,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/pdf/pdf.service.js:81","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/pdf/pdf.service.ts:105"},"level":0},{"id":"MAX_EXTRACT_PAGES","longname":"MAX_EXTRACT_PAGES","name":"MAX_EXTRACT_PAGES","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Ceiling on extracted pages; plenty for legitimate decks, stops crafted fan-outs.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":114},"order":2,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/pdf/pdf.service.js:75","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/pdf/pdf.service.ts:89"},"leve