ture service: streams uploads through workers for processing, metadata, DNA fingerprinting, stats and screenshots.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n## Functions\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#requireInputFormat\">requireInputFormat(cls)</a> ⇒ <code>string</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Resolves the upload&#39;s detected signature to an FFmpeg demuxer format,\nthrowing the route&#39;s 415 when the signature is missing or unsupported.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"VideoService\"></a>\n\n## VideoService\nVideo feature service: streams uploads through workers for processing, metadata, DNA fingerprinting, stats and screenshots.\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/video/video.service.ts:34  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/video/video.service.js:24\n<a name=\"VideoService+audio\"></a>\n\n### videoService.audio(options) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;Readable&gt;</code>\nExtracts the audio stream from a video upload.\n\n**Kind**: instance method of [<code>VideoService</code>](#VideoService)  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;Readable&gt;</code> - A readable stream of the encoded audio.  \n**Throws**:\n\n- UnsupportedMediaTypeException when the upload has no video signature or demuxer mapping.\n\n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| options | <code>{ payload: VideoAudioType; }</code> | Audio extraction options. |\n| options.payload |  | Validated query options for the audio route. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/video/video.service.ts:48  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/video/video.service.js:33\n<a name=\"requireInputFormat\"></a>\n\n## requireInputFormat(cls) ⇒ <code>string</code>\nResolves the upload's detected signature to an FFmpeg demuxer format,\nthrowing the route's 415 when the signature is missing or unsupported.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>string</code> - The resolved demuxer format name.  \n**Throws**:\n\n- <code>UnsupportedMediaTypeException</code> When the signature has no demuxer mapping.\n\n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| cls | <code>NormalizedClsService</code> | Normalized request context carrying the file signature. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/video/video.service.ts:24  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/video/video.service.js:18\n","symbols":3,"lastUsed":1795730469476},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/codecs.spec.ts":{"doclets":[],"fp":"0f450ee15e4c25b6b30800c9cfef62403cfb81c960ece79e016c5fac7ee0cbdd","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730469428,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/codecs.spec.ts":{"fp":"c908367b5074a091add5592d577076971b26d843194f08e2ffd2a78bcd127a70","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","skipped":"no-jsdoc","symbols":0,"lastUsed":1795730469431},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/codecs.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"parseBitrate","longname":"parseBitrate","name":"parseBitrate","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Parses a video bitrate literal (`1200k`, `5M`) into bits per second.","params":[{"description":"The bitrate literal from the query (e.g. '2500k').","name":"value","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The bitrate in bits per second, defaulting to 2 000 000 when unparsable.","type":{"names":["number"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":7},"order":0,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/video/worker/codecs.js:2","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/codecs.ts:14"},"level":0},{"id":"videoEncoderConstant","longname":"videoEncoderConstant","name":"videoEncoderConstant","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Maps the public codec name to the node-av FFmpeg encoder constant.","params":[{"description":"The codec from the query (`vp9` | `av1` | `x264`-family).","name":"codec"}],"returns":[{"description":"The FFmpeg encoder constant for passing to the output stream.","type":{"names":["import(\"node-av\").FFVideoEncoder<\"libvpx-vp9\"> | import(\"node-av\").FFVideoEncoder<\"libaom-av1\"> | import(\"node-av\").FFVideoEncoder<\"libx264\">"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":20},"order":1,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/video/worker/codecs.js:10","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/codecs.ts:27"},"level":0}],"fp":"78451ce49411fef9d16bb571aad04eb9f00a3960583299192dc7aa615b14512d","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730469433,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/codecs.ts":{"fp":"d13932cf32adf6e6edee71dbca6356e0ed15270365ffcef08173e52f01c69627","issues":[],"kind":"md","markdown":"## Functions\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#parseBitrate\">parseBitrate(value)</a> ⇒ <code>number</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Parses a video bitrate literal (<code>1200k</code>, <code>5M</code>) into bits per second.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#videoEncoderConstant\">videoEncoderConstant(codec)</a> ⇒ <code>import(&quot;node-av&quot;).FFVideoEncoder&lt;&quot;libvpx-vp9&quot;&gt; | import(&quot;node-av&quot;).FFVideoEncoder&lt;&quot;libaom-av1&quot;&gt; | import(&quot;node-av&quot;).FFVideoEncoder&lt;&quot;libx264&quot;&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Maps the public codec name to the node-av FFmpeg encoder constant.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"parseBitrate\"></a>\n\n## parseBitrate(value) ⇒ <code>number</code>\nParses a video bitrate literal (`1200k`, `5M`) into bits per second.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>number</code> - The bitrate in bits per second, defaulting to 2 000 000 when unparsable.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| value | <code>string</code> | The bitrate literal from the query (e.g. '2500k'). |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/codecs.ts:14  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/video/worker/codecs.js:2\n<a name=\"videoEncoderConstant\"></a>\n\n## videoEncoderConstant(codec) ⇒ <code>import(&quot;node-av&quot;).FFVideoEncoder&lt;&quot;libvpx-vp9&quot;&gt; \\| import(&quot;node-av&quot;).FFVideoEncoder&lt;&quot;libaom-av1&quot;&gt; \\| import(&quot;node-av&quot;).FFVideoEncoder&lt;&quot;libx264&quot;&gt;</code>\nMaps the public codec name to the node-av FFmpeg encoder constant.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>import(&quot;node-av&quot;).FFVideoEncoder&lt;&quot;libvpx-vp9&quot;&gt; \\| import(&quot;node-av&quot;).FFVideoEncoder&lt;&quot;libaom-av1&quot;&gt; \\| import(&quot;node-av&quot;).FFVideoEncoder&lt;&quot;libx264&quot;&gt;</code> - The FFmpeg encoder constant for passing to the output stream.  \n\n| Param | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| codec | The codec from the query (`vp9` | `av1` | `x264`-family). |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/codecs.ts:27  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/video/worker/codecs.js:10\n","symbols":2,"lastUsed":1795730469517},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/dna.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"dna","longname":"dna","name":"dna","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Computes a sequence of PDQ perceptual hashes for the video on stdin,\nsampled at 2 fps and normalized to 512px-wide RGB frames.\n\nThe decoder runs to EOF so stdin is usually fully consumed, but the\nremainder is still drained in the `finally` block: on early failure\n(e.g. no video stream) the unread HTTP upload must be discarded or\nthe client stalls mid-send.","returns":[{"description":"Resolves after the DNA JSON line is written to stdout.","type":{"names":["Promise<void>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":70},"order":0,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/video/worker/dna.js:60","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/dna.ts:23"},"level":0}],"fp":"bd2eb68c8f5fc58fa594ccba89b1990c50e89af106d7113c48c742e0b1a9b565","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730469476,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/dna.ts":{"fp":"99ba7666abfc9a57f7ea63a162d505079973b72311bfdef0d95d5449e9fb1fa0","issues":[],"kind":"md","markdown":"<a name=\"dna\"></a>\n\n## dna() ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code>\nComputes a sequence of PDQ perceptual hashes for the video on stdin,\nsampled at 2 fps and normalized to 512px-wide RGB frames.\n\nThe decoder runs to EOF so stdin is usually fully consumed, but the\nremainder is still drained in the `finally` block: on early failure\n(e.g. no video stream) the unread HTTP upload must be discarded or\nthe client stalls mid-send.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code> - Resolves after the DNA JSON line is written to stdout.  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/dna.ts:23  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/video/worker/dna.js:60\n","symbols":1,"lastUsed":1795730469543},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/filters.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"buildAudioFilters","longname":"buildAudioFilters","name":"buildAudioFilters","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Builds the audio filter chain for a transcode (channel mix, resample, loudnorm).","params":[{"description":"The validated video processor options.","name":"payload"}],"returns":[{"description":"The filters to apply on the audio stream, in order.","type":{"names":["FilterAPI[]"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":7},"order":0,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/video/worker/filters.js:2","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/filters.ts:10"},"level":0},{"id":"buildVideoFilters","longname":"buildVideoFilters","name":"buildVideoFilters","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Builds the video filter chain (trim, deinterlace, scale, fps, denoise, ...).","params":[{"description":"The validated video processor options.","name":"payload"}],"returns":[{"description":"The filters to apply on the video stream, in order.","type":{"names":["FilterAPI[]"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":22},"order":1,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/video/worker/filters.js:12","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/filters.ts:23"},"level":0}],"fp":"1ecff988f9ce6b36b1f9a636cc16566922a5f4d4aaab04208f9b29afdd6c5917","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730469521,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/filters.ts":{"fp":"d2940365ac68cbc896a05893bffb79829f92e58f48bf392b2ae67bf02a47d0b6","issues":[],"kind":"md","markdown":"## Functions\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#buildAudioFilters\">buildAudioFilters(payload)</a> ⇒ <code>FilterAPI[]</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Builds the audio filter chain for a transcode (channel mix, resample, loudnorm).</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#buildVideoFilters\">buildVideoFilters(payload)</a> ⇒ <code>FilterAPI[]</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Builds the video filter chain (trim, deinterlace, scale, fps, denoise, ...).</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"buildAudioFilters\"></a>\n\n## buildAudioFilters(payload) ⇒ <code>FilterAPI[]</code>\nBuilds the audio filter chain for a transcode (channel mix, resample, loudnorm).\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>FilterAPI[]</code> - The filters to apply on the audio stream, in order.  \n\n| Param | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| payload | The validated video processor options. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/filters.ts:10  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/video/worker/filters.js:2\n<a name=\"buildVideoFilters\"></a>\n\n## buildVideoFilters(payload) ⇒ <code>FilterAPI[]</code>\nBuilds the video filter chain (trim, deinterlace, scale, fps, denoise, ...).\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>FilterAPI[]</code> - The filters to apply on the video stream, in order.  \n\n| Param | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| payload | The validated video processor options. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/filters.ts:23  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/video/worker/filters.js:12\n","symbols":2,"lastUsed":1795730469578},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/filters.spec.ts":{"doclets":[],"fp":"740bd3a6c0ff8d2f9d2b3ff1b20cef5e7d1db93a51791c1c475954144d637c15","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730469480,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/