ead, finishes the process.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"run\"></a>\n\n## run() ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code>\nDispatches the requested video operation (processor/audio/metadata/dna/stats/screenshot).\n\n**Kind**: global function  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/index.ts:20  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/video/worker/index.js:11\n<a name=\"startVideoWorker\"></a>\n\n## startVideoWorker() ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code>\nRuns the worker job and, only inside a spawned worker thread, finishes the process.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code> - The job (with exit-code handling attached when running as a worker thread).  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/index.ts:54  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/video/worker/index.js:40\n","symbols":2,"lastUsed":1795730469621},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/inspect.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"metadata","longname":"metadata","name":"metadata","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Opens the video input with node-av and writes its container/stream metadata (including dimensions) as JSON to stdout.","meta":{"lineno":8},"order":0,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/video/worker/inspect.js:5","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/inspect.ts:13"},"returns":[{"type":{"names":["Promise<void>"]}}],"level":0},{"id":"stats","longname":"stats","name":"stats","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Opens the video input with node-av and writes its stream statistics (bitrate, dimensions, codec) as JSON to stdout.","meta":{"lineno":35},"order":1,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/video/worker/inspect.js:28","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/inspect.ts:42"},"returns":[{"type":{"names":["Promise<void>"]}}],"level":0}],"fp":"f31929f0552f2282c9c355925cc1493b75ed5ee6042bb07d633228269a877773","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730469551,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/inspect.ts":{"fp":"aae73a9745dbdd90e18d426c43505300b2ffed1188f866a3f1d067716cc8d32f","issues":[],"kind":"md","markdown":"## Functions\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#metadata\">metadata()</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Opens the video input with node-av and writes its container/stream metadata (including dimensions) as JSON to stdout.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#stats\">stats()</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Opens the video input with node-av and writes its stream statistics (bitrate, dimensions, codec) as JSON to stdout.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"metadata\"></a>\n\n## metadata() ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code>\nOpens the video input with node-av and writes its container/stream metadata (including dimensions) as JSON to stdout.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/inspect.ts:13  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/video/worker/inspect.js:5\n<a name=\"stats\"></a>\n\n## stats() ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code>\nOpens the video input with node-av and writes its stream statistics (bitrate, dimensions, codec) as JSON to stdout.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/inspect.ts:42  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/video/worker/inspect.js:28\n","symbols":2,"lastUsed":1795730469658},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/screenshot.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"firstJpeg","longname":"firstJpeg","name":"firstJpeg","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Returns the first usable frame of a decoded video as JPEG.","params":[{"description":"Decoder bound to the video stream.","name":"decoder","type":{"names":["Decoder"]}},{"description":"Demuxer supplying the packets to decode.","name":"input","type":{"names":["Demuxer"]}},{"description":"Scaler used to convert the frame to JPEG.","name":"scaler","type":{"names":["Scaler"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The first decoded frame as JPEG, or undefined when none decoded.","type":{"names":["Promise<Buffer<ArrayBufferLike>>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":72},"async":true,"order":0,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/video/worker/screenshot.js:65","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/screenshot.ts:27"},"level":0},{"id":"screenshot","longname":"screenshot","name":"screenshot","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Extracts one JPEG frame per requested timestamp as a multipart/mixed stream.","params":[{"description":"Requested timestamps in seconds (sorted, deduplicated).","name":"frames","type":{"names":["number[]"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":83},"order":1,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/video/worker/screenshot.js:72","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/screenshot.ts:42"},"returns":[{"type":{"names":["Promise<void>"]}}],"level":0}],"fp":"60fe4df03aa8f29a49a13acbdc8f24e045bf471ec866bb9ec90a41a512ce8bb4","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730469678,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/screenshot.ts":{"fp":"c27e059a2bc55e88f49d5aa4c4ddf656b8a70b8f52c8a5caa1a1b89d15d94659","issues":[],"kind":"md","markdown":"## Functions\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#firstJpeg\">firstJpeg(decoder, input, scaler)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Returns the first usable frame of a decoded video as JPEG.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#screenshot\">screenshot(frames)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Extracts one JPEG frame per requested timestamp as a multipart/mixed stream.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"firstJpeg\"></a>\n\n## firstJpeg(decoder, input, scaler) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;&gt;</code>\nReturns the first usable frame of a decoded video as JPEG.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;&gt;</code> - The first decoded frame as JPEG, or undefined when none decoded.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| decoder | <code>Decoder</code> | Decoder bound to the video stream. |\n| input | <code>Demuxer</code> | Demuxer supplying the packets to decode. |\n| scaler | <code>Scaler</code> | Scaler used to convert the frame to JPEG. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/screenshot.ts:27  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/video/worker/screenshot.js:65\n<a name=\"screenshot\"></a>\n\n## screenshot(frames) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code>\nExtracts one JPEG frame per requested timestamp as a multipart/mixed stream.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| frames | <code>number[]</code> | Requested timestamps in seconds (sorted, deduplicated). |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/screenshot.ts:42  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/video/worker/screenshot.js:72\n","symbols":2,"lastUsed":1795730469782},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/processor.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"processMedia","longname":"processMedia","name":"processMedia","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Transcodes the upload stdin into the requested format/codec and streams it out.","params":[{"description":"The validated video processor options (format, codec, bitrate, filters...).","name":"payload"}],"meta":{"lineno":67},"order":0,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/video/worker/processor.js:62","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/processor.ts:33"},"returns":[{"type":{"names":["Promise<void>"]}}],"level":0},{"id":"hasAudioTranscoding","longname":"hasAudioTranscoding","name":"hasAudioTranscoding","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Whether any audio-side option forces a transcode of the audio stream.","params":[{"description":"The validated video processor options.","name":"payload"}],"returns":[{"description":"True when the audio stream must be re-encoded.","type":{"names":["boolean"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":185},"order":1,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/video/worker/processor.js:165","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/processor.ts:150"},"level":0},{"id":"hasVideoTranscoding","longname":"hasVideoTranscoding","name":"hasVideoTranscoding","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Whether any video-side option forces a transcode of the video stream.","params":[{"description":"The validated video processor options.","name":"payload"}],"returns":[{"description":"True when the video stream must be re-encoded.","type":{"names":["boolean"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":193},"order":2,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/video/worker/processor.js:168","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/processor.ts:159"},"level":0}],"fp":"ee2278c656c1fb14e9114aab8ee488aedc6d0c79ba2c4df4254c13ef922fa4b3","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730469621,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/processor.ts":{"fp":"efbeaf69f1b6f3a6e96749ec324b6f8e83bcecdff345b6f51cc64c275673c3a4","issues":[],"kind":"md","markdown":"## Functions\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#processMedia\">processMedia(payload)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Transcodes the upload stdin into the requested format/codec and streams it out.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#hasAudioTranscoding\">hasAudioTranscoding(payload)</a> ⇒ <code>boolean</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Whether any audio-side option forces a transcode of the audio stream.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#hasVideoTranscoding\">hasVideoTranscoding(payload)</a> ⇒ <code>boolean</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Whether any video-side option forces a transcode of the video stream.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"processMedia\"></a>\n\n## processMedia(payload) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code>\nTranscodes the upload stdin into the requested format/codec and streams it out.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n\n| Param | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| payload | The validated video processor options (format, codec, bitrate, filters...). |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/processor.ts:33  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/video/worker/processor.js:62\n<a name=\"hasAudioTranscoding\"></a>\n\n## hasAudioTranscoding(payload) ⇒ <code>boolean</code>\nWhether any audio-side option forces a transcode of the audio stream.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>boolean</code> - True when the audio stream must be re-encoded.  \n\n| Param | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| payload | The validated video processor options. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/processor.ts:150  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/video/worker/processor.js:165\n<a name=\"hasVideoTranscoding\"></a>\n\n## hasVideoTranscoding(payload) ⇒ <code>boolean</code>\nWhether any video-side option forces a transcode of the video stream.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>boolean</code> - True when the video stream must be re-encoded.  \n\n| Param | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| payload | The validated video processor options. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/processor.ts:159  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/video/worker/processor.js:168\n","symbols":3,"lastUsed":1795730469713},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/worker.spec.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"stubStdin","longname":"stubStdin","name":"stubStdin","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Replaces process.stdin with a replay of the fixture.","params":[{"description":"Bytes to replay (defaults to the tiny video fixture).","name":"bytes","type":{"names":["Buffer<ArrayBufferLike>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":16},"order":0,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/worker.spec.ts:21"},"level":0},{"id":"stubStdout","longname":"stubStdout","name":"stubStdout","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Replaces process.stdout with a sink; returns the collected chunks.","params":[],"returns":[{"description":"The collected stdout chunks.","type":{"names":["Buffer<ArrayBufferLike>[]"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":23},"order":1,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/worker.spec.ts:29"},"level":0},{"id":"importWorker","longname":"importWorker","name":"importWorker","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Imports the worker module fresh with the given workerData.","params":[{"description":"The worker payload (operation + inputFormat).","name":"workerData","type":{"names":["Record<string, unknown>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":41},"async":true,"order":2,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/worker.spec.ts:50"},"returns":[{"type":{"names":["Promise<void>"]}}],"level":0},{"id":"runProcessor","longname":"runProcessor","name":"runProcessor","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Runs the processor worker with the given payload and collects its output.","params":[{"description":"Video processor options passed to the worker.","name":"payload","type":{"names":["Record<string, unknown>"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The bytes written to stdout by the worker.","type":{"names":["Promise<Buffer<ArrayBuffer>>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":51},"async":true,"order":3,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/worker.spec.ts:61"},"level":0}],"fp":"8b4b58f9983c05c110a3b05a9f7a1fe265a24dc45fa10ccb7f69d1bc4ee3be63","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730469681,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/worker.spec.ts":{"fp":"fb5e39ae1faeb00df85522605a99aab063ec13a4f60202fa79b0e6121c52658c","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","markdown":"## Functions\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#stubStdin\">stubStdin(bytes)</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Replaces process.stdin with a replay of the fixture.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#stubStdout\">stubStdout()</a> ⇒ <code>Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;[]</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Replaces process.stdout with a sink; returns the collected chunks.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#importWorker\">importWorker(workerData)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Imports the worker module fresh with the given workerData.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#runProcessor\">runProcessor(payload)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;Buffer&lt;ArrayBuffer&gt;&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Runs the processor worker with the given payload and collects its output.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"stubStdin\"></a>\n\n## stubStdin(bytes)\nReplaces process.stdin with a replay of the fixture.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| bytes | <code>Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;</code> | Bytes to replay (defaults to the tiny video fixture). |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/worker.spec.ts:21  \n<a name=\"stubStdout\"></a>\n\n## stubStdout() ⇒ <code>Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;[]</code>\nReplaces process.stdout with a sink; returns the collected chunks.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;[]</code> - The collected stdout chunks.  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/worker.spec.ts:29  \n<a name=\"importWorker\"></a>\n\n## importWorker(workerData) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code>\nImports the worker module fresh with the given workerData.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| workerData | <code>Record&lt;string, unknown&gt;</code> | The worker payload (operation + inputFormat). |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/worker.spec.ts:50  \n<a name=\"runProcessor\"></a>\n\n## runProcessor(payload) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;Buffer&lt;ArrayBuffer&gt;&gt;</code>\nRuns the processor worker with the given payload and collects its output.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;Buffer&lt;ArrayBuffer&gt;&gt;</code> - The bytes written to stdout by the worker.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| payload | <code>Record&lt;string, unknown&gt;</code> | Video processor options passed to the worker. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/video/worker/worker.spec.ts:61  \n","symbols":4,"lastUsed":1795730469741},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/schema.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"autofilter","longname":"autofilter","name":"autofilter","kind":"member","scope":"global","description":"Auto filter range, e.g. A1:C10.","meta":{"lineno":54},"order":2,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/xlsx/schema.js:39","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/schema.ts:65"},"level":0},{"id":"cellDates","longname":"cellDates","name":"cellDates","kind":"member","scope":"global","description":"Write Date cells (type `d`) instead of numeric serials when true.","meta":{"lineno":58},"order":3,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/xlsx/schema.js:40","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/schema.ts:69"},"level":0},{"id":"cols","longname":"cols","name":"cols","kind":"member","scope":"global","description":"Column properties written to `!cols` (width wpx/wch, hidden, outline level).","meta":{"lineno":62},"order":4,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/xlsx/schema.js:41","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/schema.ts:73"},"level":0},{"id":"columns","longname":"columns","name":"columns","kind":"member","scope":"global","description":"Object rows only: lock the column order (default: first-appearance order).","meta":{"lineno":66},"order":5,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/xlsx/schema.js:42","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/schema.ts:77"},"level":0},{"id":"merges","longname":"merges","name":"merges","kind":"member","scope":"global","description":"Merge ranges, e.g. A1:C2.","meta":{"lineno":70},"order":6,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/xlsx/schema.js:43","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/schema.ts:81"},"level":0},{"id":"name","longname":"name","name":"name","kind":"member","scope":"global","description":"Sheet name (1-31 chars, Excel charset); duplicates auto-uniquify. `date1904` workbooks are refused on write (SheetJS serializes 1904-flagged Date cells with the 1900 epoch).","meta":{"lineno":74},"order":7,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/xlsx/schema.js:44","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/schema.ts:85"},"level":0},{"id":"rows","longname":"rows","name":"rows","kind":"member","scope":"global","description":"Rows: objects map keys to cells; arrays emit positional cells. At least one row.","meta":{"lineno":83},"order":8,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/xlsx/schema.js:49","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/schema.ts:96"},"level":0},{"id":"sheetVisibility","longname":"sheetVisibility","name":"sheetVisibility","kind":"member","scope":"global","description":"0 visible, 1 hidden, 2 very hidden.","meta":{"lineno":87},"order":9,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/xlsx/schema.js:50","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/schema.ts:100"},"level":0},{"id":"Names","longname":"Names","name":"Names","kind":"member","scope":"global","description":"Workbook-global defined names (`x` in expressions, scoped via `Sheet`).","meta":{"lineno":130},"order":11,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/xlsx/schema.js:87","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/schema.ts:151"},"level":0},{"id":"header","longname":"header","name":"header","kind":"member","scope":"global","description":"1 = AOA rows, `A` = column-letter keys, or comma-separated custom headers.","meta":{"lineno":148},"order":13,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/xlsx/schema.js:98","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/schema.ts:174"},"level":0},{"id":"maxCells","longname":"maxCells","name":"maxCells","kind":"member","scope":"global","description":"Reject packages whose worksheets carry more cells than this; bounds parse cost.","meta":{"lineno":152},"order":14,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/xlsx/schema.js:99","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/schema.ts:178"},"level":0},{"id":"sheet","longname":"sheet","name":"sheet","kind":"member","scope":"global","description":"Sheet name or 0-based index.","meta":{"lineno":157},"order":15,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/xlsx/schema.js:101","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/schema.ts:183"},"level":0},{"id":"maxCells","longname":"maxCells","name":"maxCells","kind":"member","scope":"global","description":"Reject archives whose cells exceed this count (checked before SheetJS parses).","meta":{"lineno":167},"order":17,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/xlsx/schema.js:105","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/schema.ts:198"},"level":0},{"id":"SPREADSHEET_MIME","longname":"SPREADSHEET_MIME","name":"SPREADSHEET_MIME","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Only the plain OOXML spreadsheet mime; templates, macros and other packages are rejected.","meta":{"lineno":6},"order":0,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/xlsx/schema.js:3","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/schema.ts:8"},"level":0},{"id":"cellSchema","longname":"cellSchema","name":"cellSchema","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"One cell in a build payload: primitive or a SheetJS `CellObject`.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":17},"order":1,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/xlsx/schema.js:9","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/schema.ts:23"},"level":0},{"id":"XlsxBuildSchema","longname":"XlsxBuildSchema","name":"XlsxBuildSchema","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Body of `POST /xlsx/build`.","meta":{"lineno":122},"order":10,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/xlsx/schema.js:82","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/schema.ts:143"},"level":0},{"id":"XlsxExtractSchema","longname":"XlsxExtractSchema","name":"XlsxExtractSchema","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Flat query parameters for `POST /xlsx/extract`.\nThe raw .xlsx travels in the body; everything here is a reader option.","meta":{"lineno":142},"order":12,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/xlsx/schema.js:95","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/schema.ts:168"},"level":0},{"id":"XlsxMetadataSchema","longname":"XlsxMetadataSchema","name":"XlsxMetadataSchema","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Flat query parameters for `POST /xlsx/metadata`.","meta":{"lineno":163},"order":16,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/xlsx/schema.js:104","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/schema.ts:194"},"level":0}],"fp":"de226afa0b3c43ac9f38768e85786d5e2bcac8681757bd47f699f2d671b82d97","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730469782,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/schema.ts":{"fp":"68d516d0dfe6132bc134927fca6f0f505b0a9b666ffdc5e6cc1f3e8108a5b70b","issues":[],"kind":"md","markdown":"## Members\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#autofilter\">autofilter</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Auto filter range, e.g. A1:C10.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#cellDates\">cellDates</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Write Date cells (type <code>d</code>) instead of numeric serials when true.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#cols\">cols</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Column properties written to <code>!cols</code> (width wpx/wch, hidden, outline level).</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#columns\">columns</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Object rows only: lock the column order (default: first-appearance order).</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#merges\">merges</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Merge ranges, e.g. A1:C2.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#name\">name</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Sheet name (1-31 chars, Excel charset); duplicates auto-uniquify. <code>date1904</code> workbooks are refused on write (SheetJS serializes 1904-flagged Date cells with the 1900 epoch).</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#rows\">rows</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Rows: objects map keys to cells; arrays emit positional cells. At least one row.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#sheetVisibility\">sheetVisibility</a></dt>\n<dd><p>0 visible, 1 hidden, 2 very hidden.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#Names\">Names</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Workbook-global defined names (<code>x</code> in expressions, scoped via <code>Sheet</code>).</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#header\">header</a></dt>\n<dd><p>1 = AOA rows, <code>A</code> = column-letter keys, or comma-separated custom headers.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#maxCells\">maxCells</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Reject packages whose worksheets carry more cells than this; bounds parse cost.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#sheet\">sheet</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Sheet name or 0-based index.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#maxCells\">maxCells</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Reject archives whose cells exceed this count (checked before SheetJS parses).</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n## Constants\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#SPREADSHEET_MIME\">SPREADSHEET_MIME</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Only the plain OOXML spreadsheet mime; templates, macros and other packages are rejected.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#cellSchema\">cellSchema</a></dt>\n<dd><p>One cell in a build payload: primitive or a SheetJS <code>CellObject</code>.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#XlsxBuildSchema\">XlsxBuildSchema</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Body of <code>POST /xlsx/build</code>.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#XlsxExtractSchema\">XlsxExtractSchema</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Flat query parameters for <code>POST /xlsx/extract</code>.\nThe raw .xlsx travels in the body; everything here is a reader option.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#XlsxMetadataSchema\">XlsxMetadataSchema</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Flat query parameters for <code>POST /xlsx/metadata</code>.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"autofilter\"></a>\n\n## autofilter\nAuto filter range, e.g. A1:C10.\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/schema.ts:65  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/xlsx/schema.js:39\n<a name=\"cellDates\"></a>\n\n## cellDates\nWrite Date cells (type `d`) instead of numeric serials when true.\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/schema.ts:69  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/xlsx/schema.js:40\n<a name=\"cols\"></a>\n\n## cols\nColumn properties written to `!cols` (width wpx/wch, hidden, outline level).\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/schema.ts:73  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/xlsx/schema.js:41\n<a name=\"columns\"></a>\n\n## columns\nObject rows only: lock the column order (default: first-appearance order).\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/schema.ts:77  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/xlsx/schema.js:42\n<a name=\"merges\"></a>\n\n## merges\nMerge ranges, e.g. A1:C2.\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/schema.ts:81  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/xlsx/schema.js:43\n<a name=\"name\"></a>\n\n## name\nSheet name (1-31 chars, Excel charset); duplicates auto-uniquify. `date1904` workbooks are refused on write (SheetJS serializes 1904-flagged Date cells with the 1900 epoch).\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/schema.ts:85  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/xlsx/schema.js:44\n<a name=\"rows\"></a>\n\n## rows\nRows: objects map keys to cells; arrays emit positional cells. At least one row.\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/schema.ts:96  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/xlsx/schema.js:49\n<a name=\"sheetVisibility\"></a>\n\n## sheetVisibility\n0 visible, 1 hidden, 2 very hidden.\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/schema.ts:100  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/xlsx/schema.js:50\n<a name=\"Names\"></a>\n\n## Names\nWorkbook-global defined names (`x` in expressions, scoped via `Sheet`).\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/schema.ts:151  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/xlsx/schema.js:87\n<a name=\"header\"></a>\n\n## header\n1 = AOA rows, `A` = column-letter keys, or comma-separated custom headers.\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/schema.ts:174  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/xlsx/schema.js:98\n<a name=\"maxCells\"></a>\n\n## maxCells\nReject packages whose worksheets carry more cells than this; bounds parse cost.\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/schema.ts:178  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/xlsx/schema.js:99\n<a name=\"sheet\"></a>\n\n## sheet\nSheet name or 0-based index.\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/schema.ts:183  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/xlsx/schema.js:101\n<a name=\"maxCells\"></a>\n\n## maxCells\nReject archives whose cells exceed this count (checked before SheetJS parses).\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/schema.ts:198  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/xlsx/schema.js:105\n<a name=\"SPREADSHEET_MIME\"></a>\n\n## SPREADSHEET\\_MIME\nOnly the plain OOXML spreadsheet mime; templates, macros and other packages are rejected.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/schema.ts:8  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/xlsx/schema.js:3\n<a name=\"cellSchema\"></a>\n\n## cellSchema\nOne cell in a build payload: primitive or a SheetJS `CellObject`.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/schema.ts:23  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/xlsx/schema.js:9\n<a name=\"XlsxBuildSchema\"></a>\n\n## XlsxBuildSchema\nBody of `POST /xlsx/build`.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/schema.ts:143  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/xlsx/schema.js:82\n<a name=\"XlsxExtractSchema\"></a>\n\n## XlsxExtractSchema\nFlat query parameters for `POST /xlsx/extract`.\nThe raw .xlsx travels in the body; everything here is a reader option.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/schema.ts:168  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/xlsx/schema.js:95\n<a name=\"XlsxMetadataSchema\"></a>\n\n## XlsxMetadataSchema\nFlat query parameters for `POST /xlsx/metadata`.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/schema.ts:194  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/xlsx/schema.js:104\n","symbols":18,"lastUsed":1795730469858},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/xlsx.controller.spec.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"rawSink","longname":"rawSink","name":"rawSink","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Creates a Writable raw sink with `setHeader` mocks for assertions.","params":[],"returns":[{"description":"A writable with a mocked `setHeader`.","type":{"names":["Writable & { setHeader: ReturnType<typeof vi.fn>; }"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":8},"order":0,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/xlsx.controller.spec.ts:10"},"level":0}],"fp":"23fa9692f41a7c58854b9ad0c1d871c31da6510ae0b03bbcae4b9b8ffde9500d","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730469790,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/xlsx.controller.spec.ts":{"fp":"63729bbb49d0e10551cde0f2d20c16ae362d936a117e6d9859b4fcc7c4fb3379","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","markdown":"<a name=\"rawSink\"></a>\n\n## rawSink() ⇒ <code>Writable &amp; { setHeader: ReturnType&lt;typeof vi.fn&gt;; }</code>\nCreates a Writable raw sink with `setHeader` mocks for assertions.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Writable &amp; { setHeader: ReturnType&lt;typeof vi.fn&gt;; }</code> - A writable with a mocked `setHeader`.  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/xlsx.controller.spec.ts:10  \n","symbols":1,"lastUsed":1795730469819},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/xlsx.controller.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"XlsxController","longname":"XlsxController","name":"XlsxController","kind":"member","scope":"global","description":"Spreadsheet routes. `/xlsx/build` consumes JSON (no media interceptors);\n`/xlsx/extract` and `/xlsx/metadata` take the binary upload and are\nClamAV-scanned like any other binary payload.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":46},"order":0,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/xlsx/xlsx.controller.js:21","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/xlsx.controller.ts:36"},"level":0},{"id":"XlsxController#build","longname":"XlsxController#build","name":"build","kind":"function","scope":"instance","description":"Builds a workbook from JSON rows and cell objects.","memberof":"XlsxController","params":[{"description":"Raw reply, streamed as `.xlsx`.","name":"response","type":{"names":["FastifyReply<import(\"fastify\").RouteGenericInterface, import(\"fastify\").RawServerDefault, import(\"http\").IncomingMessage, import(\"http\").ServerResponse<import(\"http\").IncomingMessage>, unknown, import(\"fastify\").FastifySchema, import(\"fastify\").FastifyTypeProviderDefault, unknown>"]}},{"description":"Sheets, workbook properties, defined names.","name":"body","type":{"names":["{ sheets: { [x: string]: any; rows: (Record<string, string | number | boolean | { [x: string]: unknown; c?: { [x: string]: unknown; a: string; t: string; }[]; f?: string; l?: { [x: string]: unknown; Target?: string; Tooltip?: string; }; t?: \"b\" | \"n\" | \"s\" | \"d\" | \"e\" | \"z\"; v?: unknown; z?: string; }> | (string | number | boolean | { [x: string]: unknown; c?: { [x: string]: unknown; a: string; t: string; }[]; f?: string; l?: { [x: string]: unknown; Target?: string; Tooltip?: string; }; t?: \"b\" | \"n\" | \"s\" | \"d\" | \"e\" | \"z\"; v?: unknown; z?: string; })[])[]; cellDates?: boolean; cols?: { [x: string]: unknown; hidden?: boolean; level?: number; wch?: number; width?: number; wpx?: number; }[]; columns?: string[]; merges?: any[]; sheetVisibility?: 0 | 1 | 2; }[]; workbook?: { [x: string]: unknown; Names?: { [x: string]: unknown; Name: string; Ref: string; Sheet?: number; }[]; Props?: { [x: string]: unknown; Author?: string; Category?: string; Comments?: string; Company?: string; CreatedDate?: Date; Keywords?: string; Manager?: string; ModifiedBy?: string; ModifiedDate?: Date; Subject?: string; Title?: string; }; WBProps?: { [x: string]: unknown; CodeName?: string; date1904?: boolean; filterPrivacy?: boolean; }; }; }"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The workbook bytes (201).","type":{"names":["Promise<void>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":82},"async":true,"order":1,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/xlsx/xlsx.controller.js:28","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/xlsx.controller.ts:49"},"level":0},{"id":"XlsxController#extract","longname":"XlsxController#extract","name":"extract","kind":"function","scope":"instance","description":"Extracts one sheet as typed JSON.","memberof":"XlsxController","params":[{"description":"Flat reader options.","name":"query","type":{"names":["{ [x: string]: any; maxCells: number; raw: boolean; blankrows?: boolean; skipHidden?: boolean; }"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The records and sheet name (201).","type":{"names":["Promise<{ records: unknown[]; sheet: string; truncated: boolean; } | { records: unknown[]; sheet: string; truncated?: undefined; }>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":93},"order":2,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/xlsx/xlsx.controller.js:34","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/xlsx.controller.ts:66"},"level":0},{"id":"XlsxController#metadata","longname":"XlsxController#metadata","name":"metadata","kind":"function","scope":"instance","description":"Structural workbook metadata: dims, counts, props, names, formula inventory, cell census.","memberof":"XlsxController","params":[{"description":"Flat metadata options.","name":"query","type":{"names":["{ maxCells: number; }"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The metadata document (201).","type":{"names":["Promise<{ custprops: object; definedNames: { name: string; ref: string; sheet: number; }[]; props: import(\"xlsx\").FullProperties; sheets: { autofilter: boolean; cells: number; cols: number; formulas: number; hidden: boolean; merges: number; name: string; ref: string; rows: number; types: { [k: string]: number; }; }[]; totalCells: number; }>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":101},"order":3,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/xlsx/xlsx.controller.js:37","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/xlsx.controller.ts:79"},"level":0}],"fp":"44faa947c6526f141e0c40b5f005e85f31218080a484f2cf83e99f76031e0085","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730469822,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/xlsx.controller.ts":{"fp":"5ad55c16db0b0007ac47282f8e46497183ad35cd881f353d1c870390d6adaa9c","issues":[],"kind":"md","markdown":"<a name=\"XlsxController\"></a>\n\n## XlsxController\nSpreadsheet routes. `/xlsx/build` consumes JSON (no media interceptors);\n`/xlsx/extract` and `/xlsx/metadata` take the binary upload and are\nClamAV-scanned like any other binary payload.\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/xlsx.controller.ts:36  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/xlsx/xlsx.controller.js:21\n\n* [XlsxController](#XlsxController)\n    * [.build(response, body)](#XlsxController+build) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code>\n    * [.extract(query)](#XlsxController+extract) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;{ records: unknown[]; sheet: string; truncated: boolean; } \\| { records: unknown[]; sheet: string; truncated?: undefined; }&gt;</code>\n    * [.metadata(query)](#XlsxController+metadata) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;{ custprops: object; definedNames: { name: string; ref: string; sheet: number; }[]; props: import(&quot;xlsx&quot;).FullProperties; sheets: { autofilter: boolean; cells: number; cols: number; formulas: number; hidden: boolean; merges: number; name: string; ref: string; rows: number; types: { [k: string]: number; }; }[]; totalCells: number; }&gt;</code>\n\n<a name=\"XlsxController+build\"></a>\n\n### xlsxController.build(response, body) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code>\nBuilds a workbook from JSON rows and cell objects.\n\n**Kind**: instance method of [<code>XlsxController</code>](#XlsxController)  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code> - The workbook bytes (201).  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| response | <code>FastifyReply&lt;import(&quot;fastify&quot;).RouteGenericInterface, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).RawServerDefault, import(&quot;http&quot;).IncomingMessage, import(&quot;http&quot;).ServerResponse&lt;import(&quot;http&quot;).IncomingMessage&gt;, unknown, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).FastifySchema, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).FastifyTypeProviderDefault, unknown&gt;</code> | Raw reply, streamed as `.xlsx`. |\n| body | <code>{ sheets: { [x: string]: any; rows: (Record&lt;string, string \\| number \\| boolean \\| { [x: string]: unknown; c?: { [x: string]: unknown; a: string; t: string; }[]; f?: string; l?: { [x: string]: unknown; Target?: string; Tooltip?: string; }; t?: &quot;b&quot; \\| &quot;n&quot; \\| &quot;s&quot; \\| &quot;d&quot; \\| &quot;e&quot; \\| &quot;z&quot;; v?: unknown; z?: string; }&gt; \\| (string \\| number \\| boolean \\| { [x: string]: unknown; c?: { [x: string]: unknown; a: string; t: string; }[]; f?: string; l?: { [x: string]: unknown; Target?: string; Tooltip?: string; }; t?: &quot;b&quot; \\| &quot;n&quot; \\| &quot;s&quot; \\| &quot;d&quot; \\| &quot;e&quot; \\| &quot;z&quot;; v?: unknown; z?: string; })[])[]; cellDates?: boolean; cols?: { [x: string]: unknown; hidden?: boolean; level?: number; wch?: number; width?: number; wpx?: number; }[]; columns?: string[]; merges?: any[]; sheetVisibility?: 0 \\| 1 \\| 2; }[]; workbook?: { [x: string]: unknown; Names?: { [x: string]: unknown; Name: string; Ref: string; Sheet?: number; }[]; Props?: { [x: string]: unknown; Author?: string; Category?: string; Comments?: string; Company?: string; CreatedDate?: Date; Keywords?: string; Manager?: string; ModifiedBy?: string; ModifiedDate?: Date; Subject?: string; Title?: string; }; WBProps?: { [x: string]: unknown; CodeName?: string; date1904?: boolean; filterPrivacy?: boolean; }; }; }</code> | Sheets, workbook properties, defined names. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/xlsx.controller.ts:49  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/xlsx/xlsx.controller.js:28\n<a name=\"XlsxController+extract\"></a>\n\n### xlsxController.extract(query) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;{ records: unknown[]; sheet: string; truncated: boolean; } \\| { records: unknown[]; sheet: string; truncated?: undefined; }&gt;</code>\nExtracts one sheet as typed JSON.\n\n**Kind**: instance method of [<code>XlsxController</code>](#XlsxController)  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;{ records: unknown[]; sheet: string; truncated: boolean; } \\| { records: unknown[]; sheet: string; truncated?: undefined; }&gt;</code> - The records and sheet name (201).  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| query | <code>{ [x: string]: any; maxCells: number; raw: boolean; blankrows?: boolean; skipHidden?: boolean; }</code> | Flat reader options. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/xlsx/xlsx.controller.ts:66  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/xlsx/xlsx.controller.js:34\n<a name=\"XlsxController+metadata\"></a>\n\n### xlsxController.metadata(query) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;{ custprops: object; definedNames: { name: string; ref: string; sheet: number; }[]; props: import(&quot;xlsx&quot;).FullProperties; sheets: { autofilter: boolean; cells: number; cols: number; formulas: number; hidden: boolean; merges: number; name: string; ref: string; rows: number; types: { [k: string]: number; }; }[]; totalCells: number; }&gt;</code>\nStructural workbook metadata: dims, counts, props, names, formula inventory, cell census.\n\n**Kind**: instance method of [<code>XlsxController</code>](#XlsxController)  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;{ custprops: object; definedNames: { name: string; ref: string; sheet: number; }[]; props: import(&quot;xlsx&quot;).FullProperties; sheets: { autofilter: boolean; cells: number; cols: number; formulas: number; hidden: boolean; merges: number; name: string; ref: string; rows: number; types: { [k: string]: number; }; }[]; totalCells: number; }&gt;</code> - The metadata document (201).  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| query | <code>{ maxC