csSnapshotSchema","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Runtime contract for the payload served by `GET /metrics`.\nMirrors docs/metrics.md and the backend's metrics service; both sides ship together.","meta":{"lineno":50},"order":0,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/dashboard/src/lib/api.ts:55"},"level":0},{"id":"metricsToken","longname":"metricsToken","name":"metricsToken","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Reads the session token, when one was stored for this tab.","returns":[{"description":"The stored token, or undefined.","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":97},"order":6,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/dashboard/src/lib/api.ts:122"},"level":0},{"id":"setMetricsToken","longname":"setMetricsToken","name":"setMetricsToken","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Stores or clears the session token.","params":[{"description":"Token to store, or undefined/empty to clear it.","name":"token","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":104},"order":7,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/dashboard/src/lib/api.ts:130"},"level":0},{"id":"fetchMetrics","longname":"fetchMetrics","name":"fetchMetrics","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Fetches and validates the current metrics snapshot.\n\nThe dashboard polls, so there is deliberately no retry wrapper: the next\npoll is the retry. Failures surface as `ApiError` for 401/503 and render\nthe token gate / disabled banner. A payload that does not match the contract\nbecomes the same generic error, since it may contain client IPs.","returns":[{"description":"The aggregated metrics snapshot.","type":{"names":["Promise<{ generatedAt: string; inFlight: number; last24h: { bucket: string; bytesIn: number; bytesOut: number; errors: number; requests: number; }[]; metricsDisabled: boolean; perIp: { [x: string]: unknown; bytesIn: number; bytesOut: number; filesIn: number; filesOut: number; ip: string; requests: number; }[]; perRoute: { [x: string]: unknown; avgMs: number; bytesOut: number; errors: number; p50: number; p95: number; p99: number; requests: number; route: string; }[]; today: { avgMs: number; bytesIn: number; bytesOut: number; cacheHitRate: number; cacheHits: number; cacheMisses: number; clientErrors: number; filesIn: number; filesOut: number; requests: number; scanBlocked: number; scanClean: number; scanInfected: number; serverErrors: number; }; totals: { avgMs: number; bytesIn: number; bytesOut: number; cacheHitRate: number; cacheHits: number; cacheMisses: number; clientErrors: number; filesIn: number; filesOut: number; requests: number; scanBlocked: number; scanClean: number; scanInfected: number; serverErrors: number; }; uptimeSeconds: number; }>"]}}],"exceptions":[{"description":"ApiError When the backend answers with a non-2xx status."},{"description":"MetricsContractError When the payload does not match the documented contract."}],"meta":{"lineno":132},"order":8,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/dashboard/src/lib/api.ts:160"},"level":0},{"id":"ApiError#status","longname":"ApiError#status","name":"status","kind":"member","scope":"instance","description":"HTTP status code returned by the server.","memberof":"ApiError","meta":{"lineno":68},"order":1,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/dashboard/src/lib/api.ts:89"},"level":0}],"fp":"2de8c364da7ba03eb01157dcccf44e848fb94605f85f18666e0101f6c8242f69","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730471756,"symbols":0},"md:packages/dashboard/src/lib/format.spec.ts":{"fp":"af9efe0ac98d49f746eaef9e8079d8d918f3eb3bcf018df0a42b0f23d1c3972b","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","skipped":"no-jsdoc","symbols":0,"lastUsed":1795730471766},"md:packages/dashboard/src/lib/api.ts":{"fp":"7b948104a92451876be8befb2e00256084f89d7125464606b54a7527658972bc","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","markdown":"## Classes\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#ApiError\">ApiError</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Error carrying the HTTP status returned by the backend.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#MetricsContractError\">MetricsContractError</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Error thrown when a successful response does not match the metrics contract.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n## Constants\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#metricsSnapshotSchema\">metricsSnapshotSchema</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Runtime contract for the payload served by <code>GET /metrics</code>.\nMirrors docs/metrics.md and the backend&#39;s metrics service; both sides ship together.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n## Functions\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#metricsToken\">metricsToken()</a> ⇒ <code>string</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Reads the session token, when one was stored for this tab.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#setMetricsToken\">setMetricsToken(token)</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Stores or clears the session token.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#fetchMetrics\">fetchMetrics()</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;{ generatedAt: string; inFlight: number; last24h: { bucket: string; bytesIn: number; bytesOut: number; errors: number; requests: number; }[]; metricsDisabled: boolean; perIp: { [x: string]: unknown; bytesIn: number; bytesOut: number; filesIn: number; filesOut: number; ip: string; requests: number; }[]; perRoute: { [x: string]: unknown; avgMs: number; bytesOut: number; errors: number; p50: number; p95: number; p99: number; requests: number; route: string; }[]; today: { avgMs: number; bytesIn: number; bytesOut: number; cacheHitRate: number; cacheHits: number; cacheMisses: number; clientErrors: number; filesIn: number; filesOut: number; requests: number; scanBlocked: number; scanClean: number; scanInfected: number; serverErrors: number; }; totals: { avgMs: number; bytesIn: number; bytesOut: number; cacheHitRate: number; cacheHits: number; cacheMisses: number; clientErrors: number; filesIn: number; filesOut: number; requests: number; scanBlocked: number; scanClean: number; scanInfected: number; serverErrors: number; }; uptimeSeconds: number; }&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Fetches and validates the current metrics snapshot.</p>\n<p>The dashboard polls, so there is deliberately no retry wrapper: the next\npoll is the retry. Failures surface as <code>ApiError</code> for 401/503 and render\nthe token gate / disabled banner. A payload that does not match the contract\nbecomes the same generic error, since it may contain client IPs.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"ApiError\"></a>\n\n## ApiError\nError carrying the HTTP status returned by the backend.\n\n**Kind**: global class  \nsrc: packages/dashboard/src/lib/api.ts:85  \n\n* [ApiError](#ApiError)\n    * [new ApiError(status)](#new_ApiError_new)\n    * [.status](#ApiError+status)\n\n<a name=\"new_ApiError_new\"></a>\n\n### new ApiError(status)\nCreates an ApiError.\n\n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| status | <code>number</code> | HTTP status code returned by the server. |\n\n<a name=\"ApiError+status\"></a>\n\n### apiError.status\nHTTP status code returned by the server.\n\n**Kind**: instance property of [<code>ApiError</code>](#ApiError)  \nsrc: packages/dashboard/src/lib/api.ts:89  \n<a name=\"MetricsContractError\"></a>\n\n## MetricsContractError\nError thrown when a successful response does not match the metrics contract.\n\n**Kind**: global class  \nsrc: packages/dashboard/src/lib/api.ts:105  \n<a name=\"new_MetricsContractError_new\"></a>\n\n### new MetricsContractError()\nCreates a contract error with a fixed message that never echoes the payload.\n\n<a name=\"metricsSnapshotSchema\"></a>\n\n## metricsSnapshotSchema\nRuntime contract for the payload served by `GET /metrics`.\nMirrors docs/metrics.md and the backend's metrics service; both sides ship together.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: packages/dashboard/src/lib/api.ts:55  \n<a name=\"metricsToken\"></a>\n\n## metricsToken() ⇒ <code>string</code>\nReads the session token, when one was stored for this tab.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>string</code> - The stored token, or undefined.  \nsrc: packages/dashboard/src/lib/api.ts:122  \n<a name=\"setMetricsToken\"></a>\n\n## setMetricsToken(token)\nStores or clears the session token.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| token | <code>string</code> | Token to store, or undefined/empty to clear it. |\n\nsrc: packages/dashboard/src/lib/api.ts:130  \n<a name=\"fetchMetrics\"></a>\n\n## fetchMetrics() ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;{ generatedAt: string; inFlight: number; last24h: { bucket: string; bytesIn: number; bytesOut: number; errors: number; requests: number; }[]; metricsDisabled: boolean; perIp: { [x: string]: unknown; bytesIn: number; bytesOut: number; filesIn: number; filesOut: number; ip: string; requests: number; }[]; perRoute: { [x: string]: unknown; avgMs: number; bytesOut: number; errors: number; p50: number; p95: number; p99: number; requests: number; route: string; }[]; today: { avgMs: number; bytesIn: number; bytesOut: number; cacheHitRate: number; cacheHits: number; cacheMisses: number; clientErrors: number; filesIn: number; filesOut: number; requests: number; scanBlocked: number; scanClean: number; scanInfected: number; serverErrors: number; }; totals: { avgMs: number; bytesIn: number; bytesOut: number; cacheHitRate: number; cacheHits: number; cacheMisses: number; clientErrors: number; filesIn: number; filesOut: number; requests: number; scanBlocked: number; scanClean: number; scanInfected: number; serverErrors: number; }; uptimeSeconds: number; }&gt;</code>\nFetches and validates the current metrics snapshot.\n\nThe dashboard polls, so there is deliberately no retry wrapper: the next\npoll is the retry. Failures surface as `ApiError` for 401/503 and render\nthe token gate / disabled banner. A payload that does not match the contract\nbecomes the same generic error, since it may contain client IPs.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;{ generatedAt: string; inFlight: number; last24h: { bucket: string; bytesIn: number; bytesOut: number; errors: number; requests: number; }[]; metricsDisabled: boolean; perIp: { [x: string]: unknown; bytesIn: number; bytesOut: number; filesIn: number; filesOut: number; ip: string; requests: number; }[]; perRoute: { [x: string]: unknown; avgMs: number; bytesOut: number; errors: number; p50: number; p95: number; p99: number; requests: number; route: string; }[]; today: { avgMs: number; bytesIn: number; bytesOut: number; cacheHitRate: number; cacheHits: number; cacheMisses: number; clientErrors: number; filesIn: number; filesOut: number; requests: number; scanBlocked: number; scanClean: number; scanInfected: number; serverErrors: number; }; totals: { avgMs: number; bytesIn: number; bytesOut: number; cacheHitRate: number; cacheHits: number; cacheMisses: number; clientErrors: number; filesIn: number; filesOut: number; requests: number; scanBlocked: number; scanClean: number; scanInfected: number; serverErrors: number; }; uptimeSeconds: number; }&gt;</code> - The aggregated metrics snapshot.  \n**Throws**:\n\n- ApiError When the backend answers with a non-2xx status.\n- MetricsContractError When the payload does not match the documented contract.\n\nsrc: packages/dashboard/src/lib/api.ts:160  \n","symbols":9,"lastUsed":1795730471799},"tdata:packages/dashboard/src/lib/format.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"formatBytes","longname":"formatBytes","name":"formatBytes","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Formats a byte count with binary (1024) units.","params":[{"description":"Size in bytes; non-finite or negative values format as `0 B`.","name":"bytes","type":{"names":["number"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"Human-readable string such as `1.5 GB`.","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":7},"order":0,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/dashboard/src/lib/format.ts:8"},"level":0},{"id":"formatCount","longname":"formatCount","name":"formatCount","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Formats a count with thousands separators.","params":[{"description":"The count to format.","name":"value","type":{"names":["number"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"Locale-formatted string such as `1,234,567`.","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":25},"order":1,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/dashboard/src/lib/format.ts:22"},"level":0},{"id":"formatHourBucket","longname":"formatHourBucket","name":"formatHourBucket","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Turns an ISO hour bucket into an axis label like `11-17 14:00`.","params":[{"description":"ISO hour bucket, e.g. `2026-11-17T14`.","name":"bucket","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"Day and hour, e.g. `11-17 14:00`; `00:00` for malformed input.","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":33},"order":2,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/dashboard/src/lib/format.ts:31"},"level":0},{"id":"formatMs","longname":"formatMs","name":"formatMs","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Formats a duration given in milliseconds.","params":[{"description":"Duration in milliseconds; non-finite or negative values format as `0 ms`.","name":"ms","type":{"names":["number"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"String such as `12.3 ms`.","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":42},"order":3,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/dashboard/src/lib/format.ts:41"},"level":0},{"id":"formatPercent","longname":"formatPercent","name":"formatPercent","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Formats a ratio as a percentage.","params":[{"description":"Value in the range [0, 1].","name":"ratio","type":{"names":["number"]}},{"description":"Number of decimals to show.","name":"digits","type":{"names":["number"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"Percent string such as `87.5%`, or `0%` for non-finite input.","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":55},"order":4,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/dashboard/src/lib/format.ts:53"},"level":0}],"fp":"cc24c82b7116d3be5b0f1c8c09ad7a09c1282d7a75bcadd79718bd5e6d9609e1","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730471799,"symbols":0},"md:packages/dashboard/src/lib/format.ts":{"fp":"0088225bcde2f2adbcfd72cff7e87bb26dc43af1281e55905e99702597f1a190","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","markdown":"## Functions\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#formatBytes\">formatBytes(bytes)</a> ⇒ <code>string</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Formats a byte count with binary (1024) units.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#formatCount\">formatCount(value)</a> ⇒ <code>string</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Formats a count with thousands separators.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#formatHourBucket\">formatHourBucket(bucket)</a> ⇒ <code>string</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Turns an ISO hour bucket into an axis label like <code>11-17 14:00</code>.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#formatMs\">formatMs(ms)</a> ⇒ <code>string</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Formats a duration given in milliseconds.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#formatPercent\">formatPercent(ratio, digits)</a> ⇒ <code>string</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Formats a ratio as a percentage.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"formatBytes\"></a>\n\n## formatBytes(bytes) ⇒ <code>string</code>\nFormats a byte count with binary (1024) units.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>string</code> - Human-readable string such as `1.5 GB`.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| bytes | <code>number</code> | Size in bytes; non-finite or negative values format as `0 B`. |\n\nsrc: packages/dashboard/src/lib/format.ts:8  \n<a name=\"formatCount\"></a>\n\n## formatCount(value) ⇒ <code>string</code>\nFormats a count with thousands separators.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>string</code> - Locale-formatted string such as `1,234,567`.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| value | <code>number</code> | The count to format. |\n\nsrc: packages/dashboard/src/lib/format.ts:22  \n<a name=\"formatHourBucket\"></a>\n\n## formatHourBucket(bucket) ⇒ <code>string</code>\nTurns an ISO hour bucket into an axis label like `11-17 14:00`.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>string</code> - Day and hour, e.g. `11-17 14:00`; `00:00` for malformed input.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| bucket | <code>string</code> | ISO hour bucket, e.g. `2026-11-17T14`. |\n\nsrc: packages/dashboard/src/lib/format.ts:31  \n<a name=\"formatMs\"></a>\n\n## formatMs(ms) ⇒ <code>string</code>\nFormats a duration given in milliseconds.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>string</code> - String such as `12.3 ms`.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ms | <code>number</code> | Duration in milliseconds; non-finite or negative values format as `0 ms`. |\n\nsrc: packages/dashboard/src/lib/format.ts:41  \n<a name=\"formatPercent\"></a>\n\n## formatPercent(ratio, digits) ⇒ <code>string</code>\nFormats a ratio as a percentage.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>string</code> - Percent string such as `87.5%`, or `0%` for non-finite input.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ratio | <code>number</code> | Value in the range [0, 1]. |\n| digits | <code>number</code> | Number of decimals to show. |\n\nsrc: packages/dashboard/src/lib/format.ts:53  \n","symbols":5,"lastUsed":1795730471837},"tdata:packages/dashboard/src/main.tsx":{"doclets":[],"fp":"acd4eb34b487d807d2f65c345b16c75a35d7a9e4a5b26f682ba64a541a3c69bc","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730471850,"symbols":0},"md:packages/dashboard/src/main.tsx":{"fp":"00f798a486d915796d4bcf53420a0df6e4d415df4cf7d8a68e07facc41b2007c","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","skipped":"no-jsdoc","symbols":0,"lastUsed":1795730471872},"tdata:packages/dashboard/src/routes.smoke.spec.tsx":{"doclets":[],"fp":"1f0004863b11371c9840a73e8d6aa09684b8bd24397f201a822d9646005875cf","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730471850,"symbols":0},"md:packages/dashboard/src/routes.smoke.spec.tsx":{"fp":"8ec43049ee3014cb0f2a627215e6bd60185bd7172063669bc5601cfcb2590b1f","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","skipped":"no-jsdoc","symbols":0,"lastUsed":17957304