irst)"],"kind":"md","markdown":"## Functions\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#NotFound\">NotFound()</a> ⇒ <code>import(&quot;react&quot;).JSX.Element</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Fallback for unknown paths.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#RootComponent\">RootComponent()</a> ⇒ <code>import(&quot;react&quot;).JSX.Element</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Root layout: the app shell with the top navigation and routed content.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"NotFound\"></a>\n\n## NotFound() ⇒ <code>import(&quot;react&quot;).JSX.Element</code>\nFallback for unknown paths.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>import(&quot;react&quot;).JSX.Element</code> - The not-found element.  \nsrc: packages/dashboard/src/routes/__root.tsx:26  \n<a name=\"RootComponent\"></a>\n\n## RootComponent() ⇒ <code>import(&quot;react&quot;).JSX.Element</code>\nRoot layout: the app shell with the top navigation and routed content.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>import(&quot;react&quot;).JSX.Element</code> - The shell element.  \nsrc: packages/dashboard/src/routes/__root.tsx:39  \n","symbols":2,"lastUsed":1795730471911},"tdata:packages/dashboard/src/routes/ip.$ip.tsx":{"doclets":[{"id":"Route","longname":"Route","name":"Route","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"File-based route for the per-IP detail page.","meta":{"lineno":6},"order":0,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/dashboard/src/routes/ip.$ip.tsx:8"},"level":0},{"id":"RouteComponent","longname":"RouteComponent","name":"RouteComponent","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Reads the route param and renders the IP detail page.","params":[],"returns":[{"description":"The IP detail page element.","type":{"names":["import(\"react\").JSX.Element"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":13},"order":1,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/dashboard/src/routes/ip.$ip.tsx:16"},"level":0}],"fp":"2fbc057978584423b9d6b5ebf30d056ddf7658bb2146b65e9e01d44369558e95","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730471881,"symbols":0},"md:packages/dashboard/src/routes/ip.$ip.tsx":{"fp":"7575d398288f05e4db2c3c7f3f6d46c9c462086b5d677ebb99700832a42c8903","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","markdown":"## Constants\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#Route\">Route</a></dt>\n<dd><p>File-based route for the per-IP detail page.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n## Functions\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#RouteComponent\">RouteComponent()</a> ⇒ <code>import(&quot;react&quot;).JSX.Element</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Reads the route param and renders the IP detail page.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"Route\"></a>\n\n## Route\nFile-based route for the per-IP detail page.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: packages/dashboard/src/routes/ip.$ip.tsx:8  \n<a name=\"RouteComponent\"></a>\n\n## RouteComponent() ⇒ <code>import(&quot;react&quot;).JSX.Element</code>\nReads the route param and renders the IP detail page.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>import(&quot;react&quot;).JSX.Element</code> - The IP detail page element.  \nsrc: packages/dashboard/src/routes/ip.$ip.tsx:16  \n","symbols":2,"lastUsed":1795730471937},"tdata:packages/dashboard/src/routeTree.gen.ts":{"doclets":[],"fp":"99f093921fd24570df27c9566f16365f745f8c4260b7b17eb4bb0374b1d87711","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730471911,"symbols":0},"md:packages/dashboard/src/routeTree.gen.ts":{"fp":"e1f3867896e4df0d8308a580c62fb32704730cb5595661e97c3b3e5356cfca3a","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","skipped":"no-jsdoc","symbols":0,"lastUsed":1795730471911},"md:packages/backend/src/resources/image/image.service.ts":{"fp":"43eb65561343fb0a7cceea7209b07e524170b69126763627194d24ce866e1f8c","issues":[],"kind":"md","markdown":"## Members\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#ImageService\">ImageService</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Image feature service: streams uploads through sharp workers for processing, metadata, DNA, stats and OCR.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n## Functions\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#parseLangs\">parseLangs(raw)</a> ⇒ <code>string[]</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Normalizes the <code>lang</code> query value: splits on <code>+</code> or <code>,</code>, lowercases,\ntrims, dedupes, sorts; defaults to <code>[&#39;eng&#39;]</code>, caps at 4 codes.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#preprocess\">preprocess(input, logger)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Preprocesses an image for OCR: auto-orient, downscale to at most 2000 px\nwithout enlarging, greyscale, normalize, sharpen; encoded as PNG.\nPixel bombs are rejected via <code>limitInputPixels</code>; undecodable or malicious\ninput surfaces as <a href=\"UnsupportedMediaTypeException\">UnsupportedMediaTypeException</a> instead of a 500.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"ImageService\"></a>\n\n## ImageService\nImage feature service: streams uploads through sharp workers for processing, metadata, DNA, stats and OCR.\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/image/image.service.ts:71  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/image/image.service.js:49\n<a name=\"parseLangs\"></a>\n\n## parseLangs(raw) ⇒ <code>string[]</code>\nNormalizes the `lang` query value: splits on `+` or `,`, lowercases,\ntrims, dedupes, sorts; defaults to `['eng']`, caps at 4 codes.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>string[]</code> - Sorted, deduped language codes.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| raw | <code>string</code> | Raw `lang` query parameter (already regex-validated). |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/image/image.service.ts:27  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/image/image.service.js:22\n<a name=\"preprocess\"></a>\n\n## preprocess(input, logger) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;&gt;</code>\nPreprocesses an image for OCR: auto-orient, downscale to at most 2000 px\nwithout enlarging, greyscale, normalize, sharpen; encoded as PNG.\nPixel bombs are rejected via `limitInputPixels`; undecodable or malicious\ninput surfaces as [UnsupportedMediaTypeException](UnsupportedMediaTypeException) instead of a 500.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;&gt;</code> - PNG bytes ready for tesseract.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| input | <code>Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;</code> | Raw (signature-verified) image bytes. |\n| logger | <code>Logger</code> | Logger used to record decode failures for operators. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/image/image.service.ts:49  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/image/image.service.js:33\n","symbols":3,"lastUsed":1795730468069},"tdata:packages/backend/src/basic-auth.spec.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"boot","longname":"boot","name":"boot","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Creates a Fastify instance with the perimeter installed and two probe routes.","params":[{"description":"The freshly imported adapter module.","name":"module_","type":{"names":["typeof import(\"./basic-auth.js\")"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The Fastify instance from the Nest adapter.","type":{"names":["Promise<import(\"fastify\").FastifyInstance<import(\"fastify\").RawServerDefault, import(\"http\").IncomingMessage & { originalUrl?: string; }, import(\"http\").ServerResponse<import(\"http\").IncomingMessage>, import(\"fastify\").FastifyBaseLogger, import(\"fastify\").FastifyTypeProviderDefault>>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":20},"async":true,"order":0,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/backend/src/basic-auth.spec.ts:27"},"level":0},{"id":"loadEnabled","longname":"loadEnabled","name":"loadEnabled","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Loads the adapter after stubbing both-or-neither credentials.","params":[],"returns":[{"description":"The freshly imported adapter module.","type":{"names":["Promise<typeof import(\"./basic-auth.js\")>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":31},"async":true,"order":1,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/backend/src/basic-auth.spec.ts:39"},"level":0},{"id":"rejectWithChallenge","longname":"rejectWithChallenge","name":"rejectWithChallenge","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Makes the mocked guard reject with the package's challenge.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":40},"order":2,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/backend/src/basic-auth.spec.ts:49"},"level":0}],"fp":"01e5fddd94131b1f0b48ce66d5f16533362438bc84b1edbe32294f56a4934209","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730447167,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/basic-auth.spec.ts":{"fp":"ea85acecc44344d30bb189e890da828d5e9d35b5e612729d4ced30afa7b8c0a9","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","markdown":"## Functions\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#boot\">boot(module_)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;import(&quot;fastify&quot;).FastifyInstance&lt;import(&quot;fastify&quot;).RawServerDefault, import(&quot;http&quot;).IncomingMessage &amp; { originalUrl?: string; }, import(&quot;http&quot;).ServerResponse&lt;import(&quot;http&quot;).IncomingMessage&gt;, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).FastifyBaseLogger, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).FastifyTypeProviderDefault&gt;&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Creates a Fastify instance with the perimeter installed and two probe routes.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#loadEnabled\">loadEnabled()</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;typeof import(&quot;./basic-auth.js&quot;)&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Loads the adapter after stubbing both-or-neither credentials.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#rejectWithChallenge\">rejectWithChallenge()</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Makes the mocked guard reject with the package&#39;s challenge.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"boot\"></a>\n\n## boot(module_) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;import(&quot;fastify&quot;).FastifyInstance&lt;import(&quot;fastify&quot;).RawServerDefault, import(&quot;http&quot;).IncomingMessage &amp; { originalUrl?: string; }, import(&quot;http&quot;).ServerResponse&lt;import(&quot;http&quot;).IncomingMessage&gt;, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).FastifyBaseLogger, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).FastifyTypeProviderDefault&gt;&gt;</code>\nCreates a Fastify instance with the perimeter installed and two probe routes.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;import(&quot;fastify&quot;).FastifyInstance&lt;import(&quot;fastify&quot;).RawServerDefault, import(&quot;http&quot;).IncomingMessage &amp; { originalUrl?: string; }, import(&quot;http&quot;).ServerResponse&lt;import(&quot;http&quot;).IncomingMessage&gt;, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).FastifyBaseLogger, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).FastifyTypeProviderDefault&gt;&gt;</code> - The Fastify instance from the Nest adapter.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| module_ | <code>typeof import(&quot;./basic-auth.js&quot;)</code> | The freshly imported adapter module. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/basic-auth.spec.ts:27  \n<a name=\"loadEnabled\"></a>\n\n## loadEnabled() ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;typeof import(&quot;./basic-auth.js&quot;)&gt;</code>\nLoads the adapter after stubbing both-or-neither credentials.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;typeof import(&quot;./basic-auth.js&quot;)&gt;</code> - The freshly imported adapter module.  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/basic-auth.spec.ts:39  \n<a name=\"rejectWithChallenge\"></a>\n\n## rejectWithChallenge()\nMakes the mocked guard reject with the package's challenge.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/basic-auth.spec.ts:49  \n","symbols":3,"lastUsed":1795730447432},"tdata:packages/backend/src/basic-auth.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"logger","longname":"logger","name":"logger","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Logger for the basic-auth perimeter; one boot line, never per-request.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":9},"order":0,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/basic-auth.js:6","src":"packages/backend/src/basic-auth.ts:15"},"level":0},{"id":"REALM","longname":"REALM","name":"REALM","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Realm reported in the challenge emitted by the package's guard.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":13},"order":1,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/basic-auth.js:7","src":"packages/backend/src/basic-auth.ts:20"},"level":0},{"id":"STANDARD_HEADER_DISABLED","longname":"STANDARD_HEADER_DISABLED","name":"STANDARD_HEADER_DISABLED","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Empty header name. The guard reads `options.header ?? 'authorization'`, so an\nempty string makes it look up a header HTTP cannot carry. Standard\n`Authorization` stays ignored, which preserves the x-auth contract and leaves\nthe `/metrics` bearer token untouched.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":20},"order":2,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/basic-auth.js:8","src":"packages/backend/src/basic-auth.ts:28"},"level":0},{"id":"AUTH_CREDENTIALS","longname":"AUTH_CREDENTIALS","name":"AUTH_CREDENTIALS","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Credentials narrowed to required strings once the both-or-neither rule passes.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":24},"order":3,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/basic-auth.js:9","src":"packages/backend/src/basic-auth.ts:33"},"level":0},{"id":"isHealthPath","longname":"isHealthPath","name":"isHealthPath","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Whether the request targets the liveness probe. `/health` (with or without a\nquery string or trailing slash) is exempt from the perimeter so Docker\n`HEALTHCHECK` and orchestrator probes keep working without credentials.","params":[{"description":"The raw request URL, if available.","name":"url","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"True when the path is exactly `/health`.","type":{"names":["boolean"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":38},"order":4,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/basic-auth.js:16","src":"packages/backend/src/basic-auth.ts:48"},"level":0},{"id":"registerBasicAuth","longname":"registerBasicAuth","name":"registerBasicAuth","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Installs the package-backed perimeter on the Fastify instance.\n\nThe guard runs in an `onRequest` hook, ahead of body parsing and Nest\ninterceptors, so it also covers routes Fastify registers outside Nest, such\nas static dashboard assets, Swagger and unmatched URLs. `/health` stays public.\nNo-op (with a single boot warning) unless both credentials are configured.","params":[{"description":"The Fastify instance to decorate, passed by the bootstrap.","name":"instance","type":{"names":["FastifyInstance<import(\"fastify\").RawServerDefault, import(\"http\").IncomingMessage, import(\"http\").ServerResponse<import(\"http\").IncomingMessage>, import(\"fastify\").FastifyBaseLogger, import(\"fastify\").FastifyTypeProviderDefault>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":53},"order":5,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/basic-auth.js:22","src":"packages/backend/src/basic-auth.ts:63"},"returns":[{"type":{"names":["Promise<void>"]}}],"level":0},{"id":"createGuard","longname":"createGuard","name":"createGuard","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Builds the package guard from the configured pair once at boot.","params":[{"description":"The validated username and password pair.","name":"credentials","type":{"names":["{ name: string; pass: string; }"]}},{"description":"The configured username.","name":"credentials.name"},{"description":"The configured password.","name":"credentials.pass"}],"returns":[{"description":"The configured `BasicAuthGuard` instance.","type":{"names":["Promise<import(\"nest-basic-auth\").BasicAuthGuard>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":91},"async":true,"order":6,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/basic-auth.js:53","src":"packages/backend/src/basic-auth.ts:100"},"level":0},{"id":"hasCredentialPair","longname":"hasCredentialPair","name":"hasCredentialPair","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Whether the request supplied both x-auth headers. Used only to preserve the\nexact 401 body shape for a missing pair.","params":[{"description":"The incoming Fastify request.","name":"request","type":{"names":["FastifyRequest<import(\"fastify\").RouteGenericInterface, import(\"fastify\").RawServerDefault, import(\"http\").IncomingMessage, import(\"fastify\").FastifySchema, import(\"fastify\").FastifyTypeProviderDefault, unknown, import(\"fastify\").FastifyBaseLogger, import(\"fastify/types/type-provider.js\").ResolveFastifyRequestType<import(\"fastify\").FastifyTypeProviderDefault, import(\"fastify\").FastifySchema, import(\"fastify\").RouteGenericInterface>>"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"True when both header values are non-empty strings.","type":{"names":["boolean"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":109},"order":7,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/basic-auth.js:65","src":"packages/backend/src/basic-auth.ts:119"},"level":0},{"id":"isBasicAuthEnabled","longname":"isBasicAuthEnabled","name":"isBasicAuthEnabled","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Whether the perimeter is active. The environment schema enforces both-or-neither\nat boot, so a configured pair is always complete.","params":[],"returns":[{"description":"True when `AUTH_USERNAME` and `AUTH_PASSWORD` are both set.","type":{"names":["boolean"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":122},"order":8,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/basic-auth.js:73","src":"packages/backend/src/basic-auth.ts:135"},"level":0},{"id":"isBasicAuthPairComplete","longname":"isBasicAuthPairComplete","name":"isBasicAuthPairComplete","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Pure decision for the both-or-neither rule.","params":[{"description":"The configured `AUTH_USERNAME`, if any.","name":"username","type":{"names":["string"]}},{"description":"The configured `AUTH_PASSWORD`, if any.","name":"password","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"True when both are non-empty; false when both are absent; throws otherwise.","type":{"names":["boolean"]}}],"exceptions":[{"description":"Error Exactly one of the two credentials is set."}],"meta":{"lineno":132},"order":9,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/basic-auth.js:76","src":"packages/backend/src/basic-auth.ts:146"},"level":0},{"id":"readHeader","longname":"readHeader","name":"readHeader","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Reads a header the same way the package guard does, including its fallback to\nthe first value of a duplicated header.","params":[{"description":"The header value from Fastify.","name":"value","type":{"names":["string | string[]"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"A string value, or undefined when absent.","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":146},"order":10,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/basic-auth.js:84","src":"packages/backend/src/basic-auth.ts:166"},"level":0},{"id":"rejectRequest","longname":"rejectRequest","name":"rejectRequest","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Sends a 401 with the challenge set by the guard and the repo's existing body.","params":[{"description":"The Fastify reply to complete.","name":"reply","type":{"names":["FastifyReply<import(\"fastify\").RouteGenericInterface, import(\"fastify\").RawServerDefault, import(\"http\").IncomingMessage, import(\"http\").ServerResponse<import(\"http\").IncomingMessage>, unknown, import(\"fastify\").FastifySchema, import(\"fastify\").FastifyTypeProviderDefault, unknown>"]}},{"description":"Whether the request had no complete x-auth pair.","name":"isMissingPair","type":{"names":["boolean"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The sent reply.","type":{"names":["FastifyReply<import(\"fastify\").RouteGenericInterface, import(\"fastify\").RawServerDefault, import(\"http\").IncomingMessage, import(\"http\").ServerResponse<import(\"http\").IncomingMessage>, unknown, import(\"fastify\").FastifySchema, import(\"fastify\").FastifyTypeProviderDefault, unknown>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":155},"order":11,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/basic-auth.js:87","src":"packages/backend/src/basic-auth.ts:176"},"level":0},{"id":"scrubHostAuthEnvironment","longname":"scrubHostAuthEnvironment","name":"scrubHostAuthEnvironment","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Removes the host keys the package would append to explicit credentials and use\nfor its challenge. Pulled out of the module scope so importing this module has no\nglobal side effects; it runs before the package is dynamically imported.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":170},"order":12,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/basic-auth.js:97","src":"packages/backend/src/basic-auth.ts:192"},"level":0}],"fp":"6af66f0e56e25728e9890d4eb6d51ed39dbcdce0702b4427ddaa8ad473daa6ef","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","symbols":0,"lastUsed":1795730447793},"md:packages/backend/src/basic-auth.ts":{"fp":"07224e0b10b97c9df34db4d390f211f49c219eb6674b1c11207d28222955fd49","issues":[],"kind":"md","markdown":"## Constants\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#logger\">logger</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Logger for the basic-auth perimeter; one boot line, never per-request.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#REALM\">REALM</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Realm reported in the challenge emitted by the package&#39;s guard.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#STANDARD_HEADER_DISABLED\">STANDARD_HEADER_DISABLED</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Empty header name. The guard reads <code>options.header ?? &#39;authorization&#39;</code>, so an\nempty string makes it look up a header HTTP cannot carry. Standard\n<code>Authorization</code> stays ignored, which preserves the x-auth contract and leaves\nthe <code>/metrics</code> bearer token untouched.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#AUTH_CREDENTIALS\">AUTH_CREDENTIALS</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Credentials narrowed to required strings once the both-or-neither rule passes.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n## Functions\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#isHealthPath\">isHealthPath(url)</a> ⇒ <code>boolean</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Whether the request targets the liveness probe. <code>/health</code> (with or without a\nquery string or trailing slash) is exempt from the perimeter so Docker\n<code>HEALTHCHECK</code> and orchestrator probes keep working without credentials.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#registerBasicAuth\">registerBasicAuth(instance)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Installs the package-backed perimeter on the Fastify instance.</p>\n<p>The guard runs in an <code>onRequest</code> hook, ahead of body parsing and Nest\ninterceptors, so it also covers routes Fastify registers outside Nest, such\nas static dashboard assets, Swagger and unmatched URLs. <code>/health</code> stays public.\nNo-op (with a single boot warning) unless both credentials are configured.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#createGuard\">createGuard(credentials)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;import(&quot;nest-basic-auth&quot;).BasicAuthGuard&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Builds the package guard from the configured pair once at boot.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#hasCredentialPair\">hasCredentialPair(request)</a> ⇒ <code>boolean</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Whether the request supplied both x-auth headers. Used only to preserve the\nexact 401 body shape for a missing pair.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#isBasicAuthEnabled\">isBasicAuthEnabled()</a> ⇒ <code>boolean</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Whether the perimeter is active. The environment schema enforces both-or-neither\nat boot, so a configured pair is always complete.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#isBasicAuthPairComplete\">isBasicAuthPairComplete(username, password)</a> ⇒ <code>boolean</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Pure decision for the both-or-neither rule.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#readHeader\">readHeader(value)</a> ⇒ <code>string</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Reads a header the same way the package guard does, including its fallback to\nthe first value of a duplicated header.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#rejectRequest\">rejectRequest(reply, isMissingPair)</a> ⇒ <code>FastifyReply&lt;import(&quot;fastify&quot;).RouteGenericInterface, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).RawServerDefault, import(&quot;http&quot;).IncomingMessage, import(&quot;http&quot;).ServerResponse&lt;import(&quot;http&quot;).IncomingMessage&gt;, unknown, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).FastifySchema, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).FastifyTypeProviderDefault, unknown&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Sends a 401 with the challenge set by the guard and the repo&#39;s existing body.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#scrubHostAuthEnvironment\">scrubHostAuthEnvironment()</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Removes the host keys the package would append to explicit credentials and use\nfor its challenge. Pulled out of the module scope so importing this module has no\nglobal side effects; it runs before the package is dynamically imported.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"logger\"></a>\n\n## logger\nLogger for the basic-auth perimeter; one boot line, never per-request.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/basic-auth.ts:15  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/basic-auth.js:6\n<a name=\"REALM\"></a>\n\n## REALM\nRealm reported in the challenge emitted by the package's guard.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/basic-auth.ts:20  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/basic-auth.js:7\n<a name=\"STANDARD_HEADER_DISABLED\"></a>\n\n## STANDARD\\_HEADER\\_DISABLED\nEmpty header name. The guard reads `options.header ?? 'authorization'`, so an\nempty string makes it look up a header HTTP cannot carry. Standard\n`Authorization` stays ignored, which preserves the x-auth contract and leaves\nthe `/metrics` bearer token untouched.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/basic-auth.ts:28  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/basic-auth.js:8\n<a name=\"AUTH_CREDENTIALS\"></a>\n\n## AUTH\\_CREDENTIALS\nCredentials narrowed to required strings once the both-or-neither rule passes.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/basic-auth.ts:33  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/basic-auth.js:9\n<a name=\"isHealthPath\"></a>\n\n## isHealthPath(url) ⇒ <code>boolean</code>\nWhether the request targets the liveness probe. `/health` (with or without a\nquery string or trailing slash) is exempt from the perimeter so Docker\n`HEALTHCHECK` and orchestrator probes keep working without credentials.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>boolean</code> - True when the path is exactly `/health`.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| url | <code>string</code> | The raw request URL, if available. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/basic-auth.ts:48  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/basic-auth.js:16\n<a name=\"registerBasicAuth\"></a>\n\n## registerBasicAuth(instance) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code>\nInstalls the package-backed perimeter on the Fastify instance.\n\nThe guard runs in an `onRequest` hook, ahead of body parsing and Nest\ninterceptors, so it also covers routes Fastify registers outside Nest, such\nas static dashboard assets, Swagger and unmatched URLs. `/health` stays public.\nNo-op (with a single boot warning) unless both credentials are configured.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| instance | <code>FastifyInstance&lt;import(&quot;fastify&quot;).RawServerDefault, import(&quot;http&quot;).IncomingMessage, import(&quot;http&quot;).ServerResponse&lt;import(&quot;http&quot;).IncomingMessage&gt;, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).FastifyBaseLogger, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).FastifyTypeProviderDefault&gt;</code> | The Fastify instance to decorate, passed by the bootstrap. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/basic-auth.ts:63  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/basic-auth.js:22\n<a name=\"createGuard\"></a>\n\n## createGuard(credentials) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;import(&quot;nest-basic-auth&quot;).BasicAuthGuard&gt;</code>\nBuilds the package guard from the configured pair once at boot.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;import(&quot;nest-basic-auth&quot;).BasicAuthGuard&gt;</code> - The configured `BasicAuthGuard` instance.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| credentials | <code>{ name: string; pass: string; }</code> | The validated username and password pair. |\n| credentials.name |  | The configured username. |\n| credentials.pass |  | The configured password. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/basic-auth.ts:100  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/basic-auth.js:53\n<a name=\"hasCredentialPair\"></a>\n\n## hasCredentialPair(request) ⇒ <code>boolean</code>\nWhether the request supplied both x-auth headers. Used only to preserve the\nexact 401 body shape for a missing pair.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>boolean</code> - True when both header values are non-empty strings.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| request | <code>FastifyRequest&lt;import(&quot;fastify&quot;).RouteGenericInterface, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).RawServerDefault, import(&quot;http&quot;).IncomingMessage, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).FastifySchema, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).FastifyTypeProviderDefault, unknown, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).FastifyBaseLogger, import(&quot;fastify/types/type-provider.js&quot;).ResolveFastifyRequestType&lt;import(&quot;fastify&quot;).FastifyTypeProviderDefault, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).FastifySchema, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).RouteGenericInterface&gt;&gt;</code> | The incoming Fastify request. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/basic-auth.ts:119  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/basic-auth.js:65\n<a name=\"isBasicAuthEnabled\"></a>\n\n## isBasicAuthEnabled() ⇒ <code>boolean</code>\nWhether the perimeter is active. The environment schema enforces both-or-neither\nat boot, so a configured pair is always complete.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>boolean</code> - True when `AUTH_USERNAME` and `AUTH_PASSWORD` are both set.  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/basic-auth.ts:135  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/basic-auth.js:73\n<a name=\"isBasicAuthPairComplete\"></a>\n\n## isBasicAuthPairComplete(username, password) ⇒ <code>boolean</code>\nPure decision for the both-or-neither rule.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>boolean</code> - True when both are non-empty; false when both are absent; throws otherwise.  \n**Throws**:\n\n- Error Exactly one of the two credentials is set.\n\n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| username | <code>string</code> | The configured `AUTH_USERNAME`, if any. |\n| password | <code>string</code> | The configured `AUTH_PASSWORD`, if any. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/basic-auth.ts:146  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/basic-auth.js:76\n<a name=\"readHeader\"></a>\n\n## readHeader(value) ⇒ <code>string</code>\nReads a header the same way the package guard does, including its fallback to\nthe first value of a duplicated header.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>string</code> - A string value, or undefined when absent.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| value | <code>string \\| string[]</code> | The header value from Fastify. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/basic-auth.ts:166  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/basic-auth.js:84\n<a name=\"rejectRequest\"></a>\n\n## rejectRequest(reply, isMissingPair) ⇒ <code>FastifyReply&lt;import(&quot;fastify&quot;).RouteGenericInterface, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).RawServerDefault, import(&quot;http&quot;).IncomingMessage, import(&quot;http&quot;).ServerResponse&lt;import(&quot;http&quot;).IncomingMessage&gt;, unknown, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).FastifySchema, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).FastifyTypeProviderDefault, unknown&gt;</code>\nSends a 401 with the challenge set by the guard and the repo's existing body.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>FastifyReply&lt;import(&quot;fastify&quot;).RouteGenericInterface, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).RawServerDefault, import(&quot;http&quot;).IncomingMessage, import(&quot;http&quot;).ServerResponse&lt;import(&quot;http&quot;).IncomingMessage&gt;, unknown, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).FastifySchema, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).FastifyTypeProviderDefault, unknown&gt;</code> - The sent reply.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| reply | <code>FastifyReply&lt;import(&quot;fastify&quot;).RouteGenericInterface, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).RawServerDefault, import(&quot;http&quot;).IncomingMessage, import(&quot;http&quot;).ServerResponse&lt;import(&quot;http&quot;).IncomingMessage&gt;, unknown, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).FastifySchema, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).FastifyTypeProviderDefault, unknown&gt;</code> | The Fastify reply to complete. |\n| isMissingPair | <code>boolean</code> | Whether the request had no complete x-auth pair. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/basic-auth.ts:176  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/basic-auth.js:87\n<a name=\"scrubHostAuthEnvironment\"></a>\n\n## scrubHostAuthEnvironment()\nRemoves the host keys the package would append to explicit credentials and use\nfor its challenge. Pulled out of the module scope so importing this module has no\nglobal side effects; it runs before the package is dynamically imported.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/basic-auth.ts:192  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/basic-auth.js:97\n","symbols":13,"lastUsed":1795730447945},"tdata:packages/backend/src/bootstrap.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"configureFastify","longname":"configureFastify","name":"configureFastify","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Configures the Fastify instance with everything the app needs at the HTTP\nedge, shared by the production bootstrap (`main.ts`) and the e2e harness\n(`test/helpers.ts`) so the two can never drift:\n\n- the media content-type parsers that accept uploads as raw streams,\n- the basic-auth perimeter (a no-op unless both credentials are configured).","params":[{"description":"The Fastify instance to configure.","name":"instance","type":{"names":["FastifyInstance<import(\"fastify\").RawServerDefault, import(\"http\").IncomingMessage, import(\"http\").ServerResponse<import(\"http\").IncomingMessage>, import(\"fastify\").FastifyBaseLogger, import(\"fastify\").FastifyTypeProviderDefault>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":13},"order":0,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/bootstrap.js:4","src":"packages/backend/src/bootstrap.ts:18"},"returns":[{"type":{"names":["Promise<void>"]}}],"level":0}],"fp":"febacbd168e403a8220d87964dfbd45c147b7af3ab3a81deae8682732b8aa3b5","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730447469,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/bootstrap.ts":{"fp":"4912a43890d60cf67c574afd5b3f53f5ef27caebd2e9ec9d126d70023132051d","issues":[],"kind":"md","markdown":"<a name=\"configureFastify\"></a>\n\n## configureFastify(instance) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code>\nConfigures the Fastify instance with everything the app needs at the HTTP\nedge, shared by the production bootstrap (`main.ts`) and the e2e harness\n(`test/helpers.ts`) so the two can never drift:\n\n- the media content-type parsers that accept uploads as raw streams,\n- the basic-auth perimeter (a no-op unless both credentials are configured).\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| instance | <code>FastifyInstance&lt;import(&quot;fastify&quot;).RawServerDefault, import(&quot;http&quot;).IncomingMessage, import(&quot;http&quot;).ServerResponse&lt;import(&quot;http&quot;).IncomingMessage&gt;, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).FastifyBaseLogger, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).FastifyTypeProviderDefault&gt;</code> | The Fastify instance to configure. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/bootstrap.ts:18  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/bootstrap.js:4\n","symbols":1,"lastUsed":1795730447503},"tdata:packages/backend/src/app.tracing.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"traceEndpoint","longname":"traceEndpoint","name":"traceEndpoint","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"The OTLP/HTTP traces endpoint. Prefers `OTEL_TRACE_EXPORTER_URL`, falls back\nto the standard `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_ENDPOINT`. When neither is set,\ntelemetry stays disabled entirely (the SDK is never constructed, so nothing\nbinds the metrics port and e2e/unit boots emit nothing).","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":18},"order":0,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/app.tracing.js:12","src":"packages/backend/src/app.tracing.ts:27"},"level":0},{"id":"isOtelTracingEnabled","longname":"isOtelTracingEnabled","name":"isOtelTracingEnabled","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Whether OpenTelemetry starts on boot. Endpoint-gated, never implicit.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":23},"order":1,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/app.tracing.js:14","src":"packages/backend/src/app.tracing.ts:34"},"level":0},{"id":"otelSDK","longname":"otelSDK","name":"otelSDK","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"The process-wide OpenTelemetry SDK, shaped like the reference Fastify\nsetup: W3C + B3 + baggage propagation, batching OTLP exporter, host metrics\non the Prometheus exporter and auto-instrumented HTTP / Nest / pino /\nundici traffic. Constructed only when telemetry is enabled (the Prometheus\nexporter binds its port in its constructor) — start it before\n`NestFactory.create` so Fastify's plugin registration is captured; see\n`main.ts`.","meta":{"lineno":35},"order":2,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/app.tracing.js:17","src":"packages/backend/src/app.tracing.ts:49"},"level":0}],"fp":"f6b76660dc6e60df510cd9b7696b71132805cad19951d54fc4f8587d5696ee0d","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730447133,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/app.tracing.ts":{"fp":"ee22e20149ad17fc03bc2b9633fbc899f9e691ffa30ccd9435f8e286ad036cc6","issues":[],"kind":"md","markdown":"## Constants\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#traceEndpoint\">traceEndpoint</a></dt>\n<dd><p>The OTLP/HTTP traces endpoint. Prefers <code>OTEL_TRACE_EXPORTER_URL</code>, falls back\nto the standard <code>OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_ENDPOINT</code>. When neither is set,\ntelemetry stays disabled entirely (the SDK is never constructed, so nothing\nbinds the metrics port and e2e/unit boots emit nothing).</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#isOtelTracingEnabled\">isOtelTracingEnabled</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Whether OpenTelemetry starts on boot. Endpoint-gated, never implicit.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#otelSDK\">otelSDK</a></dt>\n<dd><p>The process-wide OpenTelemetry SDK, shaped like the reference Fastify\nsetup: W3C + B3 + baggage propagation, batching OTLP exporter, host metrics\non the Prometheus exporter and auto-instrumented HTTP / Nest / pino /\nundici traffic. Constructed only when telemetry is enabled (the Prometheus\nexporter binds its port in its constructor) — start it before\n<code>NestFactory.create</code> so Fastify&#39;s plugin registration is captured; see\n<code>main.ts</code>.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"traceEndpoint\"></a>\n\n## traceEndpoint\nThe OTLP/HTTP traces endpoint. Prefers `OTEL_TRACE_EXPORTER_URL`, falls back\nto the standard `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_ENDPOINT`. When neither is set,\ntelemetry stays disabled entirely (the SDK is never constructed, so nothing\nbinds the metrics port and e2e/unit boots emit nothing).\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/app.tracing.ts:27  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/app.tracing.js:12\n<a name=\"isOtelTracingEnabled\"></a>\n\n## isOtelTracingEnabled\nWhether OpenTelemetry starts on boot. Endpoint-gated, never implicit.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/app.tracing.ts:34  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/app.tracing.js:14\n<a name=\"otelSDK\"></a>\n\n## otelSDK\nThe process-wide OpenTelemetry SDK, shaped like the reference Fastify\nsetup: W3C + B3 + baggage propagation, batching OTLP exporter, host metrics\non the Prometheus exporter and auto-instrumented HTTP / Nest / pino /\nundici traffic. Constructed only when telemetry is enabled (the Prometheus\nexporter binds its port in its constructor) — start it before\n`NestFactory.create` so Fastify's plugin registration is captured; see\n`main.ts`.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/app.tracing.ts:49  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/app.tracing.js:17\n","symbols":3,"lastUsed":1795730447359},"tdata:packages/dashboard/src/telemetry.spec.ts":{"doclets":[],"fp":"f86d102aa266ab69724b0a231377149b9268939790081574993c5963b102b8cd","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730471968,"symbols":0},"md:packages/dashboard/src/telemetry.spec.ts":{"fp":"9dace26e8a86cf06ab8a080a8fef97b95ed504dd398dda923d93b17e6c0576a2","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","skipped":"no-jsdoc","symbols":0,"lastUsed":1795730471968},"tdata:packages/dashboard/src/telemetry.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"isTelemetryEnabled","longname":"isTelemetryEnabled","name":"isTelemetryEnabled","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Whether browser telemetry should start. Pure function over the build-time\nenvironment so it can be unit-tested without loading the SDK: enabled only\nin production builds with `VITE_OTEL_OTLP_ENDPOINT` set.","params":[{"description":"The Vite environment record (`import.meta.env`).","name":"environment","type":{"names":["Record<string, unknown>"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"True when the production build declares an OTLP endpoint.","type":{"names":["boolean"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":21},"order":0,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/dashboard/src/telemetry.ts:30"},"level":0}],"fp":"a619927d0f57ea2fa65495e2ab88164029e9ae189e0a970c3afb9a15052e8f82","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730471968,"symbols":0},"md:packages/dashboard/src/telemetry.ts":{"fp":"d2f1cabc2565d7cc217516882aa1e738d3a5002897cd3908751b18fde7edc44e","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","markdown":"<a name=\"isTelemetryEnabled\"></a>\n\n## isTelemetryEnabled(environment) ⇒ <code>boolean</code>\nWhether browser telemetry should start. Pure function over the build-time\nenvironment so it can be unit-tested without loading the SDK: enabled only\nin production builds with `VITE_OTEL_OTLP_ENDPOINT` set.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>boolean</code> - True when the production build declares an OTLP endpoint.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| environment | <code>Record&lt;string, unknown&gt;</code> | The Vite environment record (`import.meta.env`). |\n\nsrc: packages/dashboard/src/telemetry.ts:30  \n","symbols":1,"lastUsed":1795730471990},"tdata:packages/backend/src/utils/worker-exit.spec.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"WORKER_EXIT_API_SURFACE","longname":"WORKER_EXIT_API_SURFACE","name":"WORKER_EXIT_API_SURFACE","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Named symbol for the mdaics docs site (see https://github.com/rayenboussayed/mdaics); no runtime use.","meta":{"lineno":56},"order":0,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/backend/src/utils/worker-exit.spec.ts:75"},"level":0}],"fp":"d2821b6a83704f3dc07fc193d0c8cdb8438755532a24a2be3f9f94ec7f7a1618","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730471313,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/utils/worker-exit.spec.ts":{"fp":"6976413bbd8ee4f11407ef3332de08c8b2f5b1fbe0ad39a6d0a42a93b4fe8984","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","markdown":"<a name=\"WORKER_EXIT_API_SURFACE\"></a>\n\n## WORKER\\_EXIT\\_API\\_SURFACE\nNamed symbol for the mdaics docs site (see https://github.com/rayenboussayed/mdaics); no runtime use.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/utils/worker-exit.spec.ts:75  \n","symbols":1,"lastUsed":1795730471363},"tdata:packages/backend/src/utils/worker-exit.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"exitWorker","longname":"exitWorker","name":"exitWorker","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Ends a worker process after its job finishes. Dropping stdin lets the event\nloop drain on its own; the timer is a backstop for native media handles that\noutlive the drain. The timer is unref'd, so it never holds the process open.","params":[{"description":"Exit code for the worker process.","name":"code","type":{"names":["number"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":7},"order":0,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/utils/worker-exit.js:1","src":"packages/backend/src/utils/worker-exit.ts:7"},"level":0},{"id":"standaloneExit","longname":"standaloneExit","name":"standaloneExit","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Exits the worker thread when it is running standalone; a no-op otherwise.\nThe guard reads `FILE_FLY_WORKER` at call time: WorkerService sets it to\n\"1\" before spawning, while unit specs import the module in-process with the\nvariable unset.","params":[{"description":"Exit code for the worker process.","name":"code","type":{"names":["number"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":23},"order":1,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/utils/worker-exit.js:7","src":"packages/backend/src/utils/worker-exit.ts:24"},"level":0}],"fp":"6fb0cb41204b8ac181360204fcd601ed064566d3989a9d70d5d3d9e6e4f23bd2","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730471344,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/utils/worker-exit.ts":{"fp":"2d72c74d35abba6b70abca42c38b5642ae24f8a0081da102e664dcd5e240f453","issues":[],"kind":"md","markdown":"## Functions\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#exitWorker\">exitWorker(code)</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Ends a worker process after its job finishes. Dropping stdin lets the event\nloop drain on its own; the timer is a backstop for native media handles that\noutlive the drain. The timer is unref&#39;d, so it never holds the process open.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#standaloneExit\">standaloneExit(code)</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Exits the worker thread when it is running standalone; a no-op otherwise.\nThe guard reads <code>FILE_FLY_WORKER</code> at call time: WorkerService sets it to\n&quot;1&quot; before spawning, while unit specs import the module in-process with the\nvariable unset.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"exitWorker\"></a>\n\n## exitWorker(code)\nEnds a worker process after its job finishes. Dropping stdin lets the event\nloop drain on its own; the timer is a backstop for native media handles that\noutlive the drain. The timer is unref'd, so it never holds the process open.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| code | <code>number</code> | Exit code for the worker process. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/utils/worker-exit.ts:7  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/utils/worker-exit.js:1\n<a name=\"standaloneExit\"></a>\n\n## standaloneExit(code)\nExits the worker thread when it is running standalone; a no-op otherwise.\nThe guard reads `FILE_FLY_WORKER` at call time: WorkerService sets it to\n\"1\" before spawning, while unit specs import the module in-process with the\nvariable unset.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| code | <code>number</code> | Exit code for the worker process. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/utils/worker-exit.ts:24  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/utils/worker-exit.js:7\n","symbols":2,"lastUsed":1795730471397},"tdata:packages/backend/src/cors.spec.ts":{"doclets":[],"fp":"b5244c2124fa0f2a0ff121d278e6c64a3142b992db3fb0a547266a9d6d1254a6","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730447564,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/cors.spec.ts":{"fp":"2688981ec0424d4548cc3799292bc30c6920d241daec2571c7391015d711004d","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","skipped":"no-jsdoc","symbols":0,"lastUsed":1795730447564},"tdata:packages/backend/src/cors.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"allowedCorsHeaders","longname":"allowedCorsHeaders","name":"allowedCorsHeaders","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Request headers a cross-origin client may send beyond the CORS-safelisted set.\nThe auth pair is included so a separately hosted client can pass the basic-auth\nperimeter; content-type serves the JSON build routes and the file hash the\nupload cache hint. The W3C trace headers keep cross-origin telemetry working\nas documented in the README.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":9},"order":0,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/cors.js:2","src":"packages/backend/src/cors.ts:10"},"level":0},{"id":"buildCorsOptions","longname":"buildCorsOptions","name":"buildCorsOptions","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Builds the production CORS options.","params":[{"description":"Configured CORS_ORIGIN values; undefined disables cross-origin reads.","name":"origins","type":{"names":["string[]"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The enableCors options object, with an explicit request-header allowlist.","type":{"names":["{ allowedHeaders: any[]; credentials: boolean; exposedHeaders: any[]; origin: boolean | string[]; }"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":24},"order":1,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/cors.js:12","src":"packages/backend/src/cors.ts:26"},"level":0}],"fp":"5491846eb9e684f803ed486994092a497d1a9b283e4a2d465a74f9237f655ece","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730447628,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/cors.ts":{"fp":"e98594da38693226b80b990b795d174834bdf8325adf8a4993393c1c8749edd5","issues":[],"kind":"md","markdown":"## Constants\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#allowedCorsHeaders\">allowedCorsHeaders</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Request headers a cross-origin client may send beyond the CORS-safelisted set.\nThe auth pair is included so a separately hosted client can pass the basic-auth\nperimeter; content-type serves the JSON build routes and the file hash the\nupload cache hint. The W3C trace headers keep cross-origin telemetry working\nas documented in the README.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n## Functions\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#buildCorsOptions\">buildCorsOptions(origins)</a> ⇒ <code>{ allowedHeaders: any[]; credentials: boolean; exposedHeaders: any[]; origin: boolean | string[]; }</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Builds the production CORS options.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"allowedCorsHeaders\"></a>\n\n## allowedCorsHeaders\nRequest headers a cross-origin client may send beyond the CORS-safelisted set.\nThe auth pair is included so a separately hosted client can pass the basic-auth\nperimeter; content-type serves the JSON build routes and the file hash the\nupload cache hint. The W3C trace headers keep cross-origin telemetry working\nas documented in the README.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/cors.ts:10  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/cors.js:2\n<a name=\"buildCorsOptions\"></a>\n\n## buildCorsOptions(origins) ⇒ <code>{ allowedHeaders: any[]; credentials: boolean; exposedHeaders: any[]; origin: boolean \\| string[]; }</code>\nBuilds the production CORS options.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>{ allowedHeaders: any[]; credentials: boolean; exposedHeaders: any[]; origin: boolean \\| string[]; }</code> - The enableCors options object, with an explicit request-header allowlist.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| origins | <code>string[]</code> | Configured CORS_ORIGIN values; undefined disables cross-origin reads. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/cors.ts:26  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/cors.js:12\n","symbols":2,"lastUsed":1795730447671},"tdata:packages/backend/src/interceptors/pipeline.decorator.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"UseMediaPipeline","longname":"UseMediaPipeline","name":"UseMediaPipeline","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Applies the scan and parse gates used by media routes, with an optional\nsignature gate that enforces the accepted input formats.","params":[{"description":"Resource-specific signature interceptor, when one exists.","name":"signature","type":{"names":["Type<NestInterceptor<unknown, unknown>>"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The composed interceptor decorator.","type":{"names":["MethodDecorator & ClassDecorator"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":10},"order":0,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/interceptors/pipeline.decorator.js:4","src":"packages/backend/src/interceptors/pipeline.decorator.ts:12"},"level":0},{"id":"UseScanPipeline","longname":"UseScanPipeline","name":"UseScanPipeline","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Applies the scan gate used by document routes, which carry a JSON body and\nneed no signature probe.","returns":[{"description":"The composed interceptor decorator.","type":{"names":["MethodDecorator & ClassDecorator"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":24},"order":1,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/interceptors/pipeline.decorator.js:13","src":"packages/backend/src/interceptors/pipeline.decorator.ts:26"},"level":0}],"fp":"d7cda76306e6aec9fe30ff13ccffd96fafce06137d61042f062b0d154628639c","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730447963,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/interceptors/pipeline.decorator.ts":{"fp":"781dc1d41af6e139f598ce8928a50348e856e14d52a2893966880d8a47502cd9","issues":[],"kind":"md","markdown":"## Functions\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#UseMediaPipeline\">UseMediaPipeline(signature)</a> ⇒ <code>MethodDecorator &amp; ClassDecorator</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Applies the scan and parse gates used by media routes, with an optional\nsignature gate that enforces the accepted input formats.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#UseScanPipeline\">UseScanPipeline()</a> ⇒ <code>MethodDecorator &amp; ClassDecorator</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Applies the scan gate used by document routes, which carry a JSON body and\nneed no signature probe.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"UseMediaPipeline\"></a>\n\n## UseMediaPipeline(signature) ⇒ <code>MethodDecorator &amp; ClassDecorator</code>\nApplies the scan and parse gates used by media routes, with an optional\nsignature gate that enforces the accepted input formats.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>MethodDecorator &amp; ClassDecorator</code> - The composed interceptor decorator.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| signature | <code>Type&lt;NestInterceptor&lt;unknown, unknown&gt;&gt;</code> | Resource-specific signature interceptor, when one exists. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/interceptors/pipeline.decorator.ts:12  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/interceptors/pipeline.decorator.js:4\n<a name=\"UseScanPipeline\"></a>\n\n## UseScanPipeline() ⇒ <code>MethodDecorator &amp; ClassDecorator</code>\nApplies the scan gate used by document routes, which carry a JSON body and\nneed no signature probe.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>MethodDecorator &amp; ClassDecorator</code> - The composed interceptor decorator.  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/interceptors/pipeline.decorator.ts:26  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/interceptors/pipeline.decorator.js:13\n","symbols":2,"lastUsed":1795730448040},"tdata:packages/backend/src/shared-services.module.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"SharedServicesModule","longname":"SharedServicesModule","name":"SharedServicesModule","kind":"member","scope":"global","description":"Provides the request-agnostic services every feature module needs once. The\nClamAV client is memoized per process and CLS access is request-scoped, so a\nsingle instance serves all features. WorkerService stays per-feature: it owns\na worker-concurrency budget and an in-flight map that must not be shared.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":45},"order":0,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/shared-services.module.js:11","src":"packages/backend/src/shared-services.module.ts:18"},"level":0}],"fp":"840c4d101ec174aaca4826f3f177b4dfa2d0dd78783bc02cf3533f3f36404cd6","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730470654,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/shared-services.module.ts":{"fp":"352c5f75eb7d10cfa201e17edcff44da551eb3c47aada6e05cf9c055fb160ea2","issues":[],"kind":"md","markdown":"<a name=\"SharedServicesModule\"></a>\n\n## SharedServicesModule\nProvides the request-agnostic services every feature module needs once. The\nClamAV client is memoized per process and CLS access is request-scoped, so a\nsingle instance serves all features. WorkerService stays per-feature: it owns\na worker-concurrency budget and an in-flight map that must not be shared.\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/shared-services.module.ts:18  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/shared-services.module.js:11\n","symbols":1,"lastUsed":1795730470708},"tdata:packages/backend/src/interceptors/pipeline.decorator.spec.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"reflect","longname":"reflect","name":"reflect","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Reads the interceptor metadata Nest stores on a decorated class.","params":[{"description":"The decorated class.","name":"target"}],"returns":[{"description":"The interceptors in registration order."}],"meta":{"lineno":17},"order":0,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/backend/src/interceptors/pipeline.decorator.spec.ts:22"},"level":0}],"fp":"dcdbf33fa0a9f44b4436470031d69adbb38b44703b30f9f9c75bcc29242c3a7c","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730447960,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/interceptors/pipeline.decorator.spec.ts":{"fp":"52602507e0134f0e06c2dac7840fc90b01841897ae5218d59f0382e3ea6192cb","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","markdown":"<a name=\"reflect\"></a>\n\n## reflect ⇒\nReads the interceptor metadata Nest stores on a decorated class.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \n**Returns**: The interceptors in registration order.  \n\n| Param | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| target | The decorated class. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/interceptors/pipeline.decorator.spec.ts:22  \n","symbols":1,"lastUsed":1795730447984},"tdata:packages/backend/src/shared-services.module.spec.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"reflect","longname":"reflect","name":"reflect","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Reads Nest's module metadata.","params":[{"description":"Metadata key to read from the module class.","name":"key"}],"returns":[{"description":"The stored value, or undefined when the key is absent."}],"meta":{"lineno":12},"order":0,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/backend/src/shared-services.module.spec.ts:15"},"level":0}],"fp":"b5fb8d208cd1b6bccde78404b4fe2ba22591d2be29d12df4eea26fa93ecdd940","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730470622,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/shared-services.module.spec.ts":{"fp":"0cc9a3cad9591a23198bc201be92833050a58568d830852efdfae163fb648e18","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","markdown":"<a name=\"reflect\"></a>\n\n## reflect ⇒\nReads Nest's module metadata.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \n**Returns**: The stored value, or undefined when the key is absent.  \n\n| Param | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| key | Metadata key to read from the module class. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/shared-services.module.spec.ts:15  \n","symbols":1,"lastUsed":1795730470648},"tdata:packages/dashboard/src/lib/metrics-query.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"useMetricsQuery","longname":"useMetricsQuery","name":"useMetricsQuery","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Polls the `/metrics` feed shared by every dashboard page.\n\nThe query key, five-second interval and background refresh mirror the previous\nper-page configuration. Retry stays disabled here, as the global QueryClient\nalready sets the same default; the next poll is the retry.","returns":[{"description":"The TanStack Query result for the metrics snapshot.","type":{"names":["import(\"@tanstack/react-query\").UseQueryResult<{ generatedAt: string; inFlight: number; last24h: { bucket: string; bytesIn: number; bytesOut: number; errors: number; requests: number; }[]; metricsDisabled: boolean; perIp: { [x: string]: unknown; bytesIn: number; bytesOut: number; filesIn: number; filesOut: number; ip: string; requests: number; }[]; perRoute: { [x: string]: unknown; avgMs: number; bytesOut: number; errors: number; p50: number; p95: number; p99: number; requests: number; route: string; }[]; today: { avgMs: number; bytesIn: number; bytesOut: number; cacheHitRate: number; cacheHits: number; cacheMisses: number; clientErrors: number; filesIn: number; filesOut: number; requests: number; scanBlocked: number; scanClean: number; scanInfected: number; serverErrors: number; }; totals: { avgMs: number; bytesIn: number; bytesOut: number; cacheHitRate: number; cacheHits: number; cacheMisses: number; clientErrors: number; filesIn: number; filesOut: number; requests: number; scanBlocked: number; scanClean: number; scanInfected: number; serverErrors: number; }; uptimeSeconds: number; }, Error>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":11},"order":0,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/dashboard/src/lib/metrics-query.ts:13"},"level":0}],"fp":"36af0581de875e23033a4919b85aa3f896708247cfd52a61bd511eb26a532e16","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730471809,"symbols":0},"md:packages/dashboard/src/lib/metrics-query.ts":{"fp":"11412278f1bff285ddc5770659051e8650df50c32556641015a8a798c6a279a7","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","markdown":"<a name=\"useMetricsQuery\"></a>\n\n## useMetricsQuery() ⇒ <code>import(&quot;@tanstack/react-query&quot;).UseQueryResult&lt;{ generatedAt: string; inFlight: number; last24h: { bucket: string; bytesIn: number; bytesOut: number; errors: number; requests: number; }[]; metricsDisabled: boolean; perIp: { [x: string]: unknown; bytesIn: number; bytesOut: number; filesIn: number; filesOut: number; ip: string; requests: number; }[]; perRoute: { [x: string]: unknown; avgMs: number; bytesOut: number; errors: number; p50: number; p95: number; p99: number; requests: number; route: string; }[]; today: { avgMs: number; bytesIn: number; bytesOut: number; cacheHitRate: number; cacheHits: number; cacheMisses: number; clientErrors: number; filesIn: number; filesOut: number; requests: number; scanBlocked: number; scanClean: number; scanInfected: number; serverErrors: number; }; totals: { avgMs: number; bytesIn: number; bytesOut: number; cacheHitRate: number; cacheHits: number; cacheMisses: number; clientErrors: number; filesIn: number; filesOut: number; requests: number; scanBlocked: number; scanClean: number; scanInfected: number; serverErrors: number; }; uptimeSeconds: number; }, Error&gt;</code>\nPolls the `/metrics` feed shared by every dashboard page.\n\nThe query key, five-second interval and background refresh mirror the previous\nper-page configuration. Retry stays disabled here, as the global QueryClient\nalready sets the same default; the next poll is the retry.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>import(&quot;@tanstack/react-query&quot;).UseQueryResult&lt;{ generatedAt: string; inFlight: number; last24h: { bucket: string; bytesIn: number; bytesOut: number; errors: number; requests: number; }[]; metricsDisabled: boolean; perIp: { [x: string]: unknown; bytesIn: number; bytesOut: number; filesIn: number; filesOut: number; ip: string; requests: number; }[]; perRoute: { [x: string]: unknown; avgMs: number; bytesOut: number; errors: number; p50: number; p95: number; p99: number; requests: number; route: string; }[]; today: { avgMs: number; bytesIn: number; bytesOut: number; cacheHitRate: number; cacheHits: number; cacheMisses: number; clientErrors: number; filesIn: number; filesOut: number; requests: number; scanBlocked: number; scanClean: number; scanInfected: number; serverErrors: number; }; totals: { avgMs: number; bytesIn: number; bytesOut: number; cacheHitRate: number; cacheHits: number; cacheMisses: number; clientErrors: number; filesIn: number; filesOut: number; requests: number; scanBlocked: number; scanClean: number; scanInfected: number; serverErrors: number; }; uptimeSeconds: number; }, Error&gt;</code> - The TanStack Query result for the metrics snapshot.  \nsrc: packages/dashboard/src/lib/metrics-query.ts:13  \n","symbols":1,"lastUsed":1795730471872},"tdata:packages/dashboard/src/lib/metrics-query.spec.ts":{"doclets":[],"fp":"1283ecbaa8f062970d3d472cf889ecb9118620e66d49edd5e87a905b159d0161","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730471808,"symbols":0},"md:packages/dashboard/src/lib/metrics-query.spec.ts":{"fp":"ee585bcc1b37c25c3fca450cdd7444f66a3b72dda5824cb648db53be45bbe5de","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","skipped":"no-jsdoc","symbols":0,"lastUsed":1795730471809},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/video/video-audio.schema.spec.ts":{"doclets":[],"fp":"c93e7dc0d81a16f627698109ec74589ce715dc84680332a58f9bdc8722652364","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730469250,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/resources/video/video-audio.schema.spec.ts":{"fp":"f20bfd99e317cd1c25b05f5dfbd2839c1002ac6a643fa9213e50465fcb2c3790","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","skipped":"no-jsdoc","symbols":0,"lastUsed":1795730469250},"tdata:packages/backend/src/utils/http.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"headerValue","longname":"headerValue","name":"headerValue","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Reads a named header without indexing the headers object with a variable key.","params":[{"description":"The request headers.","name":"headers","type":{"names":["Record<string, string | string[]>"]}},{"description":"The header name to look up.","name":"name","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The header value, or undefined when absent.","type":{"names":["string | string[]"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":7},"order":0,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/utils/http.js:1","src":"packages/backend/src/utils/http.ts:9"},"level":0},{"id":"requestMime","longname":"requestMime","name":"requestMime","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Reads the current request's media type without parameters.\n\nReturns `''` when the request or the header is absent. The header is split\nbefore `;` and trimmed, matching the expression each document service used\nbefore this helper existed. It stays a pure function over the normalized CLS\ncontext so specs that stub only `request()` keep working.","params":[{"description":"Normalized request context carrying the current request.","name":"cls","type":{"names":["NormalizedClsService"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The media type without parameters, or `''` when missing.","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":20},"order":1,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/utils/http.js:4","src":"packages/backend/src/utils/http.ts:26"},"level":0}],"fp":"2c04edbae0f0a686d80ecd2cc8459d1544ede47b6f137bfde0520bafbe5a3160","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","symbols":0,"lastUsed":1795730471152},"md:packages/backend/src/utils/http.ts":{"fp":"53909b5c8b9e3a2bd2a26481302458005948bc863652f6aa6a92f17c38abf1eb","issues":[],"kind":"md","markdown":"## Functions\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#headerValue\">headerValue(headers, name)</a> ⇒ <code>string | string[]</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Reads a named header without indexing the headers object with a variable key.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#requestMime\">requestMime(cls)</a> ⇒ <code>string</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Reads the current request&#39;s media type without parameters.</p>\n<p>Returns <code>&#39;&#39;</code> when the request or the header is absent. The header is split\nbefore <code>;</code> and trimmed, matching the expression each document service used\nbefore this helper existed. It stays a pure function over the normalized CLS\ncontext so specs that stub only <code>request()</code> keep working.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"headerValue\"></a>\n\n## headerValue(headers, name) ⇒ <code>string \\| string[]</code>\nReads a named header without indexing the headers object with a variable key.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>string \\| string[]</code> - The header value, or undefined when absent.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| headers | <code>Record&lt;string, string \\| string[]&gt;</code> | The request headers. |\n| name | <code>string</code> | The header name to look up. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/utils/http.ts:9  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/utils/http.js:1\n<a name=\"requestMime\"></a>\n\n## requestMime(cls) ⇒ <code>string</code>\nReads the current request's media type without parameters.\n\nReturns `''` when the request or the header is absent. The header is split\nbefore `;` and trimmed, matching the expression each document service used\nbefore this helper existed. It stays a pure function over the normalized CLS\ncontext so specs that stub only `request()` keep working.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>string</code> - The media type without parameters, or `''` when missing.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| cls | <code>NormalizedClsService</code> | Normalized request context carrying the current request. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/utils/http.ts:26  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/utils/http.js:4\n","symbols":2,"lastUsed":1795730471242},"tdata:packages/backend/src/utils/http.spec.ts":{"doclets":[],"fp":"fdef70ecfa61e5a280933c5ae6b3fa97ca34be2407187361503d2ad91c81ad74","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730470884,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/utils/http.spec.ts":{"fp":"3be3e166cc0fe958615a15a5b94e64181ecb01f4c13c61fb5893f78dd2d3c761","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","skipped":"no-jsdoc","symbols":0,"lastUsed":1795730470885},"tdata:packages/backend/src/utils/signature-guard.spec.ts":{"doclets":[],"fp":"9df8a82e9505f6bd6d669bcdf0a46e32771327444082b36672481301ed3be936","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730471187,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/utils/signature-guard.spec.ts":{"fp":"3e14178b54f741696619aa65a90e1ef07f150f5faeb29aef1f5bb311a390c4c9","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","skipped":"no-jsdoc","symbols":0,"lastUsed":1795730471188},"tdata:packages/backend/src/utils/signature-guard.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"guardSignature","longname":"guardSignature","name":"guardSignature","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Shared guard used by the media signature interceptors: rejects a request whose\nprobed signature is not a member of the expected media family.\n\nThe check is a no-op for routes whose URL does not start with `prefix`; for\nmatching routes with a probed signature that fails `isAllowed`, an\n{@link UnsupportedMediaTypeException} carrying `message` is thrown. Routes\nwithout a probed signature pass through untouched (the probe happens earlier).","params":[{"description":"Route prefix to gate (e.g. `'/audio'`).","name":"prefix","type":{"names":["string"]}},{"description":"{@link FileTypeService} predicate for the media family.","name":"isAllowed","type":{"names":["SignaturePredicate"]}},{"description":"Exact error message thrown on rejection.","name":"message","type":{"names":["string"]}},{"description":"Normalized CLS service carrying the current request context.","name":"cls","type":{"names":["NormalizedClsService"]}},{"description":"Call handler used to continue the pipeline.","name":"next","type":{"names":["CallHandler<any>"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The observable produced by continuing the pipeline.","type":{"names":["import(\"rxjs\").Observable<any>"]}}],"exceptions":[{"type":{"names":["UnsupportedMediaTypeException"]},"description":"When the probed signature is not allowed."}],"meta":{"lineno":18},"order":0,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/utils/signature-guard.js:2","src":"packages/backend/src/utils/signature-guard.ts:31"},"level":0}],"fp":"67c28b8fe8ef78382b94145b5f80c1349d2741ef13acf3b06a81cd13615b997e","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730471215,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/utils/signature-guard.ts":{"fp":"736c9f06bced473540e0a88909a31b3879650f14d06590387f968d293fd894c4","issues":[],"kind":"md","markdown":"<a name=\"guardSignature\"></a>\n\n## guardSignature(prefix, isAllowed, message, cls, next) ⇒ <code>import(&quot;rxjs&quot;).Observable&lt;any&gt;</code>\nShared guard used by the media signature interceptors: rejects a request whose\nprobed signature is not a member of the expected media family.\n\nThe check is a no-op for routes whose URL does not start with `prefix`; for\nmatching routes with a probed signature that fails `isAllowed`, an\n[UnsupportedMediaTypeException](UnsupportedMediaTypeException) carrying `message` is thrown. Routes\nwithout a probed signature pass through untouched (the probe happens earlier).\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>import(&quot;rxjs&quot;).Observable&lt;any&gt;</code> - The observable produced by continuing the pipeline.  \n**Throws**:\n\n- <code>UnsupportedMediaTypeException</code> When the probed signature is not allowed.\n\n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| prefix | <code>string</code> | Route prefix to gate (e.g. `'/audio'`). |\n| isAllowed | <code>SignaturePredicate</code> | [FileTypeService](FileTypeService) predicate for the media family. |\n| message | <code>string</code> | Exact error message thrown on rejection. |\n| cls | <code>NormalizedClsService</code> | Normalized CLS service carrying the current request context. |\n| next | <code>CallHandler&lt;any&gt;</code> | Call handler used to continue the pipeline. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/utils/signature-guard.ts:31  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/utils/signature-guard.js:2\n","symbols":1,"lastUsed":1795730471278},"tdata:packages/dashboard/src/components/ip-detail-page.spec.tsx":{"doclets":[],"fp":"47f87446483894563be4bdeb4d2e6820d9999157e18d675eac2edde340b3e5c9","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730471408,"symbols":0},"md:packages/dashboard/src/components/ip-detail-page.spec.tsx":{"fp":"a022ffc2815178b6e4ecc9a966086920b05f7437ed0d71b8044716c073881350","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","skipped":"no-jsdoc","symbols":0,"lastUsed":1795730471416},"tdata:packages/dashboard/src/components/kpi-card.tsx":{"doclets":[{"id":"KpiCard","longname":"KpiCard","name":"KpiCard","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Single headline KPI tile.","params":[{"description":"Tile props.","name":"properties","type":{"names":["KpiCardProperties"]}},{"description":"Metric name shown above the value.","name":"properties.label"},{"description":"Pre-formatted value string.","name":"properties.value"},{"description":"Optional detail line below the value.","name":"properties.supporting"}],"returns":[{"description":"The KPI card element.","type":{"names":["import(\"react\").JSX.Element"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":12},"order":0,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/dashboard/src/components/kpi-card.tsx:31"},"level":0}],"fp":"b03fc475bca44bbc052420476f78f654d5838e3eb14d38d3d23cee071ea015e7","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795730471499,"symbols":0},"md:packages/dashboard/src/components/kpi-card.tsx":{"fp":"a308bc9805c5042726881650038464a46ffed59b30019489b9792bb63b5681c8","issues":["dist